  A mechanism to restrict the quantity of items that may be purchased by one buyer during the duration of a fixed-price listing (single or multi-variation). This is optional and can be used with an Add, Revise, or Relist call.
  """
  quantityLimitPerBuyer: Int
}

"""
Cancellation Adjustment type
A cancellation adjustment refers to the process of modifying or updating a transaction when an order
is canceled after the purchase has been made. This typically involves adjustments to the payment,
inventory, and order state, reflecting that the transaction will no longer proceed as originally planned.
"""
type CancellationAdjustment implements OrderAdjustment {
  """User-friendly ID of the adjustment."""
  adjustmentId: ID!
  """Cancellation event associated to this adjustment."""
  cancellation: OrderCancellation!
  """Creation date of the adjustment."""
  createdAt: DateTime!
  """State of the adjustment."""
  state: OrderAdjustmentState!
  """Last updated date-time of the adjustment."""
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

