"""
This type defines information about a specific category within the marketplace, including identifiers and hierarchical structure.
"""
type Category {
  """
  This array returns a list of one or more categories that are the ancestors of the current category. The list identifies the category's ancestry as a sequence of parent nodes, from the current node's immediate parent to the root node of the category tree. The first item in the array is the immediate ancestor, while the last element in list is the root category. 
  **Note:** If this category is the root, the list will be empty.
  """
  ancestors: [Category!]!
  """The unique identifier of the eBay category."""
  categoryId: ID!
  """
  The level of the category in the hierarchy of the category.
  **Note**: Root categories are always at level '0'.
  """
  level: Int!
  """
  The display name of the category. 
  **Note:** This name is not localized.
  """
  name: String!
  """Category Id (replaced by categoryId)"""
  id: ID! @deprecated(reason: "Use 'categoryId' field instead")
  """
  This array returns a list of one or more categories that are the immediate children of the current category, as well as their children, recursively down the tree node. This array is returned in no guaranteed order.
  **Note:** If this category has no children, this list will be empty.
  """
  children: [Category!]!
  """
  This boolean indicates whether or not the category is a leaf category. If 'true', this category is a leaf category in which items may be listed. If 'false', this category is not a leaf category.
  """
  leafCategory: Boolean!
  """
  This container returns information about this category's parent category, if applicable. If the category has no parent, this container will be returned null.
  """
  parent: Category
}

"""
This type is used for charitable listings to show the non-profit organization that will benefit from the sale of the item, and the percentage of each sale that the organization will receive through a charitable donation.  if the seller wishes to donate a set percentage of each sale on the listing to a non-profit organization

**Note**: **eBay for Charity** is only supported on the US, UK, Germany, and Canada marketplaces.
"""
type Charity {
  """
  The unique identifier of the non-profit organization that will benefit from each sale of the item. The ID returned here can be used in the
  [getCharityOrg](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/charity/resources/charity_org/methods/getCharityOrg) method to retrieve the name and more about the organization.
  """
  charityOrganization: CharityOrganization
  """
  The integer value returned in this field indicates the percentage of the purchase price that the seller will donate to the selected non-profit organization for each sale.
    
  The integer value returned here ranges from 10 to 100 (percent) and will be in 5 percent increments, such as 10, 15, 20, 25, and all the way up to 100 (percent).
  """
  donationPercentage: Int
}

