"""
The base request type for the **commitToPurchase** mutation. This type is used to define the information needed for creating a commitment for a listing. This includes the item ID of the item the buyer wishes to purchase, as well as the price and quantity of the item. Additional information, such as user consent and adult verification, may also be required as applicable.
"""
input CommitToPurchaseInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the item the buyer wishes to purchase. If the item is part of a multi-SKU listing, the identifier of the variation is required.
  """
  itemId: ID!
  """
  The Buy It Now price of the item the buyer wishes to purchase. The item commitment will only be created if the item's price matches this value at the time of processing. If the item's price has changed, or this value does not match the Buy It Now price of the item, an error will be returned and the item commitment will not be created.
  """
  price: AmountInput!
  """
  The number of units requested by the buyer. This value can not exceed the available quantity of the listing.
  **Default**: 1
  """
  quantity: Int = 1
  """
  This boolean specifies if the buyer gives their consent to buy an item. This field is required if the item is in a category that requires user consent. If 'true', this boolean confirms that the buyer has read and agrees to eBay's privacy policy. If this field is 'false' and the item category requires user consent, an error will occur.
  **Default**: false
  """
  userConsentReceived: Boolean = false
  """
  This boolean specifies if the buyer can bid on adult-only items. This field is required if the item is in a category that requires adult verification. If 'true', this field confirms that the buyer has been verified as an adult. If this field is 'false' and the item category requires adult verification, an error will occur.
  **Default**: false
  """
  userVerifiedAsAdult: Boolean = false
}

"""
The union type for the **commitToPurchase** mutation. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **commitToPurchase** mutation succeeds, an **itemCommitment** container that returns the unique identifier of a successfully created item commitment will be returned. If the **commitToPurchase** mutation fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the item commitment will not be created. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error.
"""
union CommitToPurchaseOutput = CommitToPurchaseBusinessRulesViolated | CommitToPurchaseSuccess | ReferenceArgumentsNotFound

"""
This type is used for a successful **commitToPurchase** mutation. On success, the unique identifier of the newly created item commitment entity is returned.
"""
type CommitToPurchaseSuccess {
  """
  The unique identifier of the item commitment entity that was successfully created using the **commitToPurchase** mutation.
  """
  commitment: ItemCommitment!
}

"""
This type is used to provide additional information, such as characteristics or attributes, about the condition of an item in a structured format.
"""
type ConditionDescriptor {
  """
  This boolean indicates whether the condition descriptor supports free text or predefined values only. If 'true', the descriptor allows user-entered text as values. If 'false', the value must be selected from the predefined list of values specified in the **conditionDescriptorValues** field.
  """
  acceptsFreeText: Boolean!
  """
  This field returns information about the category associated with the item condition.
  """
  category: Category!
  """The unique identifier of the condition descriptor."""
  conditionDescriptorId: ID!
  """
  This array returns a list of possible condition descriptor values for given condition descriptor name, applicable for the specified item condition. This field maps to the corresponding **displayName** field, and acts as the value for the associated condition descriptor name.
  """
  conditionDescriptorValues: [ConditionDescriptorValue!]!
  """
  The display name of the condition descriptor.
  **Note:** This text is localized for the specified marketplace by default. The **Accept-Language** header can be used to provide a translation to a different language from the marketplace default language.
  """
  displayName: String!
  """
  The maximum allowed length for user-entered text. This field is only applicable if the **acceptsFreeText** boolean is 'true'. If the **acceptsFreeText** boolean is 'false', this field returns null as only predefined values are supported.
  """
  maximumLength: Int
  """
  This boolean indicates if multiple values can be selected for this descriptor. If 'true', multiple values are supported for this descriptor. If 'false', only one value can be selected for this descriptor.
  """
  multipleValuesSupported: Boolean!
  """
  If applicable, this object returns information about the parent descriptor that can filter values based on its selected value. This object will be returned null if no parent descriptor exists.
  """
  parentDescriptor: ConditionDescriptor
  """
  This boolean indicates if the condition descriptor is required for listing submissions. If 'true', the condition descriptor is required for listing submission.
  """
  required: Boolean!
}

"""
This type represents a specific value associated with a condition descriptor.
"""
type ConditionDescriptorValue {
  """
  This field returns information about the category associated with the item condition.
  """
  category: Category!
  """The unique identifier for the condition descriptor value."""
  conditionDescriptorValueId: ID!
  """
  The display name for the condition descriptor value. 
  **Note**: This text is localized for the specified marketplace by default. The **Accept-Language** header can be used to provide a translation to a different language from the marketplace default language.
  """
  displayName: String!
}

