"""
This interface represents a contract cancellation that can apply to supported contracts types (for example, on orders, commitments, and similar). Different contracts types may have different cancellations.

**Note:** Additional interface types may be added in the future; clients should handle unrecognized types gracefully.
"""
interface ContractCancellation {
  """ The buyer involved in this contract cancellation """
  buyer: User!
  """
  This field provides available actions for the buyer, including a primary action and deadline. If no action is available based on current cancellation status, this field will not be set.
  """
  buyerAvailableActions: ContractCancellationActions
  """ The unique ID of the contract cancellation """
  cancellationId: ID!
  """
  The timestamp when the cancellation was closed. This field will not be set if the cancellation is not closed.
  """
  closedAt: DateTime
  """ Line-level entries included in the contract cancellation. """
  lineItems: [ContractCancellationLineItem!]!
  """
  The reason provided for the cancellation. If the buyer does not select a cancellation reason when requesting the cancellation, the value is `UNDISCLOSED`.
  """
  reason: ContractCancellationReason!
  """
  A list of one or more refunds resulting from this cancellation. Present only if refund processing was initiated during cancellation; otherwise, null.
  """
  refunds: [Refund!]
  """ The timestamp when the cancellation was requested. """
  requestedAt: DateTime!
  """ The entity that requested the cancellation (for example, `BUYER`). """
  requester: PostPurchaseActorRole!
  """
  An optional note provided when requesting the cancellation. Null if no note was provided.
  """
  requesterNote: String
  """ The seller involved in this contract cancellation """
  seller: User!
  """
  This field provides available actions for the seller, including a primary action and deadline. If no action is available based on current cancellation status, this field will not be set.
  """
  sellerAvailableActions: ContractCancellationActions
  """ The current status of this cancellation. """
  status: ContractCancellationStatus!
}

"""
This interface provides available contract cancellation actions applicable for the user.

**Note:** Additional interface types may be added in the future; clients should handle unrecognized types gracefully.
"""
interface ContractCancellationAction {
  """The unique cancellation action code for the business use case."""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the error message. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This error type provides details when a contract cancellation action is not permitted. It describes the business constraints on the contract cancellation prohibiting current user from taking the action. If an alternative action is available, it is returned in `availableActions`.
"""
type ContractCancellationActionNotPermittedError implements BusinessError {
  """
  Permitted actions that user could take based on the current cancellation status.
  """
  availableActions: [ContractCancellationAction!]
  """
  The globally unique error code for this business error. For this type, the value is `CNCL_ACTION_NOT_PERMITTED_ERROR`.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the error message. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
}

"""
This type provides available actions for a user to respond to a cancellation, plus the deadline for making one of the primary decisions.
"""
type ContractCancellationActions {
  """
  The set of primary/recommended actions that the actor must choose from before `responseDueAt`. At least one will be present.
  """
  primaryActions: [ContractCancellationAction!]!
  """
  Deadline by which one of the `primaryActions` must be taken. After this time the system may auto-process or escalate.
  """
  responseDueAt: DateTime!
}

"""
This type indicates the contract is open and pending on action from the involved party. For the seller, this can happen when the buyer submits a cancel request and seller has an action to take (for example, approve or decline). This can also occur for a post seller-initiated refund that failed.
"""
type ContractCancellationAwaitingActionFromSeller implements ContractCancellationStatus {
  """
  The machine-readable contract cancellation status code. For this type, the value is `AWAITING_ACTION_FROM_SELLER`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the contract cancellation status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates that the cancellation was completed and the workflow is in an end state.
"""
type ContractCancellationCompleted implements ContractCancellationStatus {
  """
  The machine-readable contract cancellation status code. For this type, the value is `COMPLETED`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message of the contract cancellation status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates that the cancellation was declined and the workflow is in an end state. The cancellation did not complete successfully. Typical causes include:
- Seller explicitly rejected the cancellation
- System auto-declined (for example, if the item already shipped)
- Refund attempts failed or were exhausted within cancellation life cycle

**Note:** The cancellation did not complete successfully and the cancellation is at end state; no further cancellation actions can successfully complete from this state.
"""
type ContractCancellationDeclined implements ContractCancellationStatus {
  """
  The machine-readable contract cancellation status code. For this type, the value is `DECLINED`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message of the contract cancellation status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This input type represents filters to narrow the set of contract cancellations returned.

**Note:** All filters are combined with logical AND.
"""
input ContractCancellationFilterInput {
  """
  Filter by creation date range.
    
  **Default:** last 30 days
