"""
This type is used to indicate one or more marketplace-specific product compliance or takeback policies attached to the listing. Up to 6 product compliance policies may be set per marketplace, but only 1 takeback policy may be set per marketplace.
"""
type CountryPolicy {
  """The country for this policy"""
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The policy Ids specifying product compliance or take-back policy information.
  """
  policyIds: [ID!]
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **createInStoreReturn** mutation which is used to provide specifics about the return.
"""
input CreateInStoreReturnInput {
  """This array contains the line item to be refunded in this return."""
  returnLineItemInput: [CreateReturnLineItemInput!]!
}

"""
This error type indicates that one or more validation errors occurred while creating the in-store return request.
"""
type CreateInStoreReturnInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  A machine-readable error code: `RTRN_CREATE_IN_STORE_VALIDATION_ERROR.`
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable error message describing the issue. 
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains details about one or more specific request violations.
  """
  violations: [CreateInStoreReturnInputViolation!]!
}

"""
This interface describes validation errors detected during create in-store return request evaluation. Each violation indicates that the provided input value did not comply with the business rules or constraints defined for creating in-store return (for example, exceeding the maximum allowed characters for a return note). Constraints are defined by eBay return policies and may vary by context, marketplace, or configuration.
"""
interface CreateInStoreReturnInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific approve return input violation.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the approve return input violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **createInStoreReturn** mutation includes the result of the mutation and any errors encountered.
"""
union CreateInStoreReturnOutput = CreateInStoreReturnInputValidationError | MultipleLineItemReturnNotSupportedError | OrderLineItemNotFoundError | OrderReturn | ReturnCreationNotAllowedError | ReturnRequestLineItemRequiredError

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **createItemCommitmentCancellation** mutation, identifying the item commitment to cancel, providing a reason, and whether to relist.
"""
input CreateItemCommitmentCancellationInput {
  """ An enumerated value that indicates the reason for canceling the commitment (for example, `OUT_OF_STOCK` or `BUYER_REQUESTED`).
  """
  contractCancellationReason: ContractCancellationSellerReasonInput!
  """ The ID of the item commitment to be cancelled."""
  itemCommitmentId: ID!
  """
   Whether to relist all items from the canceled item commitment.
    
  **Note:** Must be `false` if the **contractCancellationReason** is set to `OUT_OF_STOCK`.
    
  **Default:** `false`
  """
  relistItem: Boolean! = false
}

"""
This union type defines the response payload for the **createItemCommitmentCancellation** mutation. On success, the response includes a **CreateItemCommitmentCancellationSuccess** type object and any warnings; on failure it returns an error indicating the reason that the create order cancellation failed.

**Note:** Additional types may be added to this union in the future; clients should handle unrecognized types gracefully.
"""
union CreateItemCommitmentCancellationOutput = CreateItemCommitmentCancellationSuccess | ItemCommitmentCancellationEligibilityError | ItemCommitmentNotFoundError

"""
This type is returned when an item commitment cancellation is created successfully.
"""
type CreateItemCommitmentCancellationSuccess {
  """The successfully created item commitment cancellation and its details."""
  itemCommitmentCancellation: ItemCommitmentCancellation!
}

"""
This type is used to provide auction-specific price settings for auction listings. Not applicable for multiple-SKU listings.
"""
input CreateListingAuctionPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to set the lowest price at which the seller is willing to sell an auction listing. A small fee is charged to use this feature. If the **reservePrice** field value is not met or surpassed during bidding, the auction will end without a winning bidder. This price must be higher than the **startingBidPrice**. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  reservePrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is required for auction listings and sets the starting bid amount. The first bid must meet or exceed this value or it will be rejected. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  startingBidPrice: Decimal!
}

"""
This type is used if the seller wishes to make the Best Offer feature available for a fixed price or auction listing. Optionally, 'auto accept' and/or 'auto decline' price thresholds can be set up so a Best Offer can be automatically accepted or declined based on the value of the Best Offer.
"""
input CreateListingBestOfferTermsInput {
  """
  Include this field and set its value to a price at which Best Offers will be automatically accepted by the seller if they meet or exceed the price. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-accept feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to 'true'.
  """
  autoAcceptThreshold: Decimal
  """
  Include this field and set its value to a price at which Best Offers will be automatically declined by the seller if the price is at or below this value. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-decline feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to true.
  """
  autoDeclineThreshold: Decimal
  """
  This field enables or disables the Best Offer feature for a fixed-price or auction listing. If set to 'true', the Best Offer feature is enabled, allowing potential buyers to make offers on the item. If set to 'false', or omitted, the Best Offer feature is disabled.
  **Note** For auction listings, the Buy It Now and Best Offer features cannot be used simultaneously.
  **Note** If Best Offer is enabled for an auction listing, it is automatically disabled as soon as the listing receives a qualifying bid, and any pending offers or counteroffers are invalidated.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  bestOfferEnabled: Boolean = false
}

"""
This type is used to define the street address for a business entity such as the product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input CreateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput {
  """
  This field sets the first line of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine1: String!
  """
  This field sets the second line of the entity's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  This field sets the city of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  city: String!
  """
  This field sets the two-letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation of the country of the entity's address.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code!
  """
  This field sets the postal code of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 9 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String!
  """
  This field sets the state or province of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  stateOrProvince: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide contact information for a product manufacturer or responsible person. At least one of the three fields in this type must be specified for a product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input CreateListingBusinessEntityContactInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify the entity's URL for their online Contact Us/Support page.
  **Max length**: 250 characters.
  """
  contactUrl: HttpOrHttpsUrl
  """
  This field is used to specify the entity's email address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  email: String
  """
  This field is used to specify the entity's phone number.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  phone: String
}

"""
This type is used to block/disable a seller's account-level buyer restrictions and/or set a quantity limit per buyer threshold for a multiple-quantity, fixed price listing.
"""
input CreateListingBuyerRestrictionsInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to disable all buyer restrictions (that are set in the seller's account) for the listing.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  disableBuyerRestrictions: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is used to set the maximum quantity of items that a single buyer may purchase during the duration of a fixed price listing (single or multiple-SKU). The buyer is blocked from the purchase if that buyer is attempting to purchase a quantity of items that will exceed this value. Previous purchases made by the buyer are taken into account. For example, if **quantityLimitPerBuyer** is set to '5' for a listing, and *Buyer1* purchases a quantity of three in a previous sale, *Buyer1* is only allowed to purchase an additional quantity of two in subsequent orders on the same listing.
  """
  quantityLimitPerBuyer: Int
}

"""
This type is used if the seller wishes to donate a set percentage of each sale on the listing to a non-profit organization that is registered to receive donations on eBay's platform.
**Note**: **eBay for Charity** is only supported on the eBay US, eBay UK, eBay Germany, and eBay Canada marketplaces.
"""
input CreateListingCharityInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the non-profit organization that will benefit from the sale of the item. The [Charity API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/charity/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve the numeric identifiers for the charities and to find out more about the organization.
  """
  charityOrganizationId: ID!
  """
  This field sets the percentage of the purchase price that the seller chooses to donate to the selected non-profit organization for each sale generated by the listing. An integer value is used here with supported values ranging from 10 to 100. Within this range, only increments of 5 can be used, so 15, 20, 25, etc.
  **Min value**: 10
  **Max value**: 100
  """
  donationPercentage: Int!
}

"""
This type is used to specify one or more country-specific product compliance or takeback policies. Up to 6 product compliance policies may be set per country, but only 1 takeback policy may be set per country.
"""
input CreateListingCountryPolicyInput {
  """
  The two-letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation for a country that hosts an eBay marketplace, a marketplace to which the corresponding policy or policies apply. The supported values are `GB`, `DE`, `FR`, `IT`, and `ES`.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code!
  """
  This array is used to set one or more country-specific product compliance policy ID values or one takeback policy ID value that will apply to the corresponding country. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all policies defined for a seller's account.
  """
  policyIds: [ID!]!
}

"""
This type is used to specify global or country-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies for a listing.
"""
input CreateListingCustomPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to specify one or more global product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. The product compliance policies set with this array will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies should be set with the **regionalProductCompliancePolicies** container instead.
  **Note**: The maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per listing is 6.
  """
  productCompliancePolicyIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used specify one or more country-specific product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies may be needed where countries might have special legal/regulatory requirements. For example, if you sell batteries in a country requiring disclosures that apply only to that country, a country-specific product compliance policy could contain this information. If country-specific policies are not needed, use the **productCompliancePolicyIds** array instead.
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per marketplace**: 6 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per listing**: 30 (6 per country).
  """
  regionalProductCompliancePolicies: CreateListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput
  """
  This container is used to specify one or more country-specific takeback policies that will be used for a listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The law in some countries may require sellers to take back a used product when the buyer buys a new product but wishes to dispose of it. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy. If a country-specific takeback policy is not needed, one global takeback policy is set with the **takebackPolicyId** field.
  **Maximum number of takeback policies allowed per marketplace**: 1 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of takeback policies allowed per listing**: 5 (1 per country).
  """
  regionalTakebackPolicies: CreateListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput
  """
  This field is used to set the global takeback policy to use for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The takeback policy set with this field will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Country-specific policies should be set with **regionalTakebackPolicies** container instead.
  **Max length of takeback policy ID**: 15 characters.
  """
  takebackPolicyId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to provide Energy Efficiency Label related information for such categories as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Note that these three category types will also need Rating and Range product aspects. See the [Energy efficiency information](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/static/inventory/energy-efficiency.html) topic for more information.
"""
input CreateListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput {
  """
  This field is used to provide a brief text-based summary of the information included on the Energy Efficiency Label for a product. The description should be concise and informative, providing key details about the energy efficiency of the product. If you provide `imageDescription`, then you need to provide `imageUrl`.
  **Max length**: 280
  """
  imageDescription: String
  """
  This field is used to specify the URL to the Energy Efficiency Label image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  imageUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including energy efficiency labels.")
  """
  The URL to the Product Information Sheet image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  productInformationSheetUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including product information sheets.")
}

"""
This type is used to specify an eco-participation fee for item(s) in a listing. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
"""
input CreateListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput {
  """
  This is the fee paid for new items to the eco-organization (for example, *eco-organisme* in France). It is a contribution to the financing of the disposal of the item responsibly. In a multiple-SKU listing, this fee should be specified at the variation level and not in this field. The [getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports, requires, or recommends eco-participation fees at the listing or variation level.
  """
  ecoParticipationFee: Decimal!
}

"""
This type is used to provide details on how the item will be delivered to the buyer. The data in this container includes available shipping services, ship-to and excluded shipping locations, shipping costs, package details, and more.
"""
input CreateListingFulfillmentTermsInput {
  """
  This field should be included and set to 'true' if the item is a digital item that can be downloaded via a link or delivered to the buyer via email. The  [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports digital delivery.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  digitalDeliverySupported: Boolean = false
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to use eBay's Global Shipping Program (GSP) to ship items internationally. With GSP, the seller ships the item to eBay's shipping partner, and that shipping partner handles all logistics of the international shipping leg. GSP is only available for listings on the eBay GB (EBAY_GB) marketplace. eBay US (EBAY_US) has a similar program called eBay International Shipping, but there is currently no boolean field associated with this feature.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  globalShippingSupported: Boolean = false
  """
  This container is used to provide information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions. Package weight is required when calculated shipping is used, and shipping services generally have dimension and weight restrictions.
  """
  packageSpecifications: CreateListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput
  """
  This container is used to provide information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
  """
  shippingTerms: CreateListingShippingTermsInput
}

"""
This type is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for the item. GTIN is a globally unique identifier for trade items used by companies to identify products. GTINs include UPCs, EANs, and ISBNs. Optionally, eBay will search for a catalog product against a provided GTIN if the **includeEbayProductDetails** field is included and set to 'true'. If a matching eBay catalog product is found, the listing will automatically pick up product details of that catalog product,including product title, product description, product aspects, and stock photo(s).
"""
input CreateListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  This field is used to supply a European Article Number (EAN) for a product. It is a 13-digit barcode standard used internationally for retail product identification. Also known as International Article Number. Some leaf categories may require an EAN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this EAN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  """
  ean: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply an International Standard Book Number (ISBN) for a product. It is a unique identifier for books and book-like products. Can be 10 digits (older format) or 13 digits (current format). Some leaf categories may require an ISBN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this ISBN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  **Max length**: 13 characters.
  """
  isbn: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply a Universal Product Code (UPC) for a product. It is a 12-digit barcode standard used primarily in North America for retail product identification. Some leaf categories may require a UPC, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this UPC, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to 'true'.
  **Max length**: 12 characters.
  """
  upc: ID
}

"""
This type is used to provide hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
"""
input CreateListingHazardousMaterialInput {
  """
  This field is used by the seller to provide component information for the listing. For example, component information can provide the specific material of Hazmat concern.
  **Max length**: 120 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to specify one to four pictogram codes that represent the possible hazard(s) that a product poses. The pictograms that are stated on the product's Safety Data Sheet should be used. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the codes that can be passed into this array. The pictogram(s) that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This field is used to set the hazardous material signal word for the product. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the strings that can be passed into this array.
  **Max length**: 15 characters.
  """
  signalWordCode: ID
  """
  This array is used to specify one to eight hazardous statement codes that are applicable to the product. These codes map to actual hazardous statement text. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the statement codes that can be passed into this array. The hazardous statements that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Max number of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]!
}

"""
The base request type for the **createListing** mutation. This container is used to provide product details, eBay marketplace, listing terms, and price and quantity information for each item available for sale in the listing. For multiple-SKU listings, the **listingVariations** container must also be included to define the common aspects of the multiple-SKU listing and unique variations that are available through that multiple-variation listing.
"""
input CreateListingInput {
  """
  This field allows the user to set up a client-side idempotency key, and having this key defined will help in avoiding duplicate listings due to a retry if a mutation fails due to a system problem.
  **Max length**: 32 characters.
  """
  idempotencyKey: IdempotencyKey!
  """
  An array of one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing.
  **Note**: A SKU value is optional for a single-variation listing, but mandatory for a multiple-SKU listing.
  **Max number of items for a multi-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  listingItems: CreateListingItemsInput!
  """
  This container is used to provide listing terms details for the listing, including listing format, listing duration, payment terms, return policy, fulfillment terms, and more.
  """
  listingTerms: CreateListingTermsInput!
  """
  This container is required for multiple-SKU listings and not applicable to single-SKU listings. This container provides details on the available product variations within the listing, and which traits are different for each of these variations. Products in a multiple-variation listing tend to vary by one or more traits such as color and size, and interested buyers need to select which variation they want to purchase. For example, the 'Blue, Large' t-shirt.
  **Max number of variations per multiple-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  listingVariations: CreateListingVariationsInput
  """
  This field is used to identify the eBay marketplace where the listing will be created. See [`ListingMarketplace`] for list of supported enumeration values. It determines the regional settings, currency, and other marketplace-specific configurations.
  """
  marketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
  This container allows a user to run a **createListing** mutation in validation mode, which means that the listing object will be validated, but a successful mutation will not create a listing. 
  """
  options: ListingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to provide product data for the listing. Product data under this container includes title, description, product aspects, item condition, images, and more.
  """
  product: CreateListingProductInput!
  """
     This field is for the seller-defined Stock Keeping Unit (SKU) that identifies the entire listing. Providing a SKU at any level (listing or item) enables the listing to be tracked and managed by SKU.
     
  For **single-SKU listings**, this field provides the definitive SKU for the listing. If this field is omitted, the SKU provided on the single item within the `items` list can be used instead to identify the listing.
     
  For **multiple-SKU listings**, this field acts as an optional, overall identifier for the group of variations. Each individual variation must still have its own unique SKU.
     **Max length**: 50 characters.
  """
  sku: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide the available quantity for a purchasable item.
"""
input CreateListingItemAvailabilityInput {
  """
  The quantity available for an item. For auction listings, this value must always be 1. For a multiple-SKU listing, each item variation can have its own quantity value, allowing sellers to manage inventory for each variation independently.
  **Note**: For a multiple-SKU listing, the quantity for an item variation can be be set to 0 if the SKU is temporarily out of stock, but a seller wishes to retain the variation and restock inventory at a later time.
  """
  quantityAvailable: Int!
}

"""
This type is used to define motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input CreateListingItemCompatibilitiesInput {
  """
  This array is used to define a set of compatible vehicles or assemblies through a set of name-value pairs such as *Year*, *Make*, and *Model*. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Max number of allowed compatibilities on the listing**: 3000
  """
  itemCompatibilities: [CreateListingItemCompatibilityInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to define motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input CreateListingItemCompatibilityInput {
  """
  This array is used to define a set of compatible vehicles or assemblies through a set of name-value pairs such as *Year*, *Make*, and *Model*. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Max number of allowed compatibilities on the listing**: 3000
  **Max compatibility name length**: 65
  **Max compatibility value length**: 65
  """
  compatibilities: [NameValuesPairInput!]!
  """
  The seller may optionally enter any notes pertaining to the parts compatibility being specified. For example, if this Compatibility information applies to a vehicle, a seller may use this field to specify the placement of the part on a vehicle or the type of vehicle a part fits.
  **Max length**: 500 characters.
  """
  compatibilityNotes: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide more item condition information through name-value pairs about single graded and ungraded trading cards in the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
"""
input CreateListingItemConditionDescriptorInput {
  """
  This field can be used to provide additional information about a condition descriptor. One example is using this field to specify the **Certification Number** for a graded card.
  **Max length**: 30 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This field is used to pass in the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor that maps to the condition descriptor name. The IDs for condition descriptor names can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Condition descriptor names for graded cards include **Grader** and **Grade** (both required) and **Certification Number** (optional), and condition descriptor names for ungraded cards include **Card Condition**.
  """
  name: ID
  """
  This array is used to pass in the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor value that maps to an actual value supported by the condition descriptor. For example, graded cards require **Grader** and **Grade** as condition descriptor names, so the value(s) in this array will show the organization that graded the card and the card's actual grade, which ranges from 1 to 10. The numeric IDs for condition descriptor values can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Locate the Condition descriptor name first in the response, and then look for the corresponding values in the **conditionDescriptorValues** array of that response.
  """
  values: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to express the condition of an item. A large majority of eBay categories require a condition, and this condition is specified through a numeric identifier in the **conditionId** field. For non-new items, it is highly recommended that the **conditionDescription** field be used to provide specific details about the item's condition or 'wear and tear'. The **conditionDescriptor** array is used to provide condition details of graded and ungraded trading cards in a structured manner.
"""
input CreateListingItemConditionInput {
  """
  This field is used to provide additional details about a non-new item's physical state, including any defects, wear, or other characteristics that affect its condition. This field can be used for all categories except those that require the **conditionDescriptors** array.
  **Max length**: 1000 characters.
  """
  conditionDescription: String
  """
  This array is used to provide more item condition information through name-value pairs about single graded and ungraded trading cards in the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
  """
  conditionDescriptors: [CreateListingItemConditionDescriptorInput!]
  """
  This field is used to set the item's condition using the numeric identifier for a condition. Some common condition IDs include *1000 New* and *3000 Used*. Supported conditions and the text used to describe the conditions vary by marketplace and leaf category. Use the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method to get the supported condition IDs and their descriptions for leaf categories.
  """
  conditionId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to create a specific purchasable item within a listing. It includes a unique combination of identifying characteristics such as global identifiers, listing terms, availability, price, and regulatory information requirements. Every listing contains at least one item, providing a unified approach that works transparently across simple single-SKU listings and complex multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input CreateListingItemInput {
  """
  This container is used to specify the pricing information, available quantity, and eco-participation fee (if applicable) for a purchasable item. Each item should have price and quantity.
  """
  itemTerms: CreateListingItemTermsInput!
  """
  For either a single-SKU or a multiple-SKU listing, this container can be used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will prefill the listing being created. For a multiple-SKU listing, the **traits** array is required and identifies the unique traits of the variation within that multiple-SKU listing. Common unique traits within a multiple-SKU listing are 'Color' and 'Size'. For example, a 'Blue, Large' shirt. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values.
  """
  product: CreateListingItemProductInput
  """
  The seller-defined Stock-Keeping Unit (SKU) value uniquely identifies a purchasable item in the listing. Providing a SKU for any item ensures the entire listing can be managed by SKU. For single-SKU listings, this field acts as a fallback and its value is used only if a SKU is not provided at the top level (**CreateListingInput**) Otherwise, this field is ignored if provided. For multiple-SKU listings, however, this field is required and its value must be unique for each variation in the listing.
  **Max length**: 50 characters.
  """
  sku: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide the item's physical location. Item location is required for every fixed price and auction listing. The **country** field is always required, and either the **postalCode** or **location** must also be provided, but not necessarily both.
"""
input CreateListingItemLocationInput {
  """
  The two-letter country code, as defined in the ISO-3166 standard, must be specified in this field to indicate the country where the item is located. Please keep in mind that the item is often located in the same country as the listing marketplace, but this is not a requirement.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code!
  """
  The field indicates the geographic location (city and state/province) where the listing is physically located. If you do not provide a value in this field, you must provide a value in the **postalCode** field and the field value will be derived from the postal code in the created listing.
  For the CLASSIFIED_AD format for Motor vehicles, the value provided in the field is used as item location only if the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2** fields of the **CreateListingSellerContactInput** are not provided. If the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2* fields of the **CreateListingSellerContactInput** are provided, the item location field value is ignored.
  **Max length**: 200 characters.
  """
  location: String
  """
  The postal code (zip code) where the listing is physically located. Either the **location** field or the **postalCode** field must be specified or an error will occur. Postal/zip code format varies by region. e.g. US: 5-digit numeric codes (e.g., 12345), Australia: 4-digit numeric codes (e.g., 2000), GB: Variable-length alphanumeric codes with letters and numbers (e.g., SW1A 1AA). Other regions follow local postal service standards.
  **Max length**: 32 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide price data for an item in a listing, including the price for a fixed price listing or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. Other price fields include auction starting bid price, auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
"""
input CreateListingItemPricingTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide auction-specific price settings including starting bid price and reserve price.
  """
  auctionPrice: CreateListingAuctionPriceInput
  """
  This field sets the price of a fixed price item or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. This field is required for fixed price listings. The 'Buy it Now' option is disabled for an auction listing as soon as that listing has a qualifying bid. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  fixedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This container is used to provide pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
  """
  marketingPrice: CreateListingMarketingPriceInput
}

"""
This type can be used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will prefill the listing being created. For a multiple-SKU listing, the **traits** array is required and identifies the unique traits of the variation within that multiple-SKU listing. Common unique traits within a multiple-SKU listing are 'Color' and 'Size'. For example, a 'Blue, Large' shirt. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values.
"""
input CreateListingItemProductInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or an eBay product ID (ePID) for a product. If an eBay catalog product is found that maps to a GTIN or an ePID, product details of that eBay catalog product will be used to populate the listing. The product details in a catalog product include product title, product description, aspects, eBay leaf category, and stock photo.
  **Note**: If an eBay catalog product is found and used to prefill a listing, any other product-related details provided by the seller may be dropped.
  """
  productIdentifiers: CreateListingProductIdentifiersInput
  """
  This array is required for multiple-SKU listings and is used to provide the traits that make each item unique in context of the multiple-SKU listing. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values, and the trait names and trait values specified here must be defined as available trait names and trait values in the **variationDetails** container. An error will be thrown if the specified traits do not match the variation traits defined in the **variationDetails** container.
  **Note**: The traits must match the marketplace's language and locale.
  **Max allowed traits**: 5.
  **Max length for trait names and values**: 65 characters.
  """
  traits: [NameValuePairInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide an array of one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing. Use the **items** field to provide the details for each product variation.
"""
input CreateListingItemsInput {
  """
  This array is used to define a list of purchasable items to be created for the listing. For a single-SKU listing, this array must contain exactly one item object. For a multiple-SKU listing, it must contain one item object for each product variation (e.g. one for "Red / Large", one for "Blue / Small").
  **Maximum number of items for a multiple-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  items: [CreateListingItemInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide quantity and pricing information for a purchasable item. All SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing must have their own quantity and price values. All SKUs may have the same price, but prices also may vary by SKU. This container is also used to provide an eco-participation fee if applicable for the item.
"""
input CreateListingItemTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide the available quantity for a purchasable item. This field is required for all purchasable items.
  """
  availability: CreateListingItemAvailabilityInput!
  """
  This container is used to specify an eco-participation fee for an item. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
  """
  extendedProducerResponsibility: CreateListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput
  """
  This container is used to provide price data for the item, including the price for a fixed price item or the *Buy it Now* price for an auction item. Other price fields include auction starting bid price, auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
  **Note**: Each item within a multiple-SKU listing can have its own price, allowing for different pricing based on traits (e.g., larger sizes might cost more than smaller ones).
  """
  pricingTerms: CreateListingItemPricingTermsInput!
}

"""
This type is used to set the duration of the listing, and can also be used to set a future date when the listing will become active.
"""
input CreateListingLifecycleTermsInput {
  """
  This field indicates the time duration of the listing. All fixed price listings must be set to `GTC`(Good 'til Cancelled), but the listing duration days of auction and ad listings may vary based on marketplace and category. The [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see supported durations for each leaf category.
  """
  listingDurationInDays: ListingDurationInDays!
  """
  This field is used if the user wishes to have the eBay listing go live at a later date/time and not immediately upon creating the listing. The timestamp specified in this field must be a future date. For more information on eBay scheduled listings, see the [Listing durations and timings](https://www.ebay.com/help/selling/listings/creating-managing-listings/selecting-listing-duration?id=4652) help topic.
  """
  scheduledToStartAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type is used to define the radius for a local listing, making it available to buyers within that specified area. The seller's supplied **postalCode** or **location** field value will be used as the center point for this radius.
"""
input CreateListingLocalDistanceInput {
  """
  The numeric value for the radius. The unit of measurement for this value is specified in the **distanceUnit** field. This value defines the radius of the area around the seller's location where the listing will be visible to local buyers. The user can call the [getMotorsListingPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** to get supported distances. Look for the [localListingDistances](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies#response.motorsListingPolicies.localListingDistances) array in the response.
  """
  distance: Int!
  """
  The unit of measurement used for the **distance**. Currently, the only supported value is `MILES`.
  """
  distanceUnit: DistanceUnit!
}

"""
This type is used to provide the name and contact information for the manufacturer of the item. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
"""
input CreateListingManufacturerInput {
  """
  The street address for the product manufacturer is provided in this container.
  """
  address: CreateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field specifies the name of the company that manufactured the product. This field is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String!
  """
  This container is used to provide the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the product manufacturer. At least one of the three is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  """
  contact: CreateListingBusinessEntityContactInput
}

"""
This type provides pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
"""
input CreateListingMarketingPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to set and display the **Made for Outlet** comparison price for a listing, and can only be used if the listing will be displayed on an eBay Outlet page. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  madeForOutletComparisonPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to set the Minimum Advertised Price (MAP) for a listing. MAP is an agreement between suppliers (or manufacturers (OEM)) and the retailers (sellers) stipulating the lowest price a listing is allowed to be advertised at. Sellers can offer prices below MAP by means of other discounts. This only applies to fixed price listings and auction listings with the 'Buy It Now' option. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Minimum Advertised Price feature, and controls whether the discounted price is shown to buyers prior to checkout by the buyer clicking on a link on the View Item page, or the discounted price is shown just prior to checkout when the buyer has clicked the Buy button. See the [ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure] enum type for the list of possible values.
  **Default**: PRE_CHECKOUT.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPriceExposure: ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure = PRE_CHECKOUT
  """
  This field must be provided if a qualified seller is using the Strikethrough Price feature. The 'originalRetailPrice' price is the actual retail price set by the manufacturer (OEM). The price specified in this field should always be more than the price specified in the **fixedPrice** field. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  originalRetailPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOnEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  soldOffEbay: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOffEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  soldOnEbay: Boolean = false
}

"""
This type is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
"""
input CreateListingMotorVehicleDepositInput {
  """
  This field is used to set the due date (in days) for the buyer to pay off the full balance of the motor vehicle. The clock starts on the full payment due date as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The supported values here are `DAYS_3` `DAYS_7`, `DAYS_10`, and `DAYS_14`.
  **Default value**: DAYS_7
  """
  daysToMakeFullPayment: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This field sets the required deposit amount to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. This field is required if the seller is requiring a deposit. This deposit must be made immediately by the buyer if **immediatePay** is set to 'true', or within 24, 48, or 72 hours (set with **hoursToDeposit** field) if **immediatePay** is set to 'false'.
  **Max value**: 2000 USD (non-immediate pay), 500 USD (immediate pay)
  """
  depositAmount: Decimal
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  depositRequired: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is used to set the deadline (in hours) for the motor vehicle deposit. The deposit amount is specified in the **depositAmount** field. The clock starts on the deposit deadline as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The three supported integer values here are 24, 48, and 72 (hours). If **immediatePay** is 'true', and the listing qualifies for immediate payment (e.g. the 'Buy It Now' button is used), this field will not be applicable, since the buyer will be required to pay any deposit amount immediately (and not within 24, 48, and 72 hours).
  **Default value**: 48
  """
  hoursToDeposit: Int
}

"""
This type is needed for motor vehicle listings to provide the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
"""
input CreateListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput {
  """
  The Vehicle Identifier Number (VIN) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  **Max length**: 17 characters.
  """
  vin: ID
  """
  The Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  """
  vrm: ID
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **createListing** mutation. Three possible results of a **createListing** mutation are: a listing container (and possibly one or more warnings); a listing container with validation success (listingId = 0) and possibly one or more warnings; or an array of blocking errors if the mutation fails and a new listing is not created. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error, and there may also be one or more warning messages that are triggered.
"""
union CreateListingOutput = CreateListingSuccess | CreateListingValidationError | CreateListingValidationSuccess

"""
This type is used to override the shipping costs for one or more domestic or international shipping service options defined in the fulfillment business policy being used for the listing. The shipping costs provided will only affect the listing and will not update the fulfillment business policy.
"""
input CreateListingOverrideShippingOptionInput {
  """
  This field is used to override the additional unit shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost when a buyer is purchasing multiple quantities of the same line item. Note that this value should never be higher than the base shipping cost.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to specify if the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field is a shipping service. The value of this field should be set to 'false' if the shipping service is a domestic shipping service, and 'true' if it is an international shipping service.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  internationalShippingOption: Boolean = false
  """
  The integer value specified here identifies the shipping service in the fulfillment business policy whose cost value(s) will be overridden. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 if overriding a domestic shipping service option or from 1 to 5 if overriding an international shipping service option. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page.
  """
  rank: Int!
  """
  This field is used to override the shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost for the line item.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
}

"""
This type is used to specify the dimensions of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. When specifying the dimensions of the shipping package, all three values (length, width, and height) are required. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
"""
input CreateListingPackageDimensionsInput {
  """
  The height (or depth) of the shipping package specified according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  height: Float!
  """
  The length of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  length: Float!
  """
  The width of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  width: Float!
}

"""
This type is used to specify the weight of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is pounds for **majorUnit** and ounces for **minorUnit**. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is kilograms for **majorUnit** and grams for **minorUnit**.
Note: When specifying the weight of the shipping package, at least one of the two values (major or minor) is required.
"""
input CreateListingPackageWeightInput {
  """
  The major weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The major weight value is the whole number part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is pounds. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is kilograms.
  **Note**: If the package weighs less than one pound or one kilogram, *0* can be used as the value for this field.
  **Minimum value**: 0
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  majorUnit: Int
  """
  The minor weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The minor weight value is the decimal part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is ounces. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is grams.
  **Minimum value**: 0
  **Maximum value**: 15 for English measurement system (ounces); 999 for Metric measurement system (grams).
  """
  minorUnit: Int
}

"""
This type is used to provide various payment terms and information for the listing, including immediate payment requirement, offline payment methods, and motor vehicle deposit information. This type also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a payment business policy with the listing.
"""
input CreateListingPaymentTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify a payment business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all payment settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getPaymentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/payment_policy/methods/getPaymentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all payment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
     This field should be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to require immediate payment for fixed price listings and auction listings where the 'Buy it Now' option is used.
     **Default value**: false
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  immediatePay: Boolean = false
  """
     This container is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  motorVehicleDeposit: CreateListingMotorVehicleDepositInput
  """
     This field is used if the seller has any instructions related to payment instructions.
     **Max length**: 500 characters.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  paymentInstructions: String
  """
     This array is used to specify one or more offline payment methods for listings that support offline transactions. Use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see the payment methods supported for a leaf category.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  paymentMethods: [ListingPaymentMethod!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide the eBay category for the seller product, and optionally, a secondary eBay category and eBay store categories. If a seller has an eBay store and does not specify a store category ID, eBay will automatically put that listing into the default *Other* category in the seller's eBay store.
"""
input CreateListingProductCategoriesInput {
  """
  The eBay category ID for the primary category of the listing. This field is required unless an eBay catalog product is used, and the eBay category is defined in that catalog product. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  """
  primaryCategoryId: ID!
  """
  The eBay category ID for the secondary category of the listing. This field is optional, but if specified, it must be a valid eBay leaf category. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  **Note**: The secondary category must be different from the primary category.
  """
  secondaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  The eBay store primary category ID of the listing. This field is optional, but if specified, it must be a valid eBay store category ID. If this field is not specified, the listing will be placed in the default *Other* category of the seller's eBay store. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storePrimaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  The eBay store secondary category ID of the listing. This field is optional, but if specified, it must be a valid eBay store category ID. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storeSecondaryCategoryId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to match to and leverage the product details of a product defined in eBay's product catalog. The user can directly provide the identifier of the eBay catalog product, or they can provide a GTIN value that can possibly be matched to an eBay catalog product. When an eBay catalog product is used, the product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that product will be used in the resultant listing.
"""
input CreateListingProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of an eBay catalog product. If this field is provided, the title, description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that eBay product will be used in the resultant listing, overriding the seller provided information. The [search](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/catalog/resources/product_summary/methods/search) method of the **Catalog API** can be used to search for eBay catalog products and get their IDs.
  """
  ebayProductId: ID
  """
  This container is used to specify a UPC, EAN, or ISBN value for a product, and optionally, try to match the value to an eBay catalog product so that the product details of that catalog product can be prefilled in the resultant listing. Some leaf categories require a GTIN, and the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category requires a UPC, EAN, or ISBN.
  """
  globalIdentifiers: CreateListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput
  """
  This field controls whether or not an eBay catalog product is leveraged to prefill a listing with that catalog product's details, including product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo. If you want to use an eBay catalog product to populate your listing, you can either set this field to true or omit it entirely, as true is the default value. If you provide a GTIN (Global Trade Item Number) or eBay Product ID but do not want to use the corresponding eBay catalog product to prefill your listing, you must set this field to false. If set to false, you will be required to provide your own listing title, description, category, and at least one image. This is only applicable to single-SKU listings.
  **Default value**: true
  """
  includeEbayProductDetails: Boolean = true
}

"""
This type is used to provide common product details for the listing, including title, description, listing category, condition, product aspects, images, and more.
"""
input CreateListingProductInput {
  """
  This array is used to set name-value pairs that define the product aspects. Most leaf categories require at least a few aspects, and the listing will fail if these are not provided. The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method can be used to see which aspects are required, recommended, or optional for a leaf category. This method also returns typical values for an aspect name and will indicate if an aspect name supports multiple values or just one value. For a multiple-SKU listing, only the common aspects will be specified in this array, and the pivoting aspects (aka traits) will be specified at the item level.
  **Max length**: 65 characters for each aspect name and value.
  """
  aspects: [NameValuesPairInput!]
  """
  This container is used to provide the primary eBay category for the listing, and optionally, a secondary eBay category and eBay store categories. This container is required unless an eBay catalog product is used, and the eBay category is defined in that catalog product.
  **Note**: If a seller has an eBay store and does not specify a store category ID, eBay will automatically put that listing into the default *Other* category in the seller's eBay store.
  """
  categories: CreateListingProductCategoriesInput
  """
  This field is used to set the full description of the product or group of products. This field is required unless an eBay catalog product is being used and the product description is picked up from the catalog product instead. HTML markup and inline CSS can be used. However, a seller can not use any active content in their listing description. Active content includes animation or video via JavaScript, Flash, plug-ins, or form actions. All active content will be blocked/removed from a listing. Sellers are only allowed to provide links to product videos, freight shipping services, or other legally required information, and when providing these links in the listing description, the secure 'https' protocol must be used instead of 'http'. In addition, any valid links to sites outside of eBay should use the target="_blank" attribute in the a href tag so a new browser window will be loaded when the link is clicked instead of buyers being redirected off of eBay.
  **Max length**: 500,000 characters (including all markup tags/CSS).
  """
  description: String
  """
  This array is used to specify a list of image URLs that will become photos in the listing's photo gallery. Most eBay categories support up to 24 photos per listing at no extra charge. The URLs used in this array must use 'https'. Either all eBay Picture Services (EPS) or all self-hosted picture URLs may be used in this array, but not a combination of both.
  **Max images allowed on a listing**: 24
  """
  imageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]
  """
  This container is used to express the condition of the item(s) in this listing. A large majority of eBay categories require a condition, and this condition is specified through a numeric identifier in the **conditionId** field. For non-new items, it is highly recommended that the **conditionDescription** field be used to provide specific details about the item's condition or 'wear and tear'. The **conditionDescriptor** array is used to provide condition details of graded and ungraded trading cards in a structured manner.
  """
  itemCondition: CreateListingItemConditionInput
  """
  This array is used to define the motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles. Year, Make, and Model are typical aspects used to identify a motor vehicle.
  **Max compatibilities allowed on a listing**: 3000
  """
  listingCompatibilities: CreateListingItemCompatibilitiesInput
  """
  This container is needed for motor vehicle listings to provide the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
  """
  motorVehicleIdentifier: CreateListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput
  """
  This field is used to add the product title displayed on the listing. This field is required unless the listing uses an eBay catalog product (in which case the title is obtained from the eBay catalog product) or if the listing is for a motor vehicle (in which case the vehicle’s Make, Model, and Year serve as the title).
  **Max length**: 80 characters.
  """
  title: String
  """
  This array is used to add a seller's video to the listing. A unique identifier for a seller's video is passed into this array to add a product video to the listing. Although a video can be added to a listing before it is in the `LIVE` state, the video won't be available for viewing in the listing until it does reach this state. To know more about the video upload process and various states for a video, see the [Media API documentation](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/media/overview).
  **Note**: Currently, only one video may be added to each listing.
  """
  videoIds: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide product safety information for an item, including product safety statements and pictograms. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
"""
input CreateListingProductSafetyInput {
  """
  This free-form text field is used to provide additional product safety information that goes beyond what is expressed through the pictogram(s) and/or safety statements.     **Note**: This field cannot be used without the **pictogramCodes** and/or **statementCodes** arrays.
  **Max length**: 120 characters
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to provide one to four product safety pictogram codes, and if successful, the pictogram(s) associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes, and this method will also return the URLs to the pictograms so that these pictograms can be previewed before adding them to a listing.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This array is used to provide one to eight product safety statement codes, and if successful, the safety statements associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes and the safety statements associated with them.
  **Max number of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to attach one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
"""
input CreateListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to specify one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
  **Note**: Up to 6 separate product compliance policies are allowed per country.
  """
  countryPolicies: [CreateListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide country-specific takeback policies. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy.
"""
input CreateListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to specify a country-specific takeback policy. Each country may only have one country-specific takeback policy.
  """
  countryPolicies: [CreateListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
"""
input CreateListingRegulatoryInput {
  """
  This array is used to attach one or more documents to the listing using their unique identifiers. The **Media API** is used to upload documents to a seller's account. See the [DocumentTypeEnum](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/media/types/api:DocumentTypeEnum) type of the **Media API** for the full list of supported document types.
  **Max number of document IDs allowed**: 10.
  """
  documentIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used to provide Energy Efficiency Label related information for such category types as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend Energy Efficiency Label information.
  """
  energyEfficiencyLabel: CreateListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput
  """
  This container is used to provide hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
  """
  hazardousMaterial: CreateListingHazardousMaterialInput
  """
  This container is used to provide the name and contact information for the manufacturer of the item. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
  """
  manufacturer: CreateListingManufacturerInput
  """
  This container is used to provide product safety related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
  """
  productSafety: CreateListingProductSafetyInput
  """
  This field is used to provide the manufacturer's repair index score for a product. This value should be between 0.1 (extremely difficult to fix) to 10 (extremely easy to fix). A maximum of one digit to the right of the decimal point may be used. 0 or 0.0 should never be used as values as this would indicate that the product is not repairable.
  **Min value**: 0.1
  **Max value**: 10.0
  """
  repairIndexScore: Float
  """
  This array is used to provide the name and contact information for one or more responsible persons based in the EU. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide either the product manufacturer or responsible person(s) contact information in their eBay listings. This array is only necessary if the product manufacturer contact is not based in an EU country.
  **Max number of EU responsible persons allowed**: 5.
  """
  responsiblePersons: [CreateListingResponsiblePersonInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide the name and contact information for one or more responsible persons based in the EU.
"""
input CreateListingResponsiblePersonInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide a street address for a responsible person.
  """
  address: CreateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field is used to provide the company name associated with the responsible person.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String!
  """
  This container is used to provide the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the responsible person. At least one of the three is required if a responsible person is supplied.
  """
  contact: CreateListingBusinessEntityContactInput
  """
  This array is required for each responsible person specified, and the only allowed value is `EU_RESPONSIBLE_PERSON`.
  **Max number of person types allowed**: 1.
  """
  personTypes: [String!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide a domestic return policy or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This type also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this type if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
"""
input CreateListingReturnTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify a return business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all return policy settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/return_policy/methods/getReturnPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all return business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
  This container is used to state the seller's domestic return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period. 
  **Note**: If the listing only has a domestic return policy set up, but the item is shipped internationally, the settings in this container will also apply to international returns.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  domesticReturnTerms: CreateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to state the seller's international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  internationalReturnTerms: CreateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This free-form text field is used to provide more details about a seller's return policy. Currently, this field is only supported on the EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT, EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, and EBAY_ES marketplaces.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  **Max length**: 8000 (for EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT); 5000 (for EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, EBAY_ES).
  """
  returnInstructions: String
}

"""
This type is used to state the seller's domestic or international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
"""
input CreateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput {
  """
  This field specifies the refund method that will be used if the buyer returns the item. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item. Currently, the only supported value for this field is `MONEY_BACK`.
  **Note**: Although `MONEY_BACK_OR_REPLACEMENT` is defined in the schema, replacement items are not currently supported in Returns flow, so `MONEY_BACK` is the only option.
  """
  refundMethod: ListingRefundMethod
  """
  This field must be included and set to 'true' if the seller accepts returns for the item or 'false' if the seller does not accept returns for the item.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  returnAccepted: Boolean = false
  """
  This field specifies the amount of time the buyer has to return an item. The return duration begins when the item is marked 'delivered' at the buyer's specified ship-to location. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and sets the number of days that a buyer has to return the item for a full refund. Supported values are `DAYS_14`, `DAYS_30`, and `DAYS_60`. The supported return periods can vary by category (with `DAYS_14` limited to just a few categories), and the [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getReturnPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** can be used to see the supported return periods for a category.
  """
  returnDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This field specifies either the buyer or the seller as the party who pays for return shipping charges. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and specifies the person responsible for return shipping costs if the item is returned due to a buyer remorse. See the [`Invoicee`] for the list of supported enumeration values. The seller is always responsible for return shipping costs when an item is being returned due to a Significantly not as described (SNAD) issue.
  """
  returnShipmentInvoicee: Invoicee
}

"""
This type is used to specify the days and times when a seller may be contacted regarding a classified ad listing. This container is used by the **primarySellerContactHours** and **secondarySellerContactHours** containers and the days specified here should not overlap between the two.
"""
input CreateListingSellerContactHoursInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller is available the full 24 hours on the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. If this field is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  anyTime: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is used to indicate the end time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursEndAt** value should always be later than the **supportHoursStartAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursEndAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to indicate the start time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursStartAt** value should always be earlier than the **supportHoursEndAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursStartAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to specify the block of days that the support hours will apply to.
  See the [`ListingDaysCode`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  supportOnDays: ListingDaysCode
}

"""
This type is used for classified ad listings, and provides contact information for the seller, including days and hours when the seller accepts inquiries from potential buyers.
"""
input CreateListingSellerContactInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify the first line of the street address of the seller.
  """
  addressLine1: String
  """
  This field is used to specify the second line of the seller's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """This field sets the company name (if any) associated with the seller."""
  companyName: String @deprecated(reason: "Company name is no longer supported")
  """
  This field is used to indicate whether potential buyers can contact the seller via email. A value of 'true' in this field indicates that potential buyers can contact the seller of the listing via email.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  contactByEmailEnabled: Boolean = false
  """
  Two-letter [ISO 3166 Country Codes](https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html) to indicate which country the seller is located.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """This field is used to specify the county where the seller resides."""
  county: String
  """This field is used to specify the seller's phone number."""
  phone: String
  """
  This container is used to provide the seller's primary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekdays. This container should always be provided to let potential buyers know when the seller may be contacted.
  """
  primarySellerContactHours: CreateListingSellerContactHoursInput
  """
  This container is used to provide the seller's secondary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekends if the support hours vary on weekends.
  """
  secondarySellerContactHours: CreateListingSellerContactHoursInput
}

"""
This type is used to provide information on domestic and international shipping, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated) and the shipping service options available to ship the item. There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to apply a shipping discount.
"""
input CreateListingShippingOptionsInput {
  """
  This field is included to apply a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  """
  combinedShippingRuleId: ID
  """
  This field sets the shipping cost type for locations within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping. If this field is not included, the shipping cost type will default to flat-rate shipping. Note that all of the specified shipping services should support the shipping cost type specified here.
  **Note**: To specify local pick only option for listings, set this field to `NOT_SPECIFIED`.
  """
  costType: ListingShippingType
  """
  This field can be included if the seller applies a flat-rate handling cost for shipping. This cost is in addition to whatever the final shipping cost is based on the buyer's location and selected shipping service option.
  """
  packageHandlingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' to enable a seller's promotional shipping discount for the listing. A seller can only have one promotional shipping discount active on a marketplace. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the details of the promotional shipping discount, and the [SetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/SetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to add/modify the promotional shipping discount.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  promotionalShipping: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is included to apply a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  """
  rateTableId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use shippingRateTableId instead")
  """
  This field is included to apply a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  """
  shippingDiscountRuleId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use combinedShippingRuleId instead")
  """
  This field is included to apply a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  """
  shippingRateTableId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to provide information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions.
"""
input CreateListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput {
  """
  This field should be included and set to 'true' if the package has an irregular or non-standard shape. A shipping carrier may charge additional handling fees for an irregular package.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  irregularPackage: Boolean = false
  """
  The measurement system used by the marketplace for the package dimensions and weight. If the value is not supplied, the default measurement system for the marketplace will be used. See [`MeasurementSystem`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  measurementSystem: MeasurementSystem
  """
  This container is used to specify the dimensions of the shipping package.
  """
  packageDimensions: CreateListingPackageDimensionsInput
  """
  This field is used to indicate the type of package used to ship the item. See the [`ListingPackageType`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  packageType: ListingPackageType
  """
  This container is used to specify the weight of the shipping package. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type.
  """
  packageWeight: CreateListingPackageWeightInput
}

"""
This type is used to set the list of domestic or international shipping service options that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
**Maximum number of domestic shipping services**: 4
**Maximum number of international shipping services**: 5
"""
input CreateListingShippingServiceInput {
  """
  This field sets the flat-rate shipping cost to ship each additional unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for multiple-quantity, fixed price listings using flat-rate shipping. The cost specified in this field must be the same or lower than the cost specified in the **shippingCost** field, with the idea being that multiple quantities of the line item might be shipped in the same shipping package, decreasing the per-unit cost for shipping.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This array can be used to set the geographical regions or individual countries that the corresponding international shipping service operates in.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  The integer value specified here controls the order in which the corresponding shipping service will be displayed in the View Item page. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 for a shipping service that ships within the marketplace or from 5 to 9 for a shipping service that ships outside of marketplace. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page. If this field is not used, the rank and hence order of the shipping services will depend on the order they are specified under the **shippingServices** array.
  """
  rank: Int
  """
  This field sets the flat-rate shipping cost to ship one unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for each shipping service if flat-rate shipping is being used. This field must still be included and set to '0.0' if the corresponding shipping service is offered free of charge to the buyer.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field identifies the domestic or international shipping service and is required for each specified shipping service. Use the [getShippingServices](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices) method to retrieve the full list of domestic and international shipping services supported on a marketplace. The enumeration values representing each shipping service option are returned in the [shippingService](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices#response.shippingServices.shippingService) fields of the **getShippingServices** response.
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID
}

"""
This type is used to provide information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
"""
input CreateListingShippingTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to provide information about the shipping business policy to be used for the listing.
  If this field is used, none of the other fields in CreateListingShippingTermsInput container should be used since all shipping settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getFulfillmentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/fulfillment_policy/methods/getFulfillmentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all fulfillment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicy: CreateShippingBusinessPolicyInput
  """
  This field is only applicable to motor vehicle listings and indicates if the buyer is responsible for shipping or picking up the purchased vehicle.
  **Note**: This field is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  **Default value**: true
  """
  buyerResponsibleForShipping: Boolean = true
  """
  This array is used to specify locations where the seller will not ship the item. The values specified in this array can be continents, geographical regions, countries, or special locations within the marketplace. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: This array is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  excludedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This field indicates how many business days that the seller needs to ship the item after payment is made by the buyer. The handling time is required by most categories. Top-rated sellers typically set the handling time to 0 or 1 day, but longer handling times are supported.
  **Note**: This field is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  handlingTimeDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This array is used to specify locations where the seller will ship the item. The values specified in this array can be geographical regions or countries. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: This array is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This container is used to provide information on shipping, local to the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to apply a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  marketplaceShippingOptions: CreateListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to provide information on shipping not local to the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to apply a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  nonMarketplaceShippingOptions: CreateListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This field is used to provide information of shipping services that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
  **Maximum number of shipping services**: 10, out of which 5 apply for locations within the marketplace and other 5 apply for locations outside of marketplace
  **Note**: This array is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  shippingServices: [CreateListingShippingServiceInput!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **createListing** mutation that is run in `EXECUTE` mode. It will show the complete details of the listing, and will also include a list of non-blocking warning messages if any occurred.
