  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to identify the main trait by which SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing differ, and to provide image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each item variation.
"""
input CreateListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput {
  """
  The trait name by which pictures of the item variations vary. The specified trait will be used to determine which images to display when a buyer selects a variation in the View Item page. For example, if the trait is 'Color', then a corresponding product image in the **traitValueImages** array will be displayed when that color is selected in the View Item page. The trait name specified here must be one of the variation traits specified in the **variationTraits** array.
  """
  traitName: String!
  """
  This array is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the *traitImageUrls** array.
  """
  traitValueImages: [CreateListingVariationTraitValueImageInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to define name-value pairs for the traits where each SKU within a multiple-SKU listing differs, such as 'Color' and 'Size'. Each available color and each available size will be listed through the **variationTraits** array. If the listing featured t-shirts, each variation within that listing would have a unique color and size combination such as 'Blue, Large'.
"""
input CreateListingVariationsInput {
  """
  This container identifies the main trait by which variations differ, and provides image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each variation. For example, the varying trait may be 'Color', and image URLs would be provided showcasing the different color of each variation.
  """
  imagesVaryByTrait: CreateListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput
  """
  This array provides the names of the varying traits and the available values for each of these traits. For example, one trait might be 'Color', and all of the available colors would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. Another trait might be 'Size', and all of the available sizes would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. If the multiple-SKU listing has two varying traits such as 'Color' and 'Size', each variation would have a different combination of each of these traits, such as a 'Large, Red' shirt.
  The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method of the **Taxonomy API** can be used to retrieve aspects that are optional, recommended or required for a specific category. The  [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method in the **Taxonomy API** works similarly but is processed asynchronously and provides optional, recommended or required aspects every leaf category on an eBay marketplace. The [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method can be paired up with the **Taxonomy SDK** to help maintain an up-to-date list of aspects for each leaf category.
  **Max number of traits**: 5.
  **max values per trait**: 50.
  **Max length of each trait name and value**: 65 characters.
  """
  variationTraits: [NameValuesPairInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the **traitImageUrls** array.
"""
input CreateListingVariationTraitValueImageInput {
  """
  An array of one or more images that demonstrate the corresponding **traitValue**. For example, if the **traitName** is 'Color' and the **traitValue** is 'Red', the image(s) would show a red variation of the product. Depending on the product, one image per variation may be enough, but multiple images may be specified for each **traitValue**. For example, it is possible that a seller would want to show the front and back of each shirt in each color.
  **Note** All images, whether they are hosted by eBay Picture Server (EPS) or self-hosted, must comply with eBay picture requirements. eBay Picture Server (EPS) and self-hosted picture URLs should not be mixed, and all URLs must use 'https' and not 'http'.
  **Max number of images per trait value**: 12.
  """
  traitImageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]!
  """
  The trait value of the corresponding image(s) in the **traitImageUrls** array. If the **traitName** is 'Color', values in this field may include *Red*, *Blue*, *Green*, etc. At least one of the variations within the multiple-SKU listing must have this value.
  **Max length**: 65 characters.
  """
  traitValue: String!
}

"""
This type is used to enable listing upgrades such as bold titles in search results, Gallery Plus, or an added subtitle. Each of these listing upgrades will incur a small fee.
"""
input CreateListingVisualEnhancementsInput {
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller wants the listing title to be in boldface type in search results for greater visibility. Applicable listing fees apply. **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing as motor vehicle listing titles are automatically generated by eBay based on Year, Make, Model, and other aspects of the vehicle such as engine type and trim.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  boldTitle: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller wants to use the Gallery Plus feature. With Gallery Plus, a larger gallery image of the item is displayed in search results.
  **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  galleryPlus: Boolean = false
  """
  This field is used to provide a customized subtitle for the listing. By using a subtitle, more keywords can be provided and search results may be improved.
  **Max length**: 55 characters.
  """
  subtitle: String
}

""" This input type defines the payload for the **createOrderCancellation** mutation, identifying the order to cancel, providing a reason, and whether to relist all items.
