}

"""
This input is used by seller to create a new purchase quote when using the **createPurchaseQuote** mutation.
"""
input CreatePurchaseQuoteInput {
  """
  This boolean field is used to control whether or not the seller should receive an email copy of the new purchase quote sent to the buyer. If this field is included and set to 'true', the seller will receive a copy of the new purchase quote in their eBay Inbox.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  emailCopyToSeller: Boolean = false
  """
  This array is used to provide two or more item commitment identifiers that will become a part of the new purchase quote. A comma is used as a delimiter for each item commitment identifier.
  """
  lineItems: [PurchaseQuoteItemInput!]!
  """
  This container is used to add or modify available shipping or pickup logistics options provided by the seller.
  """
  logisticsOptions: PurchaseQuoteLogisticsOptionInput!
  """
  This field allows the seller to provide a custom message to the buyer regarding the new purchase quote.
  **Minimum length**: 1 character
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  messageToBuyer: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify handling charges and/or a shipping discount for a purchase quote.
  """
  total: PurchaseQuoteTotalsInput
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **createPurchaseQuote** mutation.
"""
union CreatePurchaseQuoteOutput = CreatePurchaseQuoteBusinessError | CreatePurchaseQuoteSuccess

"""
This base output type is used for a successful **createPurchaseQuote** mutation, and shows the details of the successfully created purchase quote.
"""
type CreatePurchaseQuoteSuccess {
  """This container shows the successfully created purchase quote."""
  purchaseQuote: PurchaseQuote
}

"""
This input type supports identification of the order line item, quantity, and the return reason.
"""
input CreateReturnLineItemInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the order line item associated with this return. Use this to reference the exact purchased item within the order.
  """
  orderLineItemId: ID!
  """
  The number of units from this line item to be returned. Multi-quantity purchases default to 1 if not provided. This value must be a positive integer and cannot exceed the remaining returnable quantity.
  """
  quantityReturned: Int! = 1
  """
  This field provide notes during return creation. Optionally present only if the requester has provided a note.
    
  **Note:** Constraints:
  - limited special characters allowed for punctuation
  - curse words and profanity are not allowed
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  returnNote: String
  """
  This enumerated value indicates the reason for the return. Available values can change based on the return request and category of the item. In countries where the return reason is not mandatory to provide, it returns as `UNDISCLOSED`.
  """
  returnReason: ReturnReasonInput!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **createReturnRuleListingGroup** mutation, used to create a group of lists that contain listing IDs. Each list can contain up to 5000 listings, with up to 500 listings added to a list in a single call.
"""
input CreateReturnRuleListingGroupInput {
  """
  The seller created unique name for the group.
    
  **Note:** No two groups can have the same name.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  groupName: String!
  """
  A list of listing IDs to be included in the group. Up to a maximum of 5000 listing can be added to a group, with up to 500 listings added to a group in a single call. When this field is used, keep the following in mind:
  - each listing can be part of multiple groups
  - listing IDs must be unique within the group
  - maximum of 500 listings can be added to a group in a single processing
  - minimum of 1 listing must be provided to create a group
    
  **Minimum:** 1 listing
  **Maximum:** 500 listings
  """
  listingIds: [ID!]!
  """
  The ID of the eBay marketplace where the item is listed (for example, `EBAY_US`, `EBAY_DE`, or `EBAY_UK`).
  """
  listingMarketplace: ListingMarketplace!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **createReturnRuleListingGroup** mutation defines the output structure for adding a seller-defined group of listing IDs. This type encapsulates the result of the operation, returning the list details upon success or specific business errors if the creation fails. It returns an error if:
- a group with the supplied name already exists for this seller
- the input request contains duplicate listing IDs
- the request attempts to add more listings than the allowed per-request limit (schema: 500)
- creating or expanding the list would exceed the group's total item capacity (schema: 5000)
- the provided name violates validation rules (length, allowed characters, reserved words)
- the seller has reached the maximum number of groups allowed for their account
- the return rules feature is not enabled for the seller
"""
union CreateReturnRuleListingGroupOutput = ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleListingGroup | ReturnRuleListingGroupDuplicateListingError | ReturnRuleListingGroupInvalidNameError | ReturnRuleListingGroupMaxSizeExceededError | ReturnRuleListingGroupQuotaExceededError | ReturnRuleListingIdsPerRequestLimitExceededError

"""
The base type of the **createSecondChanceListing** mutation. A Second Chance Offer is an offer that a seller makes to a buyer who was a competitive bidder on a recently ended auction listing.
"""
input CreateSecondChanceListingInput {
  """
  This container is used to identify a recently ended listing from which a Second Chance listing will be derived from. The user can either identify the ended listing using its **listingId** value or the item's **sku** value (if defined).
  """
  listingIdentifier: ListingIdentifierInput!
  """
  This container is used to set the duration of the Second Chance listing. For auctions involving motor vehicles or other high-priced items where the Reserve Price was never met and there was no winning bidder, the **fixedPrice** should be included. Otherwise, the Second Chance listing price automatically defaults to the recipient user's highest bid during the ending auction and the **fixedPrice** should not be included.
  """
  listingTerms: SecondChanceListingTermsInput!
  """
  The marketplace identifier of the listing. See [`ListingMarketplace`] enum for supported values.
  """
  marketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
  This container allows a user to run a **createSecondChanceListing** mutation in validation mode, which means that the listing object will be validated, but a successful mutation will not create the Second Chance Offer. 
  """
  options: ListingOptionsInput
  """
  The eBay User ID of the bidder who will receive the Second Chance Offer. This user must have made at least one qualifying bid in the ended auction listing.
  """
  recipientUserId: ID!
  """
  This field can be used if the seller wishes to share a message with the buyer about why the offer is being made and perhaps highlighting the conditions of the offer. The recipient will get this offer in eBay Inbox, and the text provided here will be included in that email.
  **Note**: The provided message can not contain HTML markup, asterisks, or quotes.
  **Max length**: 1000 characters.
  """
  sellerMessage: String
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **createSecondChanceListing** mutation. Three possible results of a **createSecondChanceListing** mutation are: a listing container (and possibly one or more warnings); a listing container with validation success and possibly one or more warnings; or an array of blocking errors if the mutation fails and a Second Chance Offer is not created. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error, and there may also be one or more warning messages that are triggered.
"""
union CreateSecondChanceListingOutput = CreateSecondChanceListingSuccess | CreateSecondChanceListingValidationError | CreateSecondChanceListingValidationSuccess

"""
This type is used for a successful **createSecondChanceListing** mutation that is run in `EXECUTE` mode. It will show the complete details of the listing, and will also include a list of non-blocking warning messages if any occurred.
"""
type CreateSecondChanceListingSuccess {
  """
  This container provides the full listing details of a successfully created Second Chance Offer. This container will be generated unless one or more blocking errors were triggered.
  """
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows any non-blocking warnings generated during the processing of the **createSecondChanceListing** mutation.
  **Note**: This array is returned as empty if there are no warnings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used when the **createSecondChanceListing** mutation fails due to one or more blocking validation errors. A list of validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying will be shown, and one or more non-blocking warning messages will also be shown if any were triggered during the processing of the mutation.
"""
type CreateSecondChanceListingValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. This code can be used by clients to programmatically identify and handle different types of errors without relying on error messages, which may change over time.     
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains a list of blocking validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying.
  """
  violations: [ListingValidationRuleViolation!]!
  """
  This array contains a list of non-blocking validation warnings that do not block processing but provide useful feedback for improving listings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **createSecondChanceListing** mutation that is run in `VALIDATE` mode, and the listing object is successfully validated without any errors. The results of the validation will be shown, including warnings if any occurred.
"""
type CreateSecondChanceListingValidationSuccess {
  """
  This container shows the full listing details of the successfully validated Second Chance listing object.
  """
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
     This array shows the list of non-blocking warnings generated during the validation, if any occurred.
  **Note**: This array is returned as empty if there are no warnings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This container is used to provide information of shipping business policy to be used for the listing.
If this field is used, none of the other fields in CreateListingShippingTermsInput container should be used since all shipping settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getFulfillmentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/fulfillment_policy/methods/getFulfillmentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all fulfillment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
