"""
This type defines the unique identifier of a custom list and the reason the custom list operation failed. 
"""
type CustomListFailure {
  """The unique identifier of the custom list that failed to be retrieved."""
  customListId: ID!
  """The reason the custom list failed to be retrieved. """
  reason: CustomListFailureReason!
}

"""
This enumerated type contains the reason a custom list operation failed.
"""
enum CustomListFailureReason {
  """The specified custom list cannot be found."""
  CUSTOM_LIST_NOT_FOUND
}

"""
This type defines an individual item within a user's custom list. This type contains the item details along with custom list-specific metadata like the price of the item when added to a custom list.
"""
type CustomListItem {
  """
  The date and time this item was added to this specific custom Watchlist.
  **Format**: ISO 8601 date-time string ('YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sssZ')
  **Timezone**: UTC
  """
  addedAt: DateTime!
  """This container returns information for an item in this custom list."""
  item: Item!
}

"""
This type defines the paginated response containing items from a specific custom list and provides efficient access to large collections of custom list items.
"""
type CustomListItems {
  """
  This container returns pagination information for navigating through multiple pages of custom list items.
  """
  pagination: Pagination
  """
  This array returns a list of items in the custom list. Items are ordered by the date they were added to the custom list with the most recent first. This array may be empty if the custom list has no items or if the requested page is beyond available data.
  """
  results: [CustomListItem!]!
}

"""
This type is used to specify the input parameters for retrieving items from a specific custom Watchlist.
**Note**: All parameters are optional. If not provided, default values will be used.
"""
input CustomListItemsInput {
  """
  This container can be used to specify optional pagination settings used to control page size and navigate through multiple pages of results. If pagination settings are not provided through this input, default pagination parameters will be applied.
  """
  pagination: PageInfoInput
}

"""
This type shows any global or marketplace-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies enabled for a listing.
"""
type CustomPolicies {
  """
  An array of one to six product compliance policy ID values, representing one or more product compliance policies that are applicable to the listing. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. The product compliance policies in this array will apply to all countries where the seller ships the item. Marketplace-specific product compliance policies are indicated with the **regionalProductCompliancePolicies** field.
  """
  productCompliancePolicyIds: [ID!]
  """
  The set of marketplace-specific product compliance policies that are associated with the listing. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. For example, if you sell batteries in a country requiring disclosures that apply only to that marketplace, a marketplace-specific product compliance policy could contain this information. Each listing may have up to six (6) product compliance policies for each of the following countries: `GB`, `DE`, `FR`, `IT`, and `ES`. Global product compliance policies are indicated with the **productCompliancePolicyIds** array.
  """
  regionalProductCompliancePolicies: RegionalProductCompliancePolicies
  """
  The set of marketplace-specific take-back policies that are associated with the listing. The law in some countries may require sellers to take back a used product when the buyer buys a new product. Each marketplace may only have one specific take-back policy. A global take-back policy should be set with the **takebackPolicyId** field instead. Each listing may include one (1) marketplace-specific take-back policy for each of the following countries: `GB`, `DE`, `FR`, `IT`, and `ES`.
  """
  regionalTakeBackPolicies: RegionalTakeBackPolicies
  """
  The unique identifier of a global take-back policy. The take-back policy set with this field will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Region-specific policies are set with the **regionalTakeBackPolicies** field.
  """
  takeBackPolicyId: ID
}

"""
This type indicates the item is returned because it was damaged when received. Displays as **Damaged item received**.
"""
type DamagedItemReceived implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `DAMAGED_ITEM_RECEIVED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates that the item was received damaged, likely during shipping.
"""
type DamagedItemReturned implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `RECEIVED_DAMAGED_ITEM`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable case referral reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""A slightly refined version of RFC-3339 compliant DateTime Scalar"""
scalar DateTime

"""
This type is used to set the time range if a **dateRange** filter is used. All item commitments either created or updated within this time range are retrieved.
"""
input DateTimeRangeInput {
  """
  An ISO 8601 standard timestamp, using UTC time zone. All item commitments created or updated on this or before this date, and after or on the date in the **startDateTime** field are retrieved. 
  **Note**: This date must be a later date than the date in the **startDateTime** field or an error will occur.
  **Format**: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
  **Example**: 2025-12-16T14:30:00Z
  """
  endDateTime: DateTime!
  """
  An ISO 8601 standard timestamp, using UTC time zone. All item commitments created or updated on this or after this date, and before or on the date in the **endDateTime** field are retrieved. 
  **Note**: This date must be an earlier date than the date in the **endDateTime** field or an error will occur.
  **Format**: YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
  **Example**: 2025-12-12T14:30:00Z
  """
  startDateTime: DateTime!
}

"""
A scalar representing precise decimal numeric values.
**Format**: String-encoded decimal value with arbitrary precision (e.g., '10.99', '1000.00', '0.001').
**Usage**: Used for monetary amounts, measurements, and other values requiring decimal precision.
**Example**: '19.99' for a price, '1.75' for a weight or measurement.
**Note**: Preserves exact decimal representation without floating-point rounding errors, making it suitable for financial calculations and other precision-sensitive values.
"""
scalar Decimal

""" This input type provides the fulfillment details used to support and explain declining the cancellation.
"""
input DeclineCancellationFulfillmentDetailsInput {
  """ The tracking number provided by the shipping carrier for this fulfillment. 
  """
  shipmentTrackingDetails: [DeclineCancellationShipmentTrackingDetailsInput!]
  """ The optional timestamp when the seller shipped the item. """
  shippedAt: DateTime
}

"""
This error type is returned when the decline cancellation request contains validation rule violations.
"""
type DeclineCancellationInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The globally unique error code for this business error. For this type, the value is `CNCL_DECLINE_REQ_VALIDATION_RULE_VIOLATION`.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the error message. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  A list of one or more validation violations for the decline cancellation request. This list is only returned when a violation is present.
  """
  violations: [DeclineCancellationViolation!]!
}

""" This input type provides the shipment tracking details for a declined cancellation. 
"""
input DeclineCancellationShipmentTrackingDetailsInput {
  """
  The tracking number provided by the shipping carrier for this shipment. Ensure accuracy as the buyer will use this number to track the shipment and the number cannot be verified by eBay. 
    
  Required if you include the **shippingCarrierCode** field.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  shipmentTrackingNumber: String!
  """
  The code or identifier for the shipping carrier handling the shipment. 
    
  Required if you include the **shipmentTrackingNumber** field.
  """
  shippingCarrierCode: String!
}

"""
This interface represents the validation violations encountered when attempting to decline a cancellation.
"""
interface DeclineCancellationViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the validation rule that was violated.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A developer-facing, human-readable string description of the violated validation rule. This message is intended for debugging and logs, not for displaying to end users. This string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This type, available for the seller, is used to decline cancellation action on the contract.
"""
type DeclineContractCancellationAction implements ContractCancellationAction {
  """
  The machine-readable cancellation action code for this use case. For this type, the value is `DECLINE`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message explaining the cancellation action code. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

""" This input type defines the payload for the **declineContractCancellation** mutation. It specifies the cancellation to decline and optionally includes fulfillment information. 
"""
input DeclineContractCancellationInput {
  """ The ID of the contract cancellation to decline. """
  cancellationId: ID!
  """ Optional additional fulfillment details for the contract cancellation decline, such as the dates shipped and tracking information. 
  """
  fulfillmentDetails: DeclineCancellationFulfillmentDetailsInput
}

"""
This union type defines the response payload for the **declineContractCancellation** mutation. On success, the response includes a **DeclineContractCancellationSuccess** type object; on failure it returns an error indicating the reason that the cancellation failed.

**Note:** Additional types may be added to this union in the future; clients should handle unrecognized types gracefully.
"""
union DeclineContractCancellationOutput = ContractCancellationActionNotPermittedError | ContractCancellationNotFoundError | DeclineCancellationInputValidationError | DeclineContractCancellationSuccess

"""
This type is returned when a contract cancellation has been successfully declined.
"""
type DeclineContractCancellationSuccess {
  """The successfully declined contract cancellation."""
  contractCancellation: ContractCancellation!
}

"""
The base request type for the **declineOffer** method. This type defines the input information needed for declining an active offer. This includes the item ID and offer ID associated with the offer being declined, as well as an optional message explain why the offer was not accepted.
"""
input DeclineOfferInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the purchasable item for which the offer is being declined.
  """
  itemId: ID!
  """
  An optional message explaining the reason the offer was declined. This message will be visible to the seller and can be used to explain why the offer was not accepted.
  **Maximum length**: 250 characters
  """
  message: String
  """
  The unique identifier of the offer being declined. The offer must have the 'PENDING' status and the user must be authorized to decline it.
  """
  offerId: ID!
}

"""
The union type for the **declineOffer** mutation. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **declineOffer** mutation succeeds, the offer will be declined and information about the declined offer will be returned. If the **declineOffer** mutation fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the offer will not be declined. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error.
"""
union DeclineOfferOutput = DeclineOfferSent | OfferBusinessRulesViolated | ReferenceArgumentsNotFound

"""
This type is used for a successful **declineOffer** mutation. On success, details about the declined offer are returned, such as the offer ID and updated status.
"""
type DeclineOfferSent {
  """
  This container returns details about the offer that was declined using the **declineOffer** mutation. This information includes the offer ID and updated status ('DECLINED') of the offer being declined.
  """
  offer: NegotiationOfferDetails!
}

"""This action type is used by a seller declining a return request."""
type DeclineReturnAction implements ReturnAction {
