  """
  A human-readable error message describing the issue.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains details about one or more specific request violations.
  """
  violations: [DeclineReturnInputViolation!]!
}

"""
This interface represents input violations detected during decline return request evaluation. Each violation indicates that the provided input value did not comply with the business rules or constraints defined for declining the return, such as rules that may include the maximum allowed characters for declination note. Such constraints are governed by eBay's return policies, and may vary based on context, marketplace, or configuration.
"""
interface DeclineReturnInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific decline return input violation.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the decline return input violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **declineReturn** mutation includes the result of the mutation and any errors encountered.
"""
union DeclineReturnOutput = DeclineReturnInputValidationError | OrderReturn | ReturnActionNotPermittedError | ReturnNotFoundError

"""
This type indicates the item is returned because it is defective. Displays as **Defective**.
"""
type Defective implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `DEFECTIVE`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **deleteReturnRuleListingGroup** mutation used for deleting a group of **listingIds**. Once deleted:
- the group cannot be recovered
- if any rule is using this group, the corresponding rules will be marked disabled
"""
input DeleteReturnRuleListingGroupInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the listing group to be deleted.
    
  **Note:** Deletion is permanent. Once deleted, the group cannot be recovered and if any rule is using this group, the corresponding rules will be marked disabled.
  """
  returnRuleListingGroupId: ID!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **deleteReturnRuleListingGroup** mutation returns the seller's listing groups that were successfully deleted or an error if the provided listing group ID is invalid (one that does not exist for this seller).
"""
union DeleteReturnRuleListingGroupOutput = DeleteReturnRuleListingGroupSuccess | ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleListingGroupNotFoundError

"""The details of a seller's group of listing IDs successfully deleted."""
type DeleteReturnRuleListingGroupSuccess {
  """The name of the listing group defined by the seller."""
  groupName: String!
  """The unique identifier of a listing list."""
  returnRuleListingGroupId: ID!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **deleteSellerReturnRule** mutation, which deletes a rule. Once deleted:
- the rule is no longer active and will not be evaluated
- the rule cannot be modified or re-enabled
"""
input DeleteSellerReturnRuleInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the rule to delete.
    
  **Note:** Deletion is permanent. Once deleted, the rule is no longer active, will not be evaluated, and cannot be modified or re-enabled.
  """
  ruleId: ID!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **deleteSellerReturnRule** mutation which indicates whether the seller's automation rule status was successfully deleted or if an error occurred that prevented the deletion:
- the provided **ruleId** does not exist
- the return rules feature is not enabled for the seller
- 
"""
union DeleteSellerReturnRuleOutput = DeleteSellerReturnRuleSuccess | ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleNotFoundError

"""
This type defines a successfully deleted return rule and contains its name and ID.
"""
type DeleteSellerReturnRuleSuccess {
  """The name of the deleted rule."""
  name: String!
  """The unique identifier of the deleted rule."""
  ruleId: ID!
}

"""
The base request type for the **deleteUserNote** mutation. This type defines the item or order line item for which the user note will be deleted. The input must specify the exact same item ID or order line item ID specified when creating the user note. If not, the mutation will fail. 
"""
input DeleteUserNoteInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the purchasable item in a single-SKU or multiple-SKU listing for which the user note is being deleted.
  """
  itemId: ID!
  """
  The unique identifier of the order line item for which the user note is being deleted. This field must be used if the user note being deleted is associated with a specific order line item.
  """
  orderLineItemId: ID
}

"""
The union type for the **deleteUserNote** mutation. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **deleteUserNote** mutation succeeds, a **userNote** container that returns the user note that was successfully deleted will be returned. If the **deleteUserNote** mutation fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the user note will not be deleted. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error. 
"""
union DeleteUserNoteOutput = DeleteUserNoteSuccess | ReferenceArgumentsNotFound

"""
This type is used for a successful **deleteUserNote** mutation. On success, user note that was successfully deleted is returned. 
"""
type DeleteUserNoteSuccess {
  """
  This container returns the user note that was successfully deleted. This container will also return the order line item ID if the note is for an order line item.
  """
  userNote: UserNote!
}

"""
This type indicates the buyer is returning the item due to personal preference (they did not like the item). Displays as **Did not like item**.
"""
type DidNotLikeItem implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `DID_NOT_LIKE_ITEM`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable return reason that is intended for display only. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type provides details about a digital delivery step in progress, and includes the digital delivery step state and completion date (if complete).
"""
type DigitalDeliveryExecution {
  """
  This timestamp shows the actual time that the digital delivery step was completed. This field is returned if applicable and available.
  """
  completedAt: DateTime
  """
  This container shows the current state of fulfillment that this digital delivery step is contributing towards. 
  """
  fulfillmentState: LogisticsFulfillmentState!
}

"""
This type provides details about a planned digital delivery step prior to execution.
"""
type DigitalDeliveryPlan {
  """
  This timestamp shows the latest acceptable time by which the digital delivery step should be completed. This field is returned if applicable and available.
  """
  sendBy: DateTime
}

"""
This union type is used by the **DigitalDeliveryPlan** type to provide details about a planned digital delivery step and by the **DigitalDeliveryExecution** type to provide details about a digital delivery step in progress. 
"""
union DigitalDeliveryPlanOrExecution = DigitalDeliveryExecution | DigitalDeliveryPlan

"""
This type is used to convey information about a digital delivery logistics point involved in a fulfillment plan.
"""
type DigitalDeliveryPoint implements LogisticsPoint {
  """
  The shipping address associated with this digital delivery logistics point, if applicable. This may be null.
  """
  address: PurchaseAddress
  """
  The user-friendly name of the digital delivery logistics point (for example `Customer Email Address`).
  """
  name: String!
  """
  The recipient of the item via digital delivery. This will either be an email address if the item is delivered to an external address, or a public username if the item is delivered to the buyer's eBay InBox.
  """
  recipient: DigitalUser!
  """
  The functional role of the digital delivery logistics point in the logistics flow (for example, `DIGITAL_SOURCE` or `DIGITAL_DESTINATION`).
  """
  type: DisplayableId!
}

"""
This type convey details of a digital delivery logistics step involved in a fulfillment plan. 
"""
type DigitalDeliveryStep implements LogisticsStep {
  """
  This container shows details of the digital delivery location, which is typically an email address.
  """
  deliveryPoint: LogisticsPoint!
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the party responsible for handling this digital delivery logistics step.
  """
  handler: DisplayableId
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the digital delivery logistics step, for example `Email Delivery`.
  """
  methodName: DisplayableId!
  """
  The information shown in this container is dependent on the state of the logistics step. If the logistics step has not yet started and there is no hold associated with the logistics step, it may get returned as empty or null. If the logistics step is active or completed, the state and full  details for this digital delivery step will be shown. 
  """
  planOrExecution: DigitalDeliveryPlanOrExecution!
}

"""
This type is used to identify the email address of the recipient of a digital item.
"""
type DigitalEmailUser {
  """The email address of the recipient of a digital item."""
  email: String!
}

"""
This type is used to identify the eBay username of the recipient of a digital item. This type is used if a digital item will be delivered to the eBay InBox of the recipient.
"""
type DigitalSiteUser {
  """The eBay username of the recipient of a digital item."""
  name: String!
}

"""
This union type is used by the **DigitalEmailUser** type and the **DigitalSiteUser** type to identify the recipient of a digital item. 
"""
union DigitalUser = DigitalEmailUser | DigitalSiteUser

"""
This enumerated type consists of the units of measurement that are used to specify shipping package dimensions.
