"""
This type is used to specify which listing to end and the reason for ending it.
"""
input EndListingInput {
  """
  The field is used to provide the seller's reason to end the listing. See the [`EndListingReason`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  endListingReason: EndListingReason!
  """
  This container is used to identify the listing to be ended. It can either be identified with the **listingId** or the SKU value if defined in the active listing.
  """
  listingIdentifier: ListingIdentifierInput!
  """
  This container is used to identify the listing to be ended. It can either be identified with the **listingId** or the SKU value if defined in the active listing.
  """
  listingIdentifierInput: ListingIdentifierInput @deprecated(reason: "use listingIdentifier instead")
}

"""
This union type is used for the response of an **endListing** mutation. Two possible results of a **endListing** mutation will be a **listing** container (and possibly one or more **warnings**), or an array of blocking errors if the mutation fails and the listing is not ended successfully. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error, and there may also be one or more warning messages that are triggered.
"""
union EndListingOutput = EndListingSuccess | EndListingValidationError

"""
This enumeration type is used to define the enumeration values that can be used/returned as a reason why a seller is ending an eBay listing before its scheduled end date.
"""
enum EndListingReason {
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending an auction listing to sell the item to the current high bidder. This ending reason and action could not be taken if there were less than 12 hours before the end of the auction.
  """
  END_AUCTION_AND_SELL
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a listing due to the item being out-of-stock.
  """
  END_ITEM_ON_ZERO_QUANTITY
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a listing due to a non-price related error.
  """
  ERROR_IN_LISTING
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a listing due to a price-related error.
  """
  ERROR_IN_PRICE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a listing because the item is lost or broken/damaged.
  """
  LOST
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a listing because the seller no longer wishes to sell the item.
  """
  NOT_AVAILABLE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates that the seller is ending a classified ad listing because the item has been sold. This value only applies to motor vehicle classified ad listings.
  """
  SOLD_VEHICLE
}

"""
This output type is used when an **endListing** mutation is successful, and shows the full details of the listing that was just ended, and will also show one or more warnings if any occurred during the processing of the mutation.
"""
type EndListingSuccess {
  """
  This container shows the full details of the listing that was just successfully ended.
  """
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows any non-blocking warnings generated during the processing of the **endListing** mutation.
  **Note**: This array is returned as empty if there are no warnings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used when the **endListing** mutation fails due to one or more blocking validation errors. A list of validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying will be shown, and one or more non-blocking warning messages will also be shown if any were triggered during the processing of the mutation.
"""
type EndListingValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. This code can be used by clients to programmatically identify and handle different types of errors without relying on error messages, which may change over time.     
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains a list of blocking validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying.
  """
  violations: [ListingValidationRuleViolation!]!
  """
  This array contains a list of non-blocking validation warnings that do not block processing but provide useful feedback for improving listings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This container provides information about the energy efficiency for certain durable goods
"""
