"""
This type is used to provide details on a shipping-related logistics available to the buyer to receive the item. Information included for each shipping logistics option includes seller-specified or calculated shipping cost, both the user-friendly description and enum value associated with the shipping service, and the estimated delivery time window (in hours).
"""
type ItemCommitmentShippingLogisticsOption implements ItemCommitmentLogisticsOptions {
  """
  The total shipping cost for the item if the corresponding shipping service is used. Multiple values/currencies will be shown if the buyer or seller use a different currency than the default currency of the eBay marketplace.
  """
  cost: AmountSet
  """
  The user-friendly description of the shipping service option.
  **Maximum length**: 100 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric, and may include spaces and capitalization
  """
  displayName: String
  """
  This field will indicate the latest estimated delivery time that the buyer can expect to receive the item if the corresponding shipping service is used. The value returned here will be a positive integer value representing hours. This value will generally be in 24-hour increments indicating the longest amount of business days in which the buyer could receive the item. Estimated delivery times consider the seller's stated handling time plus the expected transit time range of the shipping service.
  **Note**: Sellers generally do not ship items until the buyer's payment has cleared, so this delivery window should really only be considered after payment has been made by the buyer.
  """
  maxDeliveryTimeInHours: String
  """
  This field will indicate the earliest estimated delivery time that the buyer can expect to receive the item if the corresponding shipping service is used. The value returned here will be a positive integer value representing hours. This value will generally be in 24-hour increments indicating the shortest amount of business days in which the buyer could receive the item. Estimated delivery times consider the seller's stated handling time plus the expected transit time range of the shipping service.
  **Note**: Sellers generally do not ship items until the buyer's payment has cleared, so this delivery window should really only be considered after payment has been made by the buyer.
  """
  minDeliveryTimeInHours: String
  """
  The enumeration value associated with the shipping service. In listing and Business Policy APIs, the enumeration values of shipping services are specified to set the shipping services that are available to ship the item. 
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID
}

"""
This input type is used when retrieving item commitments for an authenticated seller or buyer. The **itemCommitmentsFirstPage** container is used for an initial search of item commitments, and includes parameters to retrieve item commitments in specific states and/or from a specific listing, as well as a field to control the number of item commitments retrieved per page of results. The **itemCommitmentsPage** container is used for a subsequent search of item commitments, and allows the user to retrieve the next or previous page of results if the query produced multiple pages of results.
**Note**: Either the **itemCommitmentsFirstPage** container or the **itemCommitmentsPage** container may be used, but not both.
"""
input ItemCommitmentsInput {
  """
  This container is used for the initial query of item commitments, and includes parameters to retrieve item commitments in specific states and/or from a specific listing, as well as a field to control the number of item commitments retrieved per page of results.
  """
  itemCommitmentsFirstPage: ItemCommitmentsFirstPageInput
  """
  This container is used for a subsequent search of item commitments, and allows the user to retrieve the next or previous page of results if the query produced multiple pages of results.
  """
  itemCommitmentsPage: PageInfoInput
}

"""
This is the base output type used for **itemCommitments** queries. The **sellerItemCommitments** container is used when queries are being made on behalf of an authenticated seller, and the **buyerItemCommitments** container is used when queries are being made on behalf of an authenticated buyer.
"""
type ItemCommitmentsOutput {
  """
  This container shows all item commitments that match the search criteria for an authenticated buyer. 
  
  Execution Errors:
  | Code                  |  Message                                                                     |
  |-----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | BAD_INPUT_VALUE       |  Input value is not correct.                                                 |
  | INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR |  System failure.                                                             |
  """
  buyerItemCommitments(input: ItemCommitmentsInput!): PaginatedItemCommitments! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.commitment.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.commitment"])
  """
  This container shows all item commitments that match the search criteria for an authenticated seller. 
  
  Execution Errors:
  | Code                  |  Message                                                                     |
  |-----------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | BAD_INPUT_VALUE       |  Input value is not correct.                                                 |
  | INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR |  System failure.                                                             |
  """
  sellerItemCommitments(input: ItemCommitmentsInput!): PaginatedItemCommitments! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.commitment.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.commitment"])
}

"""
This enumeration type contains the sort values that may be used when configuring sorting for a **sellerItemCommitments** or a **buyerItemCommitments** query.
"""
enum ItemCommitmentsSortField {
  """
  If this value is used, item commitments are sorted according to creation date.
  """
  CREATED_AT
  """
  If this value is used, item commitments are sorted according to the last time they were updated.
  """
  UPDATED_AT
}

"""
This type is used to control how item commitments are sorted in the query response. 
"""
input ItemCommitmentsSortInput {
  """
  The enumeration value here controls whether item commitments are sorted according to creation date or last update action. The supported values are:
  - CREATED_AT
  - UPDATED_AT
  **Default**: CREATED_AT
  """
  sortField: ItemCommitmentsSortField!
  """
  The enumeration value here controls whether item commitments are sorted in descending (most recent first) or ascending order. The supported values are:
  - DESC
  - ASC
  **Default**: DESC
  """
  sortOrder: SortOrder!
}

"""
This union type is used to express the different states of item commitments.
"""
union ItemCommitmentState = ItemCommitmentAbandoned | ItemCommitmentActive | ItemCommitmentCancelled | ItemCommitmentCompleted | ItemCommitmentLocked

"""
This type is used to shows total sales price of the eBay item associated with the item commitment, including any deposit for a motor vehicle. These monetary values will be shown in multiple currencies if the buyer or seller use a different currency than the default currency of the eBay marketplace.
"""
type ItemCommitmentTotals {
  """
  The total sales price for the item. Multiple values/currencies will be shown if the buyer or seller use a different currency than the default currency of the eBay marketplace.
  """
  committedTotal: AmountSet!
  """
  This  container will show the amount of any deposit that the buyer is required to make as part of a motor vehicle down payment. Multiple values/currencies will be shown if the buyer or seller use a different currency than the default currency of the eBay marketplace.
  """
  deposit: AmountSet
}

"""
A list of parts compatibility information specified as name and value pairs. Describes an assembly with which a part is compatible (i.e., compatibility by application)
"""
type ItemCompatibility {
  """
  A name-value pair describing a single compatible application. The allowed names and values are specific to the primary category in which the item is listed. For example, when listing in a Parts & Accessories category, where the applications are vehicles, the allowed names might include Year, Make, and Model, and the values would correspond to specific vehicles in eBay's catalog.
  """
  compatibilities: [NameValuesPair]
  """
  The seller may optionally enter any notes pertaining to the parts compatibility being specified. For example, if this Compatibility information applies to a vehicle, a seller may use this field to specify the placement of the part on a vehicle or the type of vehicle a part fits.
  """
  compatibilityNotes: String
}

"""
This type defines the fields that describe a specific item condition within a category.
"""
type ItemCondition {
  """
  This field returns information about the category associated with the item condition. 
  """
  category: Category!
  """
  This array returns the condition descriptors applicable to the specified item condition. 
  **Note:** This array is only returned for categories that support condition descriptors.
  """
  descriptors: [ConditionDescriptor!]!
  """
  The display name for the item condition. 
  **Note**: This name is localized for the specified marketplace by default. The **Accept-Language** header can be used to provide a translation to a different language from the marketplace default language.
  """
  displayName: String!
  """The unique identifier of the item condition."""
  itemConditionId: ID!
  """
  The short display name for the item condition. This field can be returned as null if no short name is available.
  **Note**: This text is localized for the specified marketplace by default. The **Accept-Language** header can be used to provide a translation to a different language from the marketplace default language.
  """
  shortDisplayName: String
  """
  This field is used to provide additional details about a non-new item's physical state, including any defects, wear, or other characteristics that affect its condition.
  This field can be used for all categories except those that require the **conditionDescriptors** array.
  """
  conditionDescription: String
  """
  This array is used to provide more item condition information through name-value pairs about
  single graded and ungraded trading cards in the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*,
  *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader**
  and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards,
  such as 'Near mint or better'.
    
  If there are no condition descriptors, this array will be empty.
    
  This field will be null if there is an error. You can find more details in the errors section of the response.
  """
  conditionDescriptors: [ListingConditionDescriptor!]
}

"""Indicates the geographical location of the item"""
type ItemLocation {
  """
  The two-letter country code, as defined in the ISO-3166 standard, must be specified in this field to
  indicate the country where the item is located. Please keep in mind that the item is often located in
  the same country as the listing marketplace, but this is not a requirement.
    
  This field will be null if there was an error. You can find more details in the errors section of the response
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The field indicates the geographic location (city, state, or province) where the listing is physically located.
    
  This field will be empty if a postal code is provided
    
  This will be null if there was an error. You can find more details in the errors section of the response
  """
  location: String
  """
  The postal code (ZIP code) where the listing is physically located.  This may be empty if location is provided instead.
  Either the postal code or location will be available.
    
  This will be null if there was an error
    
  The postal/zip code format varies by region.
  US: 5-digit numeric codes (e.g., 12345).
  Australia: 4-digit numeric codes (e.g., 2000).
  UK: Variable-length alphanumeric codes with letters and numbers (e.g., SW1A 1AA).
    
  Other regions follow local postal service standards.
  """
  postalCode: String
}

"""
This type indicates the item is being returned to the seller after the authentication partner deemed that the item was miscategorized. Displays as **Item miscategorized**.
"""
type ItemMiscategorized implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `ITEM_MISCATEGORIZED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type is used to define an item’s negotiations in the user-scoped view.
  - `item` is the negotiated item
  - `negotiations` are ordered by most-recent activity in descending order
"""
type ItemNegotiation {
  """This container returns details about the item being negotiated."""
  item: Item!
  """
  This container specifies the list of negotiation threads for the item. Each negotiation exposes the latest offer per thread. Negotiations are ordered by most-recent activity in descending order.
  """
  negotiations: [Negotiation!]!
}

"""
This type defines the business rule error that occurs when offers are not enabled for this item.
"""
type ItemNotEligibleForOffer implements OfferBusinessRuleViolation {
  """
  The description of the business rule failure.
  **Maximum length**: 250 characters
  """
  ruleDescription: String!
}

"""
This type indicates the item is returned because the buyer did not pick up the item. Displays as **Item not picked up**.
"""
type ItemNotPickedUp implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `ITEM_NOT_PICKED_UP`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type represents an 'Item Not Received' (INR) inquiry. The fields in this type capture the full inquiry lifecycle — from initiation through buyer and seller interactions, shipment tracking events, participants, refund processing, and final resolution. This type implements the OrderInquiry interface and specializes it for the INR Inquiry.
"""
type ItemNotReceivedInquiry implements OrderInquiry {
  """
  This array returns a list of the post-purchase cases associated with this INR inquiry.
  **Note**: This array is only returned when the inquiry has been referred to eBay.
  """
  cases: [PostPurchaseCase!] @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.resolution.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.resolution.read"])
  """
  The timestamp when the INR inquiry was closed.
  **Note**: This container will be returned null if the inquiry is still open.
  """
  closedAt: DateTime
  """The timestamp when the INR inquiry was created."""
  createdAt: DateTime!
  """The actor who originally initiated the INR inquiry (e.g., buyer)."""
  initiator: PostPurchaseActorRole!
  """
  This array returns a list of all actors who have inquired about the same subject within this inquiry — starting with the original initiator, and including any other parties (e.g., buyer, seller, participant, or system) who later engaged. For example, the system might initiate the inquiry after handling time + 1 business day to prompt a seller response, and the buyer might inquire later on EDD + 1 day. Both actors would be listed here as having inquired about the same issue.
  **Note:** This field is required and will always contain at least one actor.
  """
  inquirers: [PostPurchaseActorRole!]!
  """The unique identifier of the INR inquiry."""
  inquiryId: ID!
  """
  This array returns a list of line items associated with this INR inquiry. 
  **Note:** This list is guaranteed to be non-null but may be empty in certain valid cases. In most typical cases, it will contain at least one line item.
  """
  lineItems: [OrderInquiryLineItem!]!
  """
  This array returns a list of information or evidence provided by inquiry participants in response to system or CS requests. This includes user-submitted files, text notes, or structured responses.
  **Note:** This array may be an empty list if no additional information was provided.
  """
  providedInformation: [OrderInquiryInformation!]!
  """
  This array returns a list of refunds associated with the INR inquiry.
  **Note**: This array will only be present if there are refunds associated with the inquiry.
  """
  refunds: [Refund!] @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.refund.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.refund.read"])
  """
  This array returns a list of information or evidence requests made during the inquiry lifecycle. These requests may be generated by the system or manually initiated by participants and are typically used to collect supporting documentation or clarifications from one or more involved parties (e.g., buyer or seller). Examples include requests for tracking details, signature confirmation, proof of delivery or other relevant evidence.
  **Note**: This list may be empty if no additional information was requested.
  """
  requestedInformation: [OrderInquiryInformationRequested!]
  """
  The user or party expected to respond to the INR inquiry (e.g., seller or eBay agent).
  """
  responder: PostPurchaseActorRole!
  """
  A list of actions currently available to the seller for this INR inquiry. This container may be returned null if:
  - The viewer is not a participant.
  - No actions are currently available based on the inquiry state and role.
  - The inquiry is in a terminal state (e.g., 'CLOSED' or 'RESOLVED').
  """
  sellerAvailableActions: OrderInquiryActions @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.inquiry.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.inquiry&eBayUser"])
  """
  The current overall status of the INR inquiry (e.g., 'OPEN', 'CLOSED').
  """
  status: OrderInquiryStatus!
  """
  The refund estimation for the inquiry entity. If **refundEstimate** is not requested on an order, this will not be calculated and provided.
  """
  refundEstimate: RefundEstimate
}

"""
This type defines the fields that detail and summarize offer negotiation information specific to an item. Each item may have one or more negotiation threads, and each negotiation consists of multiple offers exchanged between participants. This entity provides both a summary and detailed history of those negotiations and includes information such as the total number of offers across all negotiations and the last accepted offer amount for the item.
"""
type ItemOfferOverview {
  """
  This field specifies the total number of unique negotiations for this item.
  **Note**: This count is computed at the item level and is not affected by the role of the querying user (buyer or seller).
  """
  negotiationCount: Int!
  """
  The complete history of all negotiation threads and associated offer details. For sellers, this response includes a list of negotiations for which the user has the 'SELLER' role. For buyers, this response includes a list of negotiations for which the user has the 'BUYER' role. Results are ordered in descending order from newest to oldest and support pagination. To retrieve specific subsets of negotiation history, use `NegotiationHistoryFilters`.
  """
  negotiationHistory(filters: NegotiationHistoryFilters): NegotiationHistoryResult! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.offer&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.offer.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.offer&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.offer.read&eBayUser"])
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Item Price."""
type ItemPrice implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'ITEM_PRICE'.
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type represents the constraints defined for item price refund withhold input.
"""
type ItemPriceRefundWithholdConstraint {
  """This object provides the allowed percentage range."""
  allowedPercentageRange: InputPercentageRange!
}

"""
This type represents input violations related to item price refund withholding. This indicates that the seller attempted to withhold the item price refund exceeding the allowed percentage range.
"""
type ItemPriceRefundWithholdViolation implements ProcessReturnRefundInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific rule that was violated (for example, `ITEM_PRICE_REFUND_WITHHOLD_VIOLATION`).
  """
  code: String!
  """
  Indicates the constraints defined for item price refund withhold input.
  """
  constraint: ItemPriceRefundWithholdConstraint!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the rule violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This type is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or an eBay product ID (ePID) for a product. It is also used to provide the unique traits of a variation within a multiple-SKU listing.
"""
type ItemSellerProduct {
  """
  This container is used to display a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or an eBay product ID (ePID) for a product. If an eBay catalog product is found that maps to a GTIN or an ePID, product details of that eBay catalog product will be used to populate the listing. The product details in a catalog product include product title, product description, aspects, eBay leaf category, and stock photo.
  """
  productIdentifiers: ListingProductIdentifiers
  """
  This array of name-value pairs identify a variation's unique combination of trait values. For example, if a particular variation was the 'Red, Large' version of the product, 'Color' would be one of the name values with its corresponding value value being 'Red', and the other name value would be 'Size' with it corresponding value value being 'Large'.
  """
  traits: [NameValuePair!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide the seller-defined or store SKU (Stock-Keeping Unit) of a purchasable item.
"""
type ItemSku {
  """The seller-defined SKU (Stock-Keeping Unit) of a purchasable item."""
  sellerSku: String
  """The store-defined SKU (Stock-Keeping Unit) of a purchasable item."""
  storeSku: String
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Item Tax."""
type ItemTax implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'ITEM_TAX'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type is used to display quantity and pricing information for a purchasable item. All SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing must have their own quantity and price values. All SKUs may have the same price, but prices also may vary by SKU. This type is also used to provide an eco-participation fee if applicable for the item.
"""
type ItemTerms {
  """
  This container displays the available quantity for a purchasable item.
  **Note**: This will only be null if an error has occurred.
  """
  availability: ListingItemAvailability
  """
  This container displays an eco-participation fee for an item. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
  """
  extendedProducerResponsibility: ExtendedProducerResponsibility
  """
  This container displays price data for the item, including the price for a fixed price item or the *Buy it Now* price for an auction item. Other price fields include auction starting bid price, auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
  **Note**: Each item within a multiple-SKU listing can have its own price, allowing for different pricing based on traits (e.g., larger sizes might cost more than smaller ones).
  **Note**: This will only be null if an error has occurred. Please see the errors array for more details
  """
  pricingTerms: ListingItemPricingTerms
}

"""This type provides details of the partial refund term for negotiation."""
type KeepItemPartialRefundTerm {
  """
  The percentage of the item's price to refund (1–99). This optional field is only present when the partial offer is specified as a percentage of the item price.
  """
  itemPriceRefundPercentage: Int
  """
  This indicates whether the original outbound shipping charge is waived for this item as part of the offer. This optional field is only present when the partial offer includes waiving the shipping charge.
  """
  itemShippingPriceWaived: Boolean
  """The total refund amount computed based on the proposed term."""
  refundAmount: AmountSet!
  """The return line item to which these terms apply."""
  returnLineItem: ReturnLineItem!
}

"""
This type defines the terms for a partial-refund on a specific return line item in a keep-item offer.
"""
input KeepItemPartialRefundTermInput {
  """
  The percentage of the item's price to refund (1–99). For example, if `20`, this means refund the seller to refund 20% of the item price if the buyer accepts and keeps the item.
  """
  itemPriceRefundPercentage: Int!
  """
  If 'true', the original outbound shipping charge for this item as part of the offer is waived; if `false`, it is not waived.
  """
  itemShippingPriceWaived: Boolean! = false
  """
  The unique identifier of the return line item ID to which these terms apply.
  """
  returnLineItemId: ID!
}

"""This type is used to identify KlarnaInstallment as the payment method."""
type KlarnaInstallment implements PaymentMethodType {
  """The unique identifier of the KlarnaInstallment payment method."""
  code: ID!
  """The descriptive name of the KlarnaInstallment payment method."""
  descriptiveName: String!
  """The display name of the KlarnaInstallment payment method."""
