"""
This type is used to express name-value pairs for entities that have one name and one value. An example of an array that uses this type is the traits array which define the unique traits of SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing.
"""
type NameValuePair {
  """The name of the entity, such as an aspect name."""
  name: String!
  """The value of the entity, such as an aspect value."""
  value: String!
}

"""
This type is used to express name-value pairs for entities that have one name and one value. An example of an array that uses this type is the **traits** array which define the unique traits of SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input NameValuePairInput {
  """The name of the entity, such as an aspect name."""
  name: String!
  """The value of the entity, such as an aspect value."""
  value: String!
}

"""Pair type of name and values"""
type NameValuesPair {
  """name of this type."""
  name: String
  """values of this type."""
  values: [String!]
}

"""
This type is used to express name-value pairs for entities that have one name and one or more values. An example of an array that uses this type are product aspects. Some product aspects can only have one value, but some can support multiple values, which is why this type uses an array for **values**.
"""
input NameValuesPairInput {
  """The name of the entity, such as an aspect name."""
  name: String!
  """
  This array may have one or more values that correspond to the entity defined in the **name** field.
  """
  values: [String!]!
}

"""
This type indicates that the buyer needs the item to be shipped instead of picked up. Applicable only for local pickup orders.
"""
type NeedItemToBeShippedCancellation implements ContractCancellationReason {
  """
  The unique cancellation reason code for this use case. For this type, the value is `NEED_ITEM_TO_BE_SHIPPED`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the cancellation reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This action type is used by a seller to offer a partial refund to buyer with the buyer keeping the item.
"""
type NegotiateOnReturnAction implements ReturnAction {
  """A machine-readable return action code: `NEGOTIATE_ON_RETURN`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable offer for a partial return action. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type represents the complete negotiation conversation between participants. Each negotiation contains the full, chronological sequence of offers and counter-offers exchanged between buyer and seller.
"""
type Negotiation {
  """A convenience accessor for the most recent offer (always non-null)."""
  latestOffer: NegotiationOfferDetails!
  """The unique identifier for this negotiation conversation."""
  negotiationId: ID!
  """
  The capability flags that define the rules and allowed actions for this negotiation. These are fixed at creation and determine aspects such as whether counter-offers are allowed (`negotiable`) and whether the negotiation involves multiple items (`multiItem`).
  **Examples**:
  - `[negotiable]`: Allows counter-offers on a single item.
  - `[multiItem, negotiable]`: Allows counter-offers on a grouped bundle of items.
  """
  offerCapabilities: [NegotiationOfferCapabilities!]!
  """
  The list of all offers exchanged in this negotiation, ordered chronologically from oldest to newest. This field shows the full progression of the negotiation over time.
  """
  offers: [NegotiationOfferDetails!]!
  """
  The object being negotiated (e.g., a single item or a bundle of items).
  """
  target: OfferTarget!
}

"""
This enumerated type defines the negotiation creator role filter for querying negotiation history. This type is used to filter negotiations based on the role of the participant who initiated them.
"""
enum NegotiationCreatorRoleFilter {
  """
  This enumeration value indicates the negotiation creator role filter includes all supported negotiations regardless of who initiated them. This enum can be used to return all available negotiations.
  """
  ALL
  """
  This enum value indicates the negotiation creator role filter includes only buyer-initiated negotiations (Best Offers). This enum can be used to return negotiations where a buyer made the first offer to a seller.
  """
  BUYER
  """
  This enum value indicates the negotiation creator role filter includes only seller-initiated negotiations. This enum can be used to return negotiations where a seller made the first offer to a buyer.
  **Note**: This negotiation type is not currently supported.
  """
  SELLER
}

"""
This type defines the filters for retrieving negotiation history.
**Defaults when omitted:**
  - Time window: last **90 days** by most-recent activity
  - Recent negotiation status: **ACTIONABLE**
  - Initiator: **BUYER**
"""
input NegotiationHistoryFilters {
  """
  This field can be used to return negotiations whose most-recent activity is **on/after** this timestamp. If both `activeAfter` and `activeBefore` are omitted, negotiation history from the last 90 days is returned by default.
  """
  activeAfter: DateTime
  """
  This field can be used to return negotiations whose most-recent activity is **on/before** this timestamp. If both `activeAfter` and `activeBefore` are omitted, negotiation history from the last 90 days is returned by default.
  """
  activeBefore: DateTime
  """
  This field can be used to filter negotiations by who initiated them. This field can be used to control which negotiations are returned based on the role of the participant who started the negotiation:
  - **`BUYER`**: Only buyer-initiated negotiations (Best Offers)
  - **`SELLER`**: Only seller-initiated negotiations (**not currently supported**)
  - **`ALL`**: All supported negotiations regardless of who initiated them
  **Default**: `BUYER`
  """
  negotiationCreatorRole: NegotiationCreatorRoleFilter = BUYER
  """
  This field can be used to set the pagination parameters for retrieving offer history.
  **Min value**: 1
  **Max value**: 200
  **Default**: 100
  """
  pagination: PageInfoInput
  """
  This field can be used to filter negotiations by their current status.
  **Default**: 'ACTIONABLE'
  """
  statusFilter: NegotiationStatusFilter = ACTIONABLE
}

"""
This type defines the paginated result containing the full negotiation history for a specific item. This includes:
- A list of negotiation threads associated with the item.
- The offers exchanged within each negotiation.
- Pagination metadata for navigating through the result set.
"""
type NegotiationHistoryResult {
  """
  A list of negotiation threads for the item. Each negotiation includes the complete set of offers exchanged within that thread, ordered with the most recent negotiation first.
  """
  negotiations: [Negotiation!]
  """
  The pagination metadata for navigating through the negotiation history.
  """
  pagination: Pagination!
}

"""
This type defines the capability flags for a negotiation. These flags describe what actions are allowed during the negotiation and help determine the negotiation's type. They influence both backend logic and frontend behavior.
**Examples**:
- Whether counter-offers are permitted.
- Whether the negotiation involves a single item or a bundled group of items.
"""
type NegotiationOfferCapabilities {
  """
  This boolean indicates whether counter-offers are allowed in the negotiation. If 'true', counter-offers are allowed; if 'false', counter-offers are not allowed.
  """
  negotiable: Boolean!
}

"""
This type represents a single offer made by a user within a negotiation thread. Each offer captures the complete context of one step in a negotiation, including pricing, quantity, lifecycle status, timestamps, and user-entered notes. This type includes references to the negotiation it belongs to and the user who submitted it.
"""
type NegotiationOfferDetails {
  """
  The date and time the offer was created, in UTC. This field uses the `DateTime` scalar (ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 format).
  """
  createdAt: DateTime!
  """
  The date and time when this offer will automatically expire. This field uses the `DateTime` scalar (ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 format).
  """
  expiresAt: DateTime
  """
  An optional message from the offer creator, visible only to participants in this negotiation. This note is scoped to this specific offer step and can be used to justify or explain the offer.
  **Format**: UTF-8
  **Maximum Length**: 250 characters
  """
  message: String
  """
  The role of the participant who submitted this offer (e.g., 'BUYER' or 'SELLER').
  """
  offerCreatorRole: NegotiationParticipantRole!
  """The user who submitted this offer."""
  offerCreatorUser: User!
  """The unique identifier for this specific offer step in the negotiation."""
  offerId: ID!
  """The price proposed by the offer creator in this step."""
  offerPrice: ConvertedAmount!
  """
  The quantity of items included in this offer.
  **Unit**: integer
  **Valid range**: greater than '1' and less than the listing’s available quantity.
  """
  quantity: Int!
  """
  The current status of the offer in its lifecycle.
  **Possible values**:
  - PENDING
  - COUNTERED
  - ACCEPTED
  - AUTO_ACCEPTED
  - SELLER_ACCEPTED
  - PAYMENT_PENDING
  - DECLINED
  - AUTO_DECLINED
  - EXPIRED
  - RETRACTED
  - ADMIN_ENDED
  """
  status: OfferStatus!
  """
  The date and time the offer was last updated, in UTC. This field uses the `DateTime` scalar (ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 format).
  """
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

"""
This enumerated type defines the role of a participant in a negotiation. Each role can initiate offers and respond to offers from the other party.
"""
enum NegotiationParticipantRole {
  """
  This enum value indicates that an interested buyer submitted the offer or counteroffer.
  """
  BUYER
  """
  This enum value indicates that the seller of the item submitted the offer or counteroffer.
  """
  SELLER
}

"""
This enumerated type specifies logical groupings of offer statuses used for filtering negotiation queries. Each value represents a broad lifecycle category, allowing developers to filter negotiation threads based on their current state.
"""
enum NegotiationStatusFilter {
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations whose latest offer was accepted will be returned. This enum includes offer statuses: 'ACCEPTED', 'AUTO_ACCEPTED'
  """
  ACCEPTED
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations that require your action will be returned. Use this to fetch negotiations where **you** must respond:
  - **Sellers**: Any buyer offers (initial or counter-offers) awaiting your decision.
  - **Buyers**: Seller counter-offers awaiting accept/decline/counter.
  This enum includes negotiations whose latest offer status is `PENDING` and awaiting your response. For sellers this includes buyer offers and counteroffers. For buyers, this includes seller counteroffers.
  """
  ACTIONABLE
  """
  This enum value indicates that all negotiations, regardless of status, will be returned.
  """
  ALL
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations in any terminal state will be returned. This enum includes offer statuses: 'ACCEPTED', 'AUTO_ACCEPTED', 'DECLINED', 'AUTO_DECLINED', 'EXPIRED', 'RETRACTED', 'ADMIN_ENDED'
  """
  COMPLETED
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations whose latest offer was declined will be returned. This enum includes offer statuses: 'DECLINED', 'AUTO_DECLINED'
  """
  DECLINED
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations whose latest offer expired will be returned. This enum includes offer status: 'EXPIRED'
  """
  EXPIRED
  """
  This enum value indicates that only negotiations waiting on the other party will be returned. This enum includes negotiations whose latest offer status is `PENDING` and awaiting the other party’s action. For sellers, this includes seller counteroffers. For buyers, this includes buyer offers and buyer counteroffers.
  """
  PENDING
}

"""
This type indicates the item is returned because the buyer no longer needs the item. Displays as **No longer need item**.
"""
type NoLongerNeedItem implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `NO_LONGER_NEED_ITEM`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""Represents a non-profit organization."""
type NonProfitOrganization {
  """Unique identifier of the non-profit organization."""
  id: ID!
}

"""
This type indicates that the buyer has not received a refund for return shipping.
"""
type NoRefundForReturnShipping implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `NO_REFUND_FOR_RETURN_SHIPPING`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable case referral reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates the item is returned because it was not as described. Displays as **Item not as described**.
"""
type NotAsDescribed implements ReturnReason {
  """A machine-readable reason code: `NOT_AS_DESCRIBED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type defines the business error that occurs during business rule violations while executing an offer action.
"""
type OfferBusinessRulesViolated implements BusinessError {
  """
  The globally unique error code for this business error type. In this case, 'OFFER_BUSINESS_RULES_VIOLATED'.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  The developer-friendly message explaining the error.
  **Maximum length**: 500 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  A list of business rule violations that caused the offer action to fail.
  """
  violations: [OfferBusinessRuleViolation!]!
}

"""
The interface representing a business rule violation. This identifies the rule that failed to execute along with an explanatory message.
"""
interface OfferBusinessRuleViolation {
  """
  The description of the business rule failure.
  **Maximum length**: 250 characters
  """
  ruleDescription: String!
}

"""
This type defines the business rule error that occurs when the buyer has been blocked by the seller.
"""
type OfferBuyerBlockedBySeller implements OfferBusinessRuleViolation {
  """
  The description of the business rule failure.
  **Maximum length**: 250 characters
  """
  ruleDescription: String!
}

"""
This type defines the business rule error that occurs when the buyer has been blocked due to low feedback.
"""
