}

"""
This type provides details about the payment method used to process a refund.
"""
type RefundPaymentMethod {
  """Represents the type of payment method used to process the refund"""
  paymentType: PaymentMethodType!
}

"""
This type defines the error returned when the refund cannot be processed. Please try again or contact us for help.
"""
type RefundProcessingError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The error code associated with the error. 
  **Note:** In this case, this field will return 'RFND_PROCESSING_ERROR'.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  The human-readable error message for the refund error. 
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters 
  **Format**: Alphanumeric
  """
  errorMessage: String!
}

"""This type specifies that the refund is in 'SCHEDULED' status."""
type RefundScheduled implements RefundStatus {
  """
  The machine-readable status code specifying the status of the refund.
  **Note**: In this case, the status code will always be returned as 'SCHEDULED'. 
  """
  code: String!
  """The human-readable text detailing the status of the refund."""
  displayText: String!
}

"""This interface defines the status of a refund."""
interface RefundStatus {
  """The machine-readable status code specifying the status of the refund."""
  code: String!
  """The human-readable text detailing the status of the refund."""
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This enumerated type indicates the seller's return resolution options, either a refund only, or a refund or a replacement.
"""
enum RefundType {
  """The seller provides refunds only when the buyer returns the product."""
  MONEY_BACK
  """
  The seller may provide either a refund or a replacement item when the buyer returns the product. The availability of a replacement item may depend on item stock and policy.
  """
  MONEY_BACK_OR_REPLACEMENT
}

"""
This interface represents any withholding applied on the refund contract. These withholding can happen from any party who is funding the refund and can reduce the refund/charge amount.
"""
interface RefundWithholding {
  """The monetary amount being withheld from the gross refund amount."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """The name of the withholding."""
  name: String!
}

"""
This type is used to display marketplace-specific product compliance policies. Each marketplace may have up to six product compliance policies.
"""
type RegionalProductCompliancePolicies {
  """Contains a country and the custom policy/policies for that country."""
  countryPolicies: [CountryPolicy!]
}

"""
The list of unique identifiers indicating the seller-created take-back policies that will be used for a listing. The law in some countries may require sellers to take back a used product when the buyer buys a new product. Each listing may include one (1) country-specific take-back policy for each of the following countries:GB, DE, FR, IT, ES. Maximum 5 policies in a listing
"""
type RegionalTakeBackPolicies {
  """Contains a country and the take back policy/policies for that country."""
  countryPolicies: [CountryPolicy!]
}

"""
This type is used to show the regulatory documents that are attached to the listing. These documents provide various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
"""
type RegulatoryDocument {
  """
  This field specifies the document ID of the regulatory document that is associated with the listing.
  ID is non-nullable field and is required if regulatory document is provided for the listing.
  """
  id: ID
}

"""
This type is used to show various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
"""
type RegulatoryInfo {
  """
  This container is used specify regulatory document ids information for the listing.
  """
  documents: [RegulatoryDocument!]
  """
  This container provides information about the energy efficiency for certain durable goods.
  """
  energyEfficiencyLabel: EnergyEfficiencyLabel
  """
  This container is used by the seller to provide hazardous material information for the listing.
  """
  hazardousMaterial: HazardousMaterial
  """The contact details for the European manufacturer of a product."""
  manufacturer: Manufacturer
  """
  This container is used by the seller to provide product safety information for the listing.
  """
  productSafety: ProductSafety
  """
  This field represents the repair index for the listing.The repair index identifies the manufacturer's repair score for a product (how easy is it to repair the product). This field is a floating point value between 0 and 10
  """
  repairIndexScore: Decimal
  """
  The contact details for the Responsible Person along with Person Type, for the a product.
  """
  responsiblePersons: [ResponsiblePerson!]
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Regulatory Tax Fee."""
type RegulatoryTaxFee implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'TAX_FEE'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify auction-specific pricing settings for auction listings.
"""
input RelistListingAuctionPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to set the lowest price at which the seller is willing to sell an auction listing. A small fee is charged to use this feature. If the **reservePrice** field value is not met or surpassed during bidding, the auction will end without a winning bidder. This price must be higher than the **startingBidPrice**. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: The **reservePrice** value for an ended auction listing may retain that value. Regardless if the **reservePrice** value is retained or not, it is a good idea for the seller to evaluate the price and make an update if desired.
  """
  reservePrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is mandatory for auction listings and sets the starting bid amount. The first bid must meet or exceed this value or it will be rejected. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: The **startingBidPrice** value for an ended auction listing should retain that value. Regardless if the **startingBidPrice** value is retained or not, it is a good idea for the seller to evaluate the price and make an update if desired.
  """
  startingBidPrice: Decimal
}

"""
This type is used to make changes to **Best Offer** settings, including enabling or disabling the Best Offer feature, or to add, modify, or remove the auto-accept and auto-reject thresholds.
"""
input RelistListingBestOfferTermsInput {
  """
  Include this field to set, modify, or remove the auto-accept threshold price. Best Offers will be automatically accepted by the seller if they meet or exceed the price. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-accept feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to 'true'.
  **Note**: To remove the auto-accept threshold price if one is set up for the listing, included this field and use an empty or null value.
  """
  autoAcceptThreshold: Decimal
  """
  Include this field to set, modify, or remove the auto-decline threshold price. Best Offers will be automatically declined by the seller if the price is at or below this value. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-decline feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to 'true'.
  **Note**: To remove the auto-decline threshold price if one is set up for the listing, included this field and use an empty or null value.
  """
  autoDeclineThreshold: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable the Best Offer feature for a fixed-price or auction listing. If set to 'true', the Best Offer feature is enabled, allowing potential buyers to make offers on the item. If set to 'false' the Best Offer feature is disabled.
  **Note** For auction listings, the Buy It Now and Best Offer features cannot be used simultaneously.
  **Note** If Best Offer is enabled for an auction listing, it is automatically disabled as soon as the listing receives a qualifying bid, and any pending offers or counteroffers are invalidated.
  """
  bestOfferEnabled: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the street address for a business entity such as the product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input RelistListingBusinessEntityAddressInput {
  """
  This field adds or modifies the first line of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine1: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the second line of the entity's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the city of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  city: String
  """
  The two letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation of the country of the entity's address.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  This field adds or modifies the postal code of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 9 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the state or province of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  stateOrProvince: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the product manufacturer or responsible person. At least one of the three fields in this type must be specified for a product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input RelistListingBusinessEntityContactInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify the entity's URL for their online Contact Us/Support page.
  **Max length**: 250 characters.
  """
  contactUrl: HttpOrHttpsUrl
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the entity's email address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  email: String
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the entity's phone number.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  phone: String
}

"""
This type is used to disable or enable a seller's account-level buyer restrictions and/or set or modify a quantity limit per buyer threshold for a multiple-quantity, fixed price listing.
"""
input RelistListingBuyerRestrictionsInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to disable all buyer restrictions (that are set in the seller's account) for the listing, or set to 'false' if the seller wishes to have all account-level buyer restrictions to apply to the listing.
  """
  disableBuyerRestrictions: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the maximum quantity of items that a single buyer may purchase during the duration of a fixed price listing (single or multiple-variation). The buyer is blocked from the purchase if that buyer is attempting to purchase a quantity of items that will exceed this value. Previous purchases made by the buyer are taken into account. For example, if **quantityLimitPerBuyer** is set to '5' for a listing, and *Buyer1* purchases a quantity of three in a previous sale, *Buyer1* is only allowed to purchase an additional quantity of two in subsequent orders on the same listing.
  """
  quantityLimitPerBuyer: Int
}

"""
This type is used if the seller wishes to make the listing a charitable listing, or if a charity is already set up, it is used to change the charitable organization and/or the donation percentage per sale.
"""
input RelistListingCharityInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the non-profit organization that will benefit from the sale of the item. The [Charity API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/charity/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve the numeric identifiers for the charities and to find out more about the organization.
  """
  charityOrganizationId: ID
  """
  This field sets the percentage of the purchase price that the seller chooses to donate to the selected non-profit organization for each sale generated by the listing. An integer value is used here with supported values ranging from 10 to 100. Within this range, only increments of 5 can be used, so 15, 20, 25, etc.
  **Min value**: 10
  **Max value**: 100
  """
  donationPercentage: Int
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify one or more country-specific product compliance or takeback policies. Up to 6 product compliance policies may be set per country, but only 1 takeback policy may be set per country.
"""
input RelistListingCountryPolicyInput {
  """
  The two-letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation for a country that hosts an eBay marketplace, a marketplace to which the corresponding policy or policies apply. The supported values are `GB`, `DE`, `FR`, `IT`, and `ES`.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code!
  """
  This array is used to set or modify one or more country-specific product compliance policy ID values or one takeback policy ID value that will apply to the corresponding country. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all policies defined for a seller's account.
  **Note**: All country-specific product policies that the seller would like to apply to the corresponding country in the listing must be included in this array, and not just the new policies being added. There can only be one takeback policy per country, so there will only be just one takeback policy ID in this array.
  """
  policyIds: [ID!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify global or country-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies for a listing.
"""
input RelistListingCustomPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the global product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. The product compliance policies set with this array will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies should be set with the **regionalProductCompliancePolicies** container instead.
  **Max number of product compliance policies allowed per listing**: 6.
  **Max length of each product compliance policy ID**: 15 characters.
  """
  productCompliancePolicyIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used add or modify the country-specific product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies may be needed where countries might have special legal/regulatory requirements. For example, if you sell batteries in a country requiring disclosures that apply only to that country, a country-specific product compliance policy could contain this information. If country-specific policies are not needed, use the **productCompliancePolicyIds** array instead.
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per marketplace**: 6 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per listing**: 30 (6 per country).
  """
  regionalProductCompliancePolicies: RelistListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify one or more country-specific takeback policies that will be used for a listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The law in some countries may require sellers to take back a used product when the buyer buys a new product but wishes to dispose of it. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy. If a country-specific takeback policy is not needed, one global takeback policy is set with the **takebackPolicyId** field.
  **Maximum number of takeback policies allowed per marketplace**: 1 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of takeback policies allowed per listing**: 5 (1 per country).
  """
  regionalTakebackPolicies: RelistListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput
  """
  This field is used to add, change, or remove the global takeback policy to use for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The takeback policy set with this field will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Country-specific policies should be set with **regionalTakebackPolicies** container instead.
  **Note**: To remove a global takeback policy, include this field and set its value as empty or null.
  **Max length of takeback policy ID**: 15 characters.
  """
  takebackPolicyId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify Energy Efficiency Label related information for such categories as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Note that these three category types will also need Rating and Range product aspects. See the [Energy efficiency information](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/static/inventory/energy-efficiency.html) topic for more information.
"""
input RelistListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify a brief text-based summary of the information included on the Energy Efficiency Label for a product. The description should be concise and informative, providing key details about the energy efficiency of the product. If this field is provided, the **imageUrl** must also be provided.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the text in the current image description if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 280 characters
  """
  imageDescription: String
  """
  This field is used to specify the URL to the Energy Efficiency Label image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  imageUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including energy efficiency labels.")
  """
  The URL to the Product Information Sheet image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  productInformationSheetUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including product information sheets.")
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify an eco-participation fee for item(s) in a listing. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
"""
input RelistListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput {
  """
  This is the fee paid for new items to the eco-organization (for example, *eco-organisme* in France). It is a contribution to the financing of the disposal of the item responsibly. In a multiple-SKU listing, this fee should be specified at the variation level and not in this field. The [getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports, requires, or recommends eco-participation fees at the listing or variation level.
  """
  ecoParticipationFee: Decimal!
}

"""
This type is used to modify details on how the item will be delivered to the buyer. The data in this container includes available shipping services, ship-to and excluded shipping locations, shipping costs, package details, and more.
"""
input RelistListingFulfillmentTermsInput {
  """
  This field should be included if the seller wishes to enable or disable digital delivery of an item. A digital delivery item is an item that can be downloaded via a link or delivered to the buyer via email. The  [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports digital delivery.
  """
  digitalDeliverySupported: Boolean
  """
  This field can be included if the seller wishes to enable or disable eBay's Global Shipping Program (GSP) to ship items internationally. With GSP, the seller ships the item to eBay's shipping partner, and that shipping partner handles all logistics of the international shipping leg. GSP is only available for listings on the eBay GB (EBAY_GB) marketplace. eBay US (EBAY_US) has a similar program called eBay International Shipping, but there is currently no boolean field associated with this feature.
  """
  globalShippingSupported: Boolean
  """
  This container is used to add or modify information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions. Package weight is required when calculated shipping is used, and shipping services generally have dimension and weight restrictions.
  """
  packageSpecifications: RelistListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput
  """
  This container is used to modify information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
  """
  shippingTerms: RelistListingShippingTermsInput
}

"""
This type is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for the item. GTIN is a globally unique identifier for trade items used by companies to identify products. GTINs include UPCs, EANs, and ISBNs. Optionally, eBay will search for a catalog product against a provided GTIN if the **includeEbayProductDetails** field is included and set to 'true'. If a matching eBay catalog product is found, the listing will automatically pick up product details of that catalog product, including product title, product description, product aspects, and stock photo(s).
"""
input RelistListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  This field is used to supply a European Article Number (EAN) for a product. It is a 13-digit barcode standard used internationally for retail product identification. Also known as International Article Number. Some leaf categories may require an EAN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this EAN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  **Max length**: 13 characters.
  """
  ean: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply an International Standard Book Number (ISBN) for a product. It is a unique identifier for books and book-like products. Can be 10 digits (older format) or 13 digits (current format). Some leaf categories may require an ISBN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this ISBN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  **Max length**: 13 characters.
  """
  isbn: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply a Universal Product Code (UPC) for a product. It is a 12-digit barcode standard used primarily in North America for retail product identification. Some leaf categories may require a UPC, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this UPC, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to 'true'.
  **Max length**: 12 characters.
  """
  upc: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
"""
input RelistListingHazardousMaterialInput {
  """
  This field is used by the seller to add or modify component information for the listing. For example, component information can provide the specific material of Hazmat concern.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current additional info text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 120 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to four pictogram codes that represent the possible hazard(s) that a product poses. The pictograms that are stated on the product's Safety Data Sheet should be used. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the codes that can be passed into this array. The pictogram(s) that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Note**: All pictogram codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the hazardous material signal word for the product. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the strings that can be passed into this array.
  **Max length**: 15 characters.
  """
  signalWordCode: ID
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to eight hazardous statement codes that are applicable to the product. These codes map to actual hazardous statement text. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the statement codes that can be passed into this array. The hazardous statements that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Note**: All statement codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max no of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]
}

"""
The base request type for the **relistListing** mutation. This container is used to provide product details, eBay listing terms, and price and quantity information for each item that will be available for sale in the new listing. This **relistListing** mutation is used to relist a recently ended listing, and the seller has the option to relist with all of the same data and settings, or the seller can also choose to make updates. For multiple-SKU listings, the **listingVariations** container will be used to add or modify variation information for a multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input RelistListingInput {
  """
  This field allows the user to set up a client-side idempotency key, and having this key defined will help in avoiding duplicate listings due to a retry if a mutation fails due to a system problem.
  **Note**: The **idempotencyKey** value, if set for the ended listing, will not carry over to the relisted listing, so this field must be included with a new value if the user wishes to make use of it.
  **Max length**: 32 characters.
  """
  idempotencyKey: IdempotencyKey
  """
  This container is used to identify the listing to be relisted. The listing can either be identified with the **listingId** or the SKU value if defined in the ended listing.
  """
  listingIdentifier: ListingIdentifierInput!
  """
  An array of one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing.
  **Note**: A SKU value is optional for a single-SKU listing, but mandatory for a multiple-SKU listing.
  **Note**: Price(s), Global Trade Item Numbers (GTINs), and the eBay Product ID (ePID) defined in the ended listing will be carried over in the relisted listing unless the seller desires to make updates. The quantity should be checked and updated as needed though.
  **Max number of items for a multiple-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  listingItems: RelistListingItemsInput
  """
  This container is used to provide listing terms details for the listing, including listing format, listing duration, payment terms, return policy, fulfillment terms, and more.
  **Note**: A majority of the listing terms defined in the ended listing will be carried over in the relisted listing unless the seller desires to make updates.
  """
  listingTerms: RelistListingTermsInput
  """
  This container provides details on the available product variations within a multiple-SKU listing, and which traits are different for each of these variations. Products in a multiple-SKU listing tend to vary by one or more traits such as color and size, and interested buyers need to select which variation they want to purchase. For example, the 'Blue, Large' t-shirt.
  **Note**: A majority of the variation information defined in the ended listing will be carried over in the relisted multiple-SKU listing unless the seller desires to make updates.
  """
  listingVariations: RelistListingVariationsInput
  """
  This field is used to identify the eBay marketplace where the listing will be created. Generally, an ended listing will be relisted on the same eBay marketplace. See [`ListingMarketplace`] for list of supported enumeration values. It determines the regional settings, currency, and other marketplace-specific configurations.
  """
  marketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
  This container allows a user to run a **relistListing** mutation in validation mode, which means that the listing object will be validated, but a successful mutation will not relist a listing. 
  """
  options: ListingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify product data for the listing. Product data under this container includes title, description, product aspects, item condition, images, and more.
  **Note**: A majority of the product data defined in the ended listing will be carried over in the relisted listing unless the seller desires to make updates.
  """
  product: RelistListingProductInput
}

"""
This type is used to update the available quantity for a purchaseable item.
"""
input RelistListingItemAvailabilityInput {
  """
  The quantity available for an item. For auction listings, this value must always be 1, and it should still be 1 if the item in the ended auction listing didn't sell. For a multiple-SKU listing, each item variation can have its own quantity value, allowing sellers to manage inventory for each variation independently.
  **Note**: For a multiple-SKU listing, the quantity for an item variation can be se set to 0 if the SKU is temporarily out of stock, but a seller wishes to retain the variation and restock inventory at a later time.
  **Note**: It depends on how a listing was ended, but it is possible that any given purchasable item may still have quantity defined, but it is highly recommended that a seller revisits their inventory and makes sure that the quantity value is accurate.
  """
  quantityAvailable: Int!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input RelistListingItemCompatibilitiesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or update the list of compatible vehicles or assemblies through a set of name-value pairs such as *Year*, *Make*, and *Model*. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Note**: The specified compatibility list of the ended listing will be retained, but this array will be needed if the seller wants to make any changes.
  **Max number of allowed compatibilities on the listing**: 3000
  """
  itemCompatibilities: [RelistListingItemCompatibilityInput!]
  """
  This field indicates if the entire compatibility list is to be deleted. If `true`, all existing compatibilities will be removed from the listing's compatibility list. If `false` or omitted, the compatibilities specified in the `itemCompatibilities` will be added or updated in the listing's compatibility list.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  replaceAll: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input RelistListingItemCompatibilityInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the list of compatible vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts and Accessory item. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to the compatibility list, the full set of compatibility name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the compatibilities that are being added or modified.
  **Max number of allowed compatibilities on the listing**: 3000
  **Max compatibility name length**: 65
  **Max compatibility value length**: 65
  """
  compatibilities: [NameValuesPairInput!]!
  """
  The seller can use this field to add or modify compatibility notes pertaining to the parts compatibility being specified. For example, if this compatibility information applies to a vehicle, a seller may use this field to specify the placement of the part on a vehicle or the type of vehicle a part fits.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current compatibility notes text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 500 characters.
  """
  compatibilityNotes: String
  """
  This field indicates if the compatibility is to be deleted. If `true`, the compatibility specified by the `compatibilities` will be removed from the listing's compatibility list. If `false` or omitted, the compatibility specified by the `compatibilities` will be added or updated in the listing's compatibility list.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  removeCompatibilityFromListing: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify condition descriptor data (through name-value pairs) for a single graded and ungraded trading card listing in one of the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
"""
input RelistListingItemConditionDescriptorInput {
  """
  This field can be used to add or modify additional information about a condition descriptor. One example is using this field to specify the **Certification Number** for a graded card.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current additional information text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 30 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This field is used to add or change the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor that maps to the condition descriptor name. The IDs for condition descriptor names can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Condition descriptor names for graded cards include **Grader** and **Grade** (both required) and **Certification Number** (optional), and condition descriptor names for ungraded cards include **Card Condition**.
  """
  name: ID
  """
  This array is used to add or change the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor value that maps to an actual value supported by the condition descriptor. For example, graded cards require **Grader** and **Grade** as condition descriptor names, so the value(s) in this array will show the organization that graded the card and the card's actual grade, which ranges from 1 to 10. The numeric IDs for condition descriptor values can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Locate the Condition descriptor name first in the response, and then look for the corresponding values in the **conditionDescriptorValues** array of that response.
  """
  values: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to change the condition of the item, to add or modify the condition description for a used item, or to make any changes to the condition descriptor data for a single trading cards listing.
"""
input RelistListingItemConditionInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify additional details about a non-new item's physical state, including any defects, wear, or other characteristics that affect its condition. This field can be used for all categories except those that require the **conditionDescriptors** array.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current condition description if one exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 1000 characters.
  """
  conditionDescription: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify item condition information (through name-value pairs) for a single graded and ungraded trading card listed in the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to condition descriptor data, the full set of condition descriptor name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the condition descriptor data that is being added or modified.
  """
  conditionDescriptors: [RelistListingItemConditionDescriptorInput!]
  """
  This field is used to change the item's condition using the numeric identifier for a condition. Supported conditions and the text used to describe the conditions vary by marketplace and leaf category. Use the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method to get the supported condition IDs and their descriptions for leaf categories.
  **Note**: The **conditionId** value will be retained from the original listing, so this field will generally not be needed unless the seller decides that a less appropriate item condition was being used previously.
  """
  conditionId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to modify a specific purchasable item within a listing, allowing you to create, update, or remove them. It includes a unique combination of identifying characteristics such as global identifiers, listing terms, availability, price, and regulatory information requirements. Every listing contains at least one item, providing a unified approach that works transparently across simple single-SKU listings and complex multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input RelistListingItemInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the pricing information, available quantity, and eco-participation fee (if applicable) for a purchasable item. Each item should have price and quantity.
  """
  itemTerms: RelistListingItemTermsInput
  """
  For either a single-SKU or a multiple-SKU listing, this container can be used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will prefill the relisted listing. For a multiple-SKU listing, the **traits** array is required and identifies the unique traits of the variation within that multiple-SKU listing. Common unique traits within a multiple-SKU listing are 'Color' and 'Size'. For example, a 'Blue, Large' shirt. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values.
  """
  product: RelistListingItemProductInput
  """
  The field indicates whether to delete this variation. If set to true, the variation is removed from the listing. Note that this is only applicable for multiple-SKU listings; for single-SKU listings, the field value is ignored if included.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  removeItemFromListing: Boolean
  """
  The seller-defined Stock-Keeping Unit (SKU) that uniquely identifies a purchasable item in the listing. When updating a SKU-managed listing, the behavior of this field is conditional. For single-SKU listings, this field is ignored, as the listing is already identified by its SKU. For multiple-SKU listings, you must provide a variation's existing SKU to identify it for modification (e.g. changing its price). To add a new variation, you must assign it a new SKU, and this value must be unique for each variation in the listing.
  **Note**: For relist operations, the presence of a SKU in the item container will cause the listing to be treated as a multiple-SKU (MSKU) listing.
  **Max length**: 50 characters.
  """
  sku: String
}

"""
This type is used to provide the item's physical location. Item location is required for every listing. The **country** field is always required, and either the **postalCode** or **location** must also be provided, but not necessarily both.
"""
input RelistListingItemLocationInput {
  """
  The two-letter country code, as defined in the ISO-3166 standard, must be specified in this field to indicate the country where the item is located. Please keep in mind that the item is often located in the same country as the listing marketplace, but this is not a requirement.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The field indicates the geographic location (city and state/province) where the listing is physically located. If you do not provide a value in this field, you must provide a value in the **postalCode** field and the field value will be derived from the postal code.
  For the CLASSIFIED_AD format for Motor vehicles, the value provided in the field is used as item location only if the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2** fields of the **UpdateListingSellerContactInput** are not provided. If the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2** fields of the **UpdateListingSellerContactInput** are provided, the item location field value is ignored.
  **Max length**: 200 characters.
  """
  location: String
  """
  The postal code (zip code) where the listing is physically located. Either the **location** field or the **postalCode** field must be specified or an error will occur. Postal/zip code format varies by region. e.g. US: 5-digit numeric codes (e.g., 12345), Australia: 4-digit numeric codes (e.g., 2000), GB: Variable-length alphanumeric codes with letters and numbers (e.g., SW1A 1AA). Other regions follow local postal service standards.
  **Max length**: 32 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify price data for an item in a listing, including the price for a fixed price listing or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. Other price fields include auction starting bid price, auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
"""
input RelistListingItemPricingTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify auction-specific price settings including starting bid price and reserve price.
  """
  auctionPrice: RelistListingAuctionPriceInput
  """
  This field sets or modifies the price of a fixed price item or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. This field is mandatory for fixed price listings. The 'Buy it Now' option is disabled for an auction listing as soon as that listing has a qualifying bid. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: The **fixedPrice** values for all items in an ended fixed price listing should retain those values. The 'Buy it Now' price for an auction item may also be retained if the auction listing ended without bids. Regardless if the price values from the last listing have been retained or not, it is a good idea for the seller to evaluate the price(s) and make any necessary updates.
  **Note**: For relist operations when listing format is not provided, the mapping behavior depends on the presence of auction price container. If only `fixedPrice` is provided (no `auctionPrice` container), it will be treated as a fixed price listing. If `fixedPrice` is provided along with `auctionPrice` container, it will be treated as an auction listing.
  """
  fixedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This container is used to add or modify pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
  """
  marketingPrice: RelistListingMarketingPriceInput
}

"""
This type can be used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will prefill the relisted listing.
"""
input RelistListingItemProductInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or an eBay product ID (ePID) for a product. If an eBay catalog product is found that maps to a GTIN or an ePID, product details of that eBay catalog product will be used to populate the listing. The product details in a catalog product include product title, product description, aspects, eBay leaf category, and stock photo.
  **Note**: If an eBay catalog product is found and used to prefill a relisted listing, any other product-related details defined in the ended listed and/or provided by the seller may be dropped.
  """
  productIdentifiers: RelistListingProductIdentifiersInput
  """
  This array is mandatory for multiple-SKU listings and is used to provide the traits that make each item unique in context of the multiple-SKU listing. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values, and the trait names and trait values specified here must be defined as available trait names and trait values in the **variationDetails** container. An error will be thrown if the specified traits do not match the variation traits defined in the **variationDetails** container.
  **Note**: The trait names and values must match the marketplace's language and locale.
  **Max allowed traits**: 5.
  **Max length for trait names and values**: 65 characters.
  """
  traits: [NameValuePairInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to modify an array of one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing.
"""
input RelistListingItemsInput {
  """
  This array is used to manage the list of items or variations in the listing, allowing you to create, update, or remove them. For a single-SKU listing, this array must contain exactly one item. For a multiple-SKU listing, it must contain one item for each product variation (e.g., one for "Red / Large", one for "Blue / Small").
  **Maximum number of items for a multiple-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  items: [RelistListingItemInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to provide quantity and pricing information for a purchasable item. All SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing must have their own quantity and price values. All SKUs may have the same price, but prices also may vary by SKU. This container is also used to provided an eco-participation fee if applicable for the item.
"""
input RelistListingItemTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to provide the available quantity for a purchasable item. Quantity is mandatory for all purchasable items.
  **Note**: It depends on how a listing was ended, but it is possible that any given purchasable item may still have quantity defined, but it is highly recommended that a seller revisits their inventory and makes sure that the quantity value is accurate.
  """
  availability: RelistListingItemAvailabilityInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify an eco-participation fee for an item. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
  """
  extendedProducerResponsibility: RelistListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput
  """
  This container is used to provide price data for the item, including the price for a fixed price item or the *Buy it Now* price for an auction item. Other price fields include auction starting bid price, auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
  **Note**: Each item within a multiple-SKU listing can have its own price, allowing for different pricing based on traits (e.g., larger sizes might cost more than smaller ones).
  **Note**: Price settings will generally carry over from the ended listing, but it is highly recommended that the price data is rechecked and that any necessary adjustments are made.
  """
  pricingTerms: RelistListingItemPricingTermsInput
}

"""
This type is used to change the duration of the listing, and can also be used to set the future date when a relisted listing will become active.
"""
input RelistListingLifecycleTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to change the duration of the listing that is to be relisted. All fixed price listings must be set to `GTC`(Good 'til Cancelled), but the listing duration days of auction and ad listings may vary based on marketplace and category. The [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see supported durations for each leaf category.
  """
  listingDurationInDays: ListingDurationInDays
  """
  This field is used if the user wishes to publish the relisted listing at a future date and not right after a successful mutation. The timestamp specified in this field must be a future date. For more information on eBay scheduled listings, see the [Listing durations and timings](https://www.ebay.com/help/selling/listings/creating-managing-listings/selecting-listing-duration?id=4652) help topic.
  """
  scheduledToStartAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the radius for a local listing, making it available to buyers within that specified area. The seller's supplied **postalCode** or **location** field value will be used as the center point for this radius.
"""
input RelistListingLocalDistanceInput {
  """
  The numeric value for the radius. The unit of measurement for this value is specified in the **distanceUnit** field. This value defines the radius of the area around the seller's location where the listing will be visible to local buyers. The user can call the [getMotorsListingPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** to get supported distances. Look for the [localListingDistances](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies#response.motorsListingPolicies.localListingDistances) array in the response.
  """
  distance: Int!
  """
  The unit of measurement used for the **distance**. Currently, the only supported value is `MILES`.
  """
  distanceUnit: DistanceUnit
}

"""
This type is used to add a product manufacturer contact or to update any of the data currently associated with the product manufacturer that is already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
"""
input RelistListingManufacturerInput {
  """
  This container adds or modifies the street address for the product manufacturer.
  """
  address: RelistListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field adds or modifies the name of the company that manufactured the product. This field is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the product manufacturer. At least one of the three is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  """
  contact: RelistListingBusinessEntityContactInput
}

"""
This type adds or modifies pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
"""
input RelistListingMarketingPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the price that will be displayed as the **Made for Outlet** comparison price for a listing, and can only be used if the listing will be displayed on an eBay Outlet page. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  madeForOutletComparisonPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the Minimum Advertised Price (MAP) for a listing. MAP is an agreement between suppliers (or manufacturers (OEM)) and the retailers (sellers) stipulating the lowest price a listing is allowed to be advertised at. Sellers can offer prices below MAP by means of other discounts. This only applies to fixed price listings and auction listings with the 'Buy It Now' option. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Minimum Advertised Price feature, and controls whether the discounted price is shown to buyers prior to checkout by the buyer clicking on a link on the View Item page, or the discounted price is shown just prior to checkout when the buyer has clicked the Buy button. See [`ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPriceExposure: ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure
  """
  This 'originalRetailPrice' price must be provided if a qualified seller is using the Strikethrough Price feature. The 'originalRetailPrice' price is the actual retail price set by the manufacturer (OEM). The price specified in this field should always be more than the price specified in the **fixedPrice** field. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  originalRetailPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOnEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  """
  soldOffEbay: Boolean
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOffEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  """
  soldOnEbay: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
"""
input RelistListingMotorVehicleDepositInput {
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the due date (in days) for the buyer to pay off the full balance of the motor vehicle. The clock starts on the full payment due date as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The supported values here are `DAYS_3` `DAYS_7`, `DAYS_10`, and `DAYS_14`.
  """
  daysToMakeFullPayment: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This field sets or modifies the deposit amount to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. This field is required if the seller is requiring a deposit. This deposit must be made immediately by the buyer if **immediatePay** is set to 'true', or within 24, 48, or 72 hours (set with **hoursToDeposit** field) if **immediatePay** is set to 'false'.
  **Max value**: 2000 USD (non-immediate pay), 500 USD (immediate pay)
  """
  depositAmount: Decimal
  """
  This boolean field is included and set to 'true' if the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle.
  **Note**: If a motor vehicle deposit is currently required for the motor vehicle listing, but the seller wants to disable, the field can be included and set to 'false'.
  """
  depositRequired: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to set the deadline (in hours) for the motor vehicle deposit. The deposit amount is specified in the **depositAmount** field. The clock starts on the deposit deadline as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The three supported integer values here are 24, 48, and 72 (hours). If **immediatePay** is 'true', and the listing qualifies for immediate payment (e.g. the 'Buy It Now' button is used), this field will not be applicable, since the buyer will be required to pay any deposit amount immediately (and not within 24, 48, and 72 hours).
  """
  hoursToDeposit: Int
}

"""
This type is needed for motor vehicle listings to provide the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
"""
input RelistListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change the Vehicle Identifier Number (VIN) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  **Max length**: 17 characters.
  """
  vin: ID
  """
  This field is used to add or change the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  """
  vrm: ID
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **relistListing** mutation. Three possible results of a **relistListing** mutation are: a listing container (and possibly one or more warnings); a listing container with validation success (listingId = 0) and possibly one or more warnings; or an array of blocking errors if the mutation fails and a listing is not relisted. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error, and there may also be one or more warning messages that are triggered.
"""
union RelistListingOutput = RelistListingSuccess | RelistListingValidationError | RelistListingValidationSuccess

"""
This type is used to override the shipping costs for one or more domestic or international shipping service options defined in the fulfillment business policy being used for the listing. The shipping costs provided will only affect the listing and will not update the fulfillment business policy.
"""
input RelistListingOverrideShippingOptionInput {
  """
  This field is used to override the additional unit shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost when a buyer is purchasing multiple quantities of the same line item. Note that this value should never be higher than the base shipping cost.
  **Note**: If the additional shipping cost of the corresponding shipping service was already overriding the cost set up in the fulfillment business policy, the dollar value supplied here will replace that value.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to specify if the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field is a shipping service. The value of this field should be set to 'false' if the shipping service is a domestic shipping service, and 'true' if it is an international shipping service.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  internationalShippingOption: Boolean = false
  """
  The integer value specified here identifies the shipping service in the fulfillment business policy whose cost value(s) will be overridden. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 if overriding a shipping service option that ships within the marketplace or from 5 to 9 if overriding a shipping service option that ships outside of the marketplace. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page.
  """
  rank: Int!
  """
  This field is used to override the shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost for the line item.
  **Note**: If the shipping cost of the corresponding shipping service was already overriding the cost set up in the fulfillment business policy, the dollar value supplied here will replace that value.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the dimensions of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. When specifying the dimensions of the shipping package, all three values (length, width, and height) are required. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
"""
input RelistListingPackageDimensionsInput {
  """
  The height (or depth) of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  height: Float
  """
  The length of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  length: Float
  """
  The width of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  width: Float
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the weight of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is pounds for **majorUnit** and ounces for **minorUnit**. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is kilograms for **majorUnit** and grams for **minorUnit**.
"""
input RelistListingPackageWeightInput {
  """
  The major weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The major weight value is the whole number part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is pounds. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is kilograms.
  **Note**: If the package weighs less than one pound or one kilogram, *0* can be used as the value for this field.
  """
  majorUnit: Int
  """
  The minor weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The minor weight value is the decimal part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is ounces. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is grams.
  **Minimum value**: 0
  **Maximum value**: 15 for English measurement system (ounces); 999 for Metric measurement system (grams).
  """
  minorUnit: Int
}

"""
This type is used to modify various payment terms and information for the listing, including immediate payment requirement, offline payment methods, and motor vehicle deposit information. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a payment business policy with the listing.
"""
input RelistListingPaymentTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change a payment business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all payment settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getPaymentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/payment_policy/methods/getPaymentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all payment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
  This field is included to enable or disable the immediate payment requirement for fixed price listings and auction listings where the 'Buy it Now' option is used.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  immediatePay: Boolean
  """
  This container is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  motorVehicleDeposit: RelistListingMotorVehicleDepositInput
  """
  This field is used if the seller wants to add or modify instructions related to payment.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite existing payment instructions if defined in the listing.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  **Max length**: 500 characters.
  """
  paymentInstructions: String
  """
  This array is used to modify the list of offline payment methods for listings that support offline transactions. Use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see the payment methods supported for a leaf category.
  **Note**: The full list of payment methods must be included in the array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  paymentMethods: [ListingPaymentMethod!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the primary eBay category for the listing, and optionally, add or modify a secondary eBay category and/or eBay store categories.
"""
input RelistListingProductCategoriesInput {
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to change the eBay primary category of the listing. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  **Note**: If the eBay primary category is being changed, it is recommended that the user check to see if the optional, recommended, and required aspects are different for that new category and to make adjustments as needed.
  """
  primaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to add or change the eBay secondary category of the listing. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  **Note**: The secondary category must be different from the primary category.
  """
  secondaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to change the eBay store primary category of the listing. If this field was not specified during the original creation of the listing, the listing is placed in the default *Other* category of the seller's eBay store. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storePrimaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to add or change the eBay store secondary of the listing. This field is optional, but if specified, it must be a valid eBay store category ID. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storeSecondaryCategoryId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to match to and leverage the product details of a product defined in eBay's product catalog. The user can directly provide the identifier of the eBay catalog product, or they can provide a GTIN value that can possibly be matched to an eBay catalog product. When an eBay catalog product is used, the product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that product will be used in the relisted listing.
"""
input RelistListingProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of an eBay catalog product. If this field is provided, the title, description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that eBay product will be used in the resultant listing, overriding the seller provided information and/or the information defined in the ended listing. The [search](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/catalog/resources/product_summary/methods/search) method of the **Catalog API** can be used to search for eBay catalog products and get their IDs.
  """
  ebayProductId: ID
  """
  This container is used to specify a UPC, EAN, or ISBN value for a product, and optionally, try to match the value to an eBay catalog product so that the product details of that catalog product can be prefilled in the resultant listing. Some leaf categories require a GTIN, and the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category requires a UPC, EAN, or ISBN.
  """
  globalIdentifiers: RelistListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput
  """
  This field controls whether or not an eBay catalog product is leveraged to prefill a listing with that catalog product's details, including product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo. If you want to use an eBay catalog product to populate your listing, you can either set this field to true or omit it entirely, as true is the default value. If you provide a GTIN (Global Trade Item Number) or eBay Product ID but do not want to use the corresponding eBay catalog product to prefill your listing, you must set this field to false. If set to false, you will be required to provide your own listing title, description, category, and at least one image. This is only applicable to single-SKU listings.
  **Default value**: true
  """
  includeEbayProductDetails: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify common product details for the listing, including title, description, listing category, condition, product aspects, images, and more.
"""
input RelistListingProductInput {
  """
  This array is used to set or modify name-value pairs that define the product aspects. Most leaf categories require at least a few aspects, and the listing will fail if these are not provided. The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method can be used to see which aspects are required, recommended, or optional for a leaf category. This method also returns typical values for an aspect name and will indicate if an aspect name supports multiple values or just one value. For a multiple-SKU listing, only the common aspects will be specified in this array, and the pivoting aspects (aka traits) will be specified at the item level.
  **Note**: The specified aspects of the ended listing will be retained, but this array will be needed if the seller wants to make any changes. Changes most likely will be necessary if the primary eBay category is being changed.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to product aspects, the full set of aspect name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the aspects that are being added or modified.
  **Max length**: 65 characters for each aspect name and value.
  """
  aspects: [NameValuesPairInput]
  """
  This container is used to change the primary eBay category for the listing, and optionally, to add or modify a secondary eBay category and/or eBay store categories.
  **Note**: The specified categories of the ended listing will be retained, but this container can be used in case the seller wants to change or add new categories.
  """
  categories: RelistListingProductCategoriesInput
  """
  This field is used to modify the full description of the product or group of products. HTML markup and inline CSS can be used. However, a seller can not use any active content in their listing description. Active content includes animation or video via JavaScript, Flash, plug-ins, or form actions. All active content will be blocked/removed from a listing. Sellers are only allowed to provide links to product videos, freight shipping services, or other legally required information, and when providing these links in the listing description, the secure 'https' protocol must be used instead of 'http'. In addition, any valid links to sites outside of eBay should use the target="_blank" attribute in the a href tag so a new browser window will be loaded when the link is clicked instead of buyers being redirected off of eBay.
  **Note**: The **description** of the ended listing will be retained, so this field will only need to be included if the seller wishes to modify the description.
  **Max length**: 500,000 characters (including all markup tags/CSS)
  """
  description: String
  """
  This array is used to update the list of image URLs that will become photos in the listing's photo gallery. Most eBay categories support up to 24 photos per listing at no extra charge. The URLs used in this array must use 'https'. Either all eBay Picture Services (EPS) or all self-hosted picture URLs may be used in this array, but not a combination of both.
  **Note**: The list of images of the ended listing will be retained, but this array will be needed if the seller wants to add or remove any images.
  **Note**: The full set of image URLs that you wish to be images in the listing must be included, and not just the images that are being added.
  **Max images allowed on a listing**: 24
  """
  imageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]
  """
  This container is used to change the condition of the item, to add or modify the condition description for a used item, or to make any changes to the condition descriptor data for a single trading cards listing.
  **Note**: All condition information of the ended listing will be retained, but this container will be needed if the seller wants to make any changes.
  """
  itemCondition: RelistListingItemConditionInput
  """
  This container is used to add or update the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles. Year, Make, and Model are typical aspects used to identify a motor vehicle.
  **Note**: The specified compatibility list of the ended listing will be retained, but this container will be needed if the seller wants to make any changes.
  **Max compatibilities allowed on a listing**: 3000
  """
  listingCompatibilities: RelistListingItemCompatibilitiesInput
  """
  This container is needed for motor vehicle listings and is used to add or change the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
  """
  motorVehicleIdentifier: RelistListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput
  """
  This field is used to modify the product title displayed on the listing. The **title** of the ended listing will be retained, so this field will only need to be included if the seller wishes to modify the title.
  **Max length**: 80 characters.
  """
  title: String
  """
  This array is used to add, replace, or remove a seller's video to the listing. A unique identifier for a seller's video is passed into this array to add a product video to the listing. Although a video can be added to a listing before it is in the `LIVE` state, the video won't be available for viewing in the listing until it does reach this state. To know more about the video upload process and various states for a video, see the [Media API documentation](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/media/overview).
  **Note**: Currently, only one video may be added to each listing.
  **Note**: If set, the video attached to the ended listing will be retained, but this array will be needed if the seller wants to change or remove the video. If a video is already associated with a listing, but a new video ID is passed into this field, that video will replace the current one. To remove the current video and not add a new one, include this array as empty and the current video will be removed.
  **Max videos allowed on a listing**: 1
  """
  videoIds: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify product safety information for an item, including product safety statements and pictograms. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
"""
input RelistListingProductSafetyInput {
  """
  This free-form text field is used to add or modify additional product safety information that goes beyond what is expressed through the pictogram(s) and/or safety statements.
  **Note**: This field cannot be used without the **pictogramCodes** and/or **statementCodes** arrays.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current additional info text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 120 characters
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to four product safety pictogram codes, and if successful, the pictogram(s) associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes, and this method will also return the URLs to the pictograms so that these pictograms can be previewed before adding them to a listing.
  **Note**: All pictogram codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to eight product safety statement codes, and if successful, the safety statements associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes and the safety statements associated with them.
  **Note**: All statement codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to attach one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
"""
input RelistListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
  **Note**: All country-specific product compliance policies that the seller wants to be attached to the listing should be included in this array, and not just any new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of product compliance policies allowed per marketplace**: 6.
  """
  countryPolicies: [RelistListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or change country-specific takeback policies. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy.
"""
input RelistListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to specify a country-specific takeback policy. Each country may only have one country-specific takeback policy.
  **Note**: All country-specific takeback policies that the seller would like to apply to the listing must be included in this array, and not just the new policies being added.
  **Max number of takeback policies allowed per marketplace**: 1.
  """
  countryPolicies: [RelistListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
"""
input RelistListingRegulatoryInput {
  """
  This array is used to attach one or more documents to the listing using their unique identifiers. The **Media API** is used to upload documents to a seller's account. See the [DocumentTypeEnum](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/media/types/api:DocumentTypeEnum) type of the **Media API** for the full list of supported document types.
  **Note**: The document ID values for all documents that the seller would like to attach to the updated listing must be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of document IDs allowed**: 10.
  **Max length of each document ID**: 50 characters.
  """
  documentIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used to add or modify Energy Efficiency Label related information for such category types as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend Energy Efficiency Label information.
  """
  energyEfficiencyLabel: RelistListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
  """
  hazardousMaterial: RelistListingHazardousMaterialInput
  """
  This container is used to add a product manufacturer contact or to update any of the data currently associated with the product manufacturer that is already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
  """
  manufacturer: RelistListingManufacturerInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify product safety related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
  """
  productSafety: RelistListingProductSafetyInput
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the manufacturer's repair index score for a product. This value should be between 0.1 (extremely difficult to fix) to 10 (extremely easy to fix). A maximum of one digit to the right of the decimal point may be used. 0 or 0.0 should never be used as values as this would indicate that the product is not repairable.
  **Min value**: 0.1
  **Max value**: 10.0
  """
  repairIndexScore: Float
  """
  This array is used to add one or more responsible person contacts or to update any of the data currently associated with one or more of the responsible person entities that are already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide either the product manufacturer or responsible person(s) contact information in their eBay listings. This array is only necessary if the product manufacturer contact is not based in an EU country.
  **Note**: If the listing already has one or more responsible persons defined, all current data must be included in the array, even the data that is not changing.
  **Max number of EU responsible persons allowed**: 5.
  """
  responsiblePersons: [RelistListingResponsiblePersonInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to add one or more responsible person contacts or to update any of the data currently associated with one or more of the responsible person entities that are already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide either the product manufacturer or responsible person(s) contact information in their eBay listings.
"""
input RelistListingResponsiblePersonInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify a street address for a responsible person.
  """
  address: RelistListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the company name associated with the responsible person.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String!
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the responsible person. At least one of the three is required if a responsible person is supplied.
  """
  contact: RelistListingBusinessEntityContactInput
  """
  This array is required for each responsible person specified, and the only allowed value is `EU_RESPONSIBLE_PERSON`.
  **Max number of person types allowed**: 1.
  """
  personTypes: [String!]!
}

"""
This container is used to add or modify a domestic return policy or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
"""
input RelistListingReturnTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change a return business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all return policy settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/return_policy/methods/getReturnPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all return business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
  This container is used to modify the seller's domestic return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
  **Note**: If the listing only has a domestic return policy set up, but the item is shipped internationally, the settings in this container will also apply to international returns.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  domesticReturnTerms: RelistListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the seller's international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  internationalReturnTerms: RelistListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This free-form text field is used to add or modify details about a seller's return policy. Currently, this field is only supported on the EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT, EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, and EBAY_ES marketplaces.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite existing return instructions if defined in the listing.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  **Max length**: 8000 (for EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT); 5000 (for EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, EBAY_ES).
  """
  returnInstructions: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the seller's domestic or international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
"""
input RelistListingReturnTermsOptionsInput {
  """
  This field specifies the refund method that will be used if the buyer returns the item. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item. Currently, the only supported value for this field is `MONEY_BACK`.
  **Note**: Although `MONEY_BACK_OR_REPLACEMENT` is defined in the schema, replacement items are not currently supported in Returns flow, so `MONEY_BACK` is the only option.
  """
  refundMethod: ListingRefundMethod
  """
  This field is used to indicate whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item. This field set to 'true' if the seller accepts returns for the item or 'false' if the seller does not accept returns for the item.
  """
  returnAccepted: Boolean
  """
  This field specifies the amount of time the buyer has to return an item. The return duration begins when the item is marked 'delivered' at the buyer's specified ship-to location. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and sets the number of days that a buyer has to return the item for a full refund. Supported values are `DAYS_14`, `DAYS_30`, and `DAYS_60`. The supported return periods can vary by category (with `DAYS_14` limited to just a few categories), and the [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getReturnPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** can be used to see the supported return periods for a category.
  """
  returnDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This option specifies either the buyer or the seller as the party who pays for return shipping charges. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and specifies the person responsible for return shipping costs if the item is returned due to a buyer remorse. See [`Invoicee`] for the list of supported enumeration values. The seller is always responsible for return shipping costs when an item is being returned due to a Significantly not as described (SNAD) issue.
  """
  returnShipmentInvoicee: Invoicee
}

"""
This type is used to specify the days and times when a seller may be contacted regarding a classified ad listing. This container is used by the **primarySellerContactHours** and **secondarySellerContactHours** containers and the days specified here should not overlap between the two.
"""
input RelistListingSellerContactHoursInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller is available the full 24 hours on the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. If this field is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  anyTime: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to indicate the end time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursEndAt** value should always be later than the **supportHoursStartAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursEndAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to indicate the start time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursStartAt** value should always be earlier than the **supportHoursEndAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursStartAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to specify the block of days that the support hours will apply to. See [`ListingDaysCode`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  supportOnDays: ListingDaysCode
}

"""
This type is used for classified ad listings, and provides contact information for the seller, including days and hours when the seller accepts inquiries from potential buyers.
"""
input RelistListingSellerContactInput {
  """The first line of the street address of the seller."""
  addressLine1: String
  """
  The second line of the seller's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the company name (if any) associated with the seller.
  """
  companyName: String @deprecated(reason: "Company name is no longer supported")
  """
  This field is used to indicate whether potential buyers can contact the seller via email. A value of 'true' in this field indicates that potential buyers can contact the seller of the listing via email.
  """
  contactByEmailEnabled: Boolean
  """
  Two-letter [ISO 3166 Country Codes](https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html) to indicate which country the seller is located.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """The county where the seller resides."""
  county: String
  """The seller's phone number."""
  phone: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the seller's primary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekdays. This container should always be provided to let potential buyers know when the seller may be contacted.
  """
  primarySellerContactHours: RelistListingSellerContactHoursInput
  """
  This container is used to provide the seller's secondary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekends if the support hours vary on weekends.
  """
  secondarySellerContactHours: RelistListingSellerContactHoursInput
}

"""
This type is used to modify information on domestic and international shipping, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated) and the shipping service options available to ship the item. There is also a field to add or change a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
"""
input RelistListingShippingOptionsInput {
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  **Note**: To remove the existing combined shipping rule, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  combinedShippingRuleId: ID
  """
  This field is used to change the shipping cost type for locations within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping. Note that all of the specified shipping services should support the shipping cost type specified here.
  **Note**: To specify local pick only option for listings, set this field to `NOT_SPECIFIED`.
  """
  costType: ListingShippingType
  """
  This field is included to add, modify, or remove a flat-rate handling cost for shipping. This cost is in addition to whatever the final shipping cost is based on the buyer's location and selected shipping service option.
  **Note**: To remove the existing package handling cost, include this field and set value to '0.0'.
  """
  packageHandlingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable a seller's promotional shipping discount for the listing. A seller can only have one promotional shipping discount active on a marketplace. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the details of the promotional shipping discount, and the [SetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/SetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to add/modify the promotional shipping discount.
  """
  promotionalShipping: Boolean
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping rate table, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  rateTableId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use shippingRateTableId instead")
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping discount profile, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  shippingDiscountRuleId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use combinedShippingRuleId instead")
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping rate table, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  shippingRateTableId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions.
"""
input RelistListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput {
  """
  This field should be included if the seller wants to mark the shipping package as irregular size or if the seller wishes to undo this setting. A shipping carrier may charge additional handling fees for an irregular package.
  """
  irregularPackage: Boolean
  """
  The measurement system used by the marketplace for the package dimensions and weight. If the value is not supplied, the default measurement system for the marketplace will be used. See [`MeasurementSystem`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  measurementSystem: MeasurementSystem
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the dimensions of the shipping package.
  """
  packageDimensions: RelistListingPackageDimensionsInput
  """
  This field is used to change the type of package used to ship the item. See [`ListingPackageType`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  packageType: ListingPackageType
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the weight of the shipping package. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type.
  """
  packageWeight: RelistListingPackageWeightInput
}

"""
This type is used to modify the list of domestic or international shipping service options that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
"""
input RelistListingShippingServiceInput {
  """
  This field adds or modifies the flat-rate shipping cost to ship each additional unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for multiple-quantity, fixed price listings using flat-rate shipping. The cost specified in this field must be the same or lower than the cost specified in the **shippingCost** field, with the idea being that multiple quantities of the line item might be shipped in the same shipping package, decreasing the per-unit cost for shipping.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the list of geographical regions or individual countries that the corresponding international shipping service operates in.
  **Note**: The full list of shipping locations must be included if any changes are being made, and not just the ones that are being added.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  The integer value specified here controls the order in which the corresponding shipping service will be displayed in the View Item page. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 for a shipping service that ships within the marketplace or from 5 to 9 for a shipping service that ships outside of the marketplace. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page. If this field is not used, the rank and hence order of the shipping services will depend on the order they are specified under the **shippingServices** array.
  """
  rank: Int
  """
  This field adds or modifies the flat-rate shipping cost to ship one unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for each shipping service if flat-rate shipping is being used. This field must still be included and set to '0.0' if the corresponding shipping service is offered free of charge to the buyer.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field identifies the domestic or international shipping service and is required for each specified shipping service. Use the [getShippingServices](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices) method to retrieve the full list of domestic and international shipping services supported on a marketplace. The enumeration values representing each shipping service option are returned in the [shippingService](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices#response.shippingServices.shippingService) fields of the **getShippingServices** response.
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID
}

"""
This type is used to modify information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping service options offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
"""
input RelistListingShippingTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to provide information about the shipping business policy to be used for the listing.
  If this field is used, none of the other fields in RelistListingShippingTermsInput container should be used since all shipping settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getFulfillmentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/fulfillment_policy/methods/getFulfillmentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all fulfillment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicy: RelistShippingBusinessPolicyInput
  """
  This field is only applicable to motor vehicle listings and indicates if the buyer is responsible for shipping or picking up the purchased vehicle.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  buyerResponsibleForShipping: Boolean
  """
  This array is used to add or modify locations where the seller will not ship the item. The values specified in this array can be continents, geographical regions, countries, or special locations within the marketplace. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: The entire array of excluded shipping locations must be included if the list is being updated, and not just locations that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  excludedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This field indicates how many business days that the seller needs to ship the item after payment is made by the buyer. The handling time is required by most categories. Top-rated sellers typically set the handling time to 0 or 1 day, but longer handling times are supported.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  handlingTimeDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This array is used to add or modify locations where the seller will ship the item. The values specified in this array can be continents, geographical regions or countries. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: The entire array of shipping locations must be included if the list is being updated, and not just locations that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This container is used to modify information on shipping local to marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to add or change a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  marketplaceShippingOptions: RelistListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to modify information on shipping not local to marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  nonMarketplaceShippingOptions: RelistListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This field is used to provide information of shipping services that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
  **Maximum number of shipping services**: 10, out of which 5 apply for locations within the marketplace and other 5 apply for locations outside of marketplace
  **Note**: This array is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  shippingServices: [RelistListingShippingServiceInput!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **relistListing** mutation. It will show the complete details of the listing, and will also include a list of non-blocking warning messages if any occurred.
"""
type RelistListingSuccess {
  """This container shows the complete details of the relisted listing."""
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows the type of discount(s) applied to the listing fees, if any.
  """
  listingDiscount: [ListingFeeDiscount!]
  """
     This array shows the list of estimated listing fees that the relisted listing will incur.
  **Note**: Always consider the fee amounts to be estimated only.
  """
  listingFees: [SellerListingFee!]
  """
  This array shows the list of non-blocking warnings triggered by the mutation request, if any occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify various tax information, including VAT rates, sales tax rates tor US territories and Canadian provinces, and special tax category codes.
"""
input RelistListingTaxTermsInput {
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller wants the sales tax rate for the jurisdiction to apply to the cumulative amount of item cost and shipping charges, or set to 'false' if the seller does not want sales tax to apply to shipping charges. This field is only applicable if the **salesTaxPercentage** and **salesTaxJurisdictionId** fields are also set.
  """
  salesTaxApplicableToShipping: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to specify a US territory or a Canadian province that will be charged the sales tax rate specified in the **salesTaxPercentage** field. The supported US territories are `AS` (America Samoa), `GU` (Guam), `MP` (Northern Mariana Islands), `PW` (Palau), and `VI` (US Virgin Islands). The two-letter codes for Canadian provinces can be found here on the [Government of Canada](https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/businesses/topics/completing-slips-summaries/financial-slips-summaries/return-investment-income-t5/provincial-territorial-codes.html) website.
  **Note**: Sales tax rates are only applicable on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA and EBAY_CAFR marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxJurisdictionId: String
  """
  This field is used along with **salesTaxJurisdictionId** field to set or modify the sales tax rate for a specific US territory or a Canadian province. The percentage set here will be applied to sale price as the sales tax for the order line item. The value passed in is stored with a precision of 1 digits after the decimal point.
  **Note**: Sales tax rates are only applicable on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA and EBAY_CAFR marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller has an account level sales tax table set up and wishes to use the sales tax rates set up in that table. If this field is set to 'true', the values contained in the other sales tax fields (if set) in this container will be overridden by the values set in the sales tax table.
  """
  salesTaxTableUsed: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to provide a special category of tax such as a recycling fee or disposal tax.
  """
  thirdPartyTaxCategoryCode: String
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the VAT (Value-added Tax) percentage rate that will be charged to buyers when an item is purchased from the listing. VAT is not applicable to all countries, including the US. Allowed VAT percentage rates can vary by region/country, so sellers should be aware of the rates they are legally required/allowed to charge, and they are responsible for charging the correct VAT rate. Only one digit is allowed to the right of the decimal point.
  """
  vatPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field should be included and set to 'true' if the seller is registered on the listing site as a Business Seller and intends to use listing features that are offered to business users only. This field must be included and set to 'true' if the **vatRestrictedToBusinessUser** field is also included and set to 'true'.
  """
  vatRecognizedBusinessSeller: Boolean
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if a business seller wishes to make the listing exclusively available to potential buyers registered on eBay as business users. This feature is only applicable to business sellers residing in Germany, Austria, or Switzerland who are listing in a B2B VAT-enabled category on the eBay Germany (EBAY_DE), Austria (EBAY_AT), or Switzerland (EBAY_CH) marketplaces. To set this field as 'true', the **vatRecognizedBusinessSeller** field must also be included and set to 'true'.
  """
  vatRestrictedToBusinessUser: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify listing terms details for the listing, including listing duration, item location, return policy, fulfillment terms, and more.
"""
input RelistListingTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used for classified ad listings, and adds or modifies contact information for the seller, including days and hours when the seller accepts inquiries from potential buyers.
  """
  adsSellerContact: RelistListingSellerContactInput
  """
  This container is used if the seller wishes to make changes to **Best Offer** settings, including enabling or disabling the Best Offer feature, or to add, modify, or remove the auto-accept and auto-reject thresholds.
  """
  bestOfferTerms: RelistListingBestOfferTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to disable or enable a seller's account-level buyer restrictions and/or set or modify a quantity limit per buyer threshold for a multiple-quantity, fixed price listing.
  """
  buyerRestrictions: RelistListingBuyerRestrictionsInput
  """
  This container is used if the seller wishes to make the listing a charitable listing, or if a charity is already set up, this container is used to change the charitable organization and/or the donation percentage per sale.
  **Note**: eBay for Charity is only supported on the eBay US, eBay UK, eBay Germany, and eBay Canada marketplaces.
  """
  charity: RelistListingCharityInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify global or country-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies for a listing.
  """
  customPolicies: RelistListingCustomPoliciesInput
  """
  This container is used to modify details on how the item will be delivered to the buyer. The data under this container includes available shipping services, ship-to and excluded shipping locations, shipping costs, package details, and more. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a fulfillment business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
  """
  fulfillmentTerms: RelistListingFulfillmentTermsInput
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to make the listing private. With private listings, the eBay user and feedback scores for bidders and buyers are obfuscated to everyone except for the seller. If the ended listing was a private listing and the seller does not wish to keep this setting, this field should be included and set to 'false'.
  """
  hideParticipation: Boolean
  """
  This array can be used if the seller wishes to add or modify site visibility settings. With site visibility, sellers can choose to actively display their listing on one or more other eBay marketplaces for a small fee. Currently, this feature can only be used on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA, EBAY_GB, and EBAY_IE marketplaces. EBAY_US and EBAY_CA listings can specify `EBAY_GB` and `EBAY_IE` in this array to have their listing displayed on the EBAY_GB and EBAY_IE marketplaces, and EBAY_GB and EBAY_IE listings can specify `EBAY_US` and `EBAY_CA` in this array to have their listing display on the EBAY_US and EBAY_CA marketplaces.
  """
  internationalSiteVisibility: [CrossBorderTradingRegion!]
  """
  This container is used to change the actual physical location of the item(s) in this listing. The **country** field is always required, and then either the **location** or **postalCode** must be provided, but not necessarily both.
  """
  itemLocation: RelistListingItemLocationInput
  """
  This container is used to change the duration of the listing, and can also be used to set a future date when the listing will become active.
  """
  lifecycleTerms: RelistListingLifecycleTermsInput
  """
  This field can be used if the seller wishes to change the listing format. See [`ListingFormatType`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  **Note^^: If the listing format is being changed, there's a good chance that many other fields will need to be changed, added, or removed just because the requirements for each listing format are different.
  """
  listingFormat: ListingFormatType
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the radius for a Motors Local Listing. The value supplied in the **distance** field sets the radius of the area in which the vehicle will be available and exposed to interested local buyers. The seller's supplied **postalCode** or **location** field value will be used as the center point for this radius. You can use the [getMotorsListingPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** to get the supported listing distance values for a leaf category. Seller provide the unit of measurement for the **distance** value through the **distanceUnit** field.
  """
  localListingDistance: RelistListingLocalDistanceInput
  """
  This field is needed to modify the lot size for the lot-enabled listing. With lot-enabled listing, the seller is selling a set of two or more similar/related items as a part of one listing. An example of a lot listing might be a collection of children's clothes. The value specified in this field will be the number of distinct items in the lot. Not all leaf categories support lot listings, and the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories do support lot listings.
  **Min value**: 2
  **Max value**: 450,000
  """
  lotSize: Int
  """
  A reference identifier used to attribute the source of data across API families. This ID is returned in the response of the **listingPreviewsCreationTaskById** query of the **Inventory Mapping API**. To ensure continuity and traceability of the data flow, it is strongly recommend that you include this reference ID in any create, update, or relist mutation. Using this ID associates any mutations with the listing preview referenced to create or update the listing.
  **Max length**: 25
  """
  mappingReferenceId: String
  """
  This container is used to modify payment terms and information for the listing, including immediate payment requirement, offline payment methods, and motor vehicle deposit information. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a payment business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies. This container is optional for sellers not opted into business policies.
  """
  paymentTerms: RelistListingPaymentTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
  """
  regulatory: RelistListingRegulatoryInput
  """
  This container is used to modify a domestic return policy and/or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies. With the exception of a few categories, this container is generally required even if the seller's *return policy* is to not accept returns.
  """
  returnTerms: RelistListingReturnTermsInput
  """
  This field is used by the seller to add or modify custom, application-specific data associated with the listing. The string specified here is stored by eBay with the listing but it is not used by eBay in any way other than that.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite the custom data text that is currently associated with the listing.
  **Max length**: 32
  """
  sellerCustomData: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify various tax information, including VAT rates, sales tax rates to US territories and Canadian provinces, and special tax category codes.
  """
  taxTerms: RelistListingTaxTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to enable or disable Bold Title or Gallery Plus listing upgrades, or to add, modify, or remove a Subtitle. Each of these listing upgrades will incur a small fee when the item is relisted.
  **Note**: Any listing upgrades set for the ended listing will carry over to the relisted listing and will incur fees upon relisting.
  """
  visualEnhancements: RelistListingVisualEnhancementsInput
}

"""
This type is used when the **relistListing** mutation fails due to one or more blocking validation errors. A list of validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying will be shown, and one or more non-blocking warning messages will also be shown if any were triggered during the processing of the mutation.
"""
type RelistListingValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. This code can be used by clients to programmatically identify and handle different types of errors without relying on error messages, which may change over time.     
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains a list of blocking validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying.
  """
  violations: [ListingValidationRuleViolation!]!
  """
  This array contains a list of non-blocking validation warnings that do not block processing but provide useful feedback for improving listings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **relistListing** mutation that is run in `VALIDATE` mode, and the listing object is successfully validated without any errors. The results of the validation will be shown, including warnings if any occurred.
"""
type RelistListingValidationSuccess {
  """
  This container shows the complete details of the validated listing object.
  """
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows the type of discount(s) applied to the expected fees, if any.
  """
  listingDiscount: [ListingFeeDiscount!]
  """
  This array shows the list of estimated listing fees that the listing object would occur if relisted.
  """
  listingFees: [SellerListingFee!]
  """
  This array shows the list of non-blocking warnings generated during the validation, if any occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to identify or modify the main trait by which SKUs within a multiple-SKU listing differ, and to provide image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each item variation.
"""
input RelistListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput {
  """
  The trait name by which pictures of the item variations vary. The specified trait will be used to determine which images to display when a buyer selects a variation in the View Item page. For example, if the trait is 'Color', then a corresponding product image in the **traitValueImages** array will be displayed when that color is selected in the View Item page. The trait name specified here must be one of the variation traits specified in the **variationTraits** array.
  **Max length**: 65 characters.
  """
  traitName: String!
  """
  This array is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the *traitImageUrls** array.
  **Note**: The full list of trait value images must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  """
  traitValueImages: [RelistListingVariationTraitValueImageInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify name-value pairs for the traits where each SKU within a multiple-variation listing differs, such as 'Color' and 'Size'. Each available color and each available size will be listed through the **variationTraits** array. If the listing featured t-shirts, each variation within that listing would have a unique color and size combination such as 'Blue, Large'.
"""
input RelistListingVariationsInput {
  """
  This container identifies the main trait by which variations differ, and provides image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each variation. For example, the varying trait may be 'Color', and image URLs would be provided showcasing the different color of each variation.
  """
  imagesVaryByTrait: RelistListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput
  """
  This array provides the names of the varying traits and the available values for each of these traits. For example, one trait might be 'Color', and all of the available colors would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. Another trait might be 'Size', and all of the available sizes would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. If the multiple-SKU listing has two varying traits such as 'Color' and 'Size', each variation would have a different combination of each of these traits, such as a 'Large, Red' shirt.
  The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method of the **Taxonomy API** can be used to retrieve aspects that are optional, recommended or required for a specific category. The  [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method in the **Taxonomy API** works similarly but is processed asynchronously and provides optional, recommended or required aspects every leaf category on an eBay marketplace. The [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method can be paired up with the **Taxonomy SDK** to help maintain an up-to-date list of aspects for each leaf category.
  **Note**: The full list of all variation traits and values must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  **Max number of traits**: 5.
  **max values per trait**: 50.
  **Max length of each trait name and value**: 65 characters.
  """
  variationTraits: [NameValuesPairInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the **traitImageUrls** array.
"""
input RelistListingVariationTraitValueImageInput {
  """
  An array of one or more images that demonstrate the corresponding **traitValue**. For example, if the **traitName** is 'Color' and the **traitValue** is 'Red', the image(s) would show a red variation of the product. Depending on the product, one image per variation may be enough, but multiple images may be specified for each **traitValue**. For example, it is possible that a seller would want to show the front and back of each shirt in each color.
  **Note**: The full list of image URLs must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  **Note** All images, whether they are hosted by eBay Picture Server (EPS) or self-hosted, must comply with eBay picture requirements. eBay Picture Server (EPS) and self-hosted picture URLs should not be mixed, and all URLs must use 'https' and not 'http'.
  **Max number of images per trait value**: 12.
  """
  traitImageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]!
  """
  The trait value of the corresponding image(s) in the **traitImageUrls** array. If the **traitName** is 'Color', values in this field may include *Red*, *Blue*, *Green*, etc. At least one of the variations within the multiple-SKU listing must have this value.
  **Max length**: 65 characters.
  """
  traitValue: String!
}

"""
This type is used to enable or disable Bold Title or Gallery Plus listing upgrades, or to add, modify, or remove a Subtitle. Each of these listing upgrades will incur a small fee.
"""
input RelistListingVisualEnhancementsInput {
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable the Bold Title listing upgrade. With this upgrade, the listing title will be in boldface type in search results for greater visibility.
  **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing as motor vehicle listing titles are automatically generated by eBay based on Year, Make, Model, and other aspects of the vehicle such as engine type and trim.
  """
  boldTitle: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable the Gallery Plus feature. With Gallery Plus, a larger gallery image of the item is displayed in search results.
  **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing.
  """
  galleryPlus: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to add or modify a customized subtitle for the listing. By using a subtitle, more keywords can be provided and search results may be improved.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current subtitle if one is defined for the listing.
  **Max length**: 55 characters.
  """
  subtitle: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify a domestic return policy or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
"""
input RelistShippingBusinessPolicyInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify a fulfillment business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all shipping settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getFulfillmentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/fulfillment_policy/methods/getFulfillmentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all fulfillment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID!
  """
  This array is used to override the shipping costs for one or more shipping service options defined in the fulfillment terms being used for the listing.
  """
  overrideShippingOptions: [RelistListingOverrideShippingOptionInput!]
}

"""
This type indicates that the buyer cancelled due to a change of mind about the purchase.
"""
type RemorseCancellation implements ContractCancellationReason {
  """
  The unique cancellation reason code for this use case. For this type, the value is `REMORSE`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the cancellation reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
The union type for the **removeAllFromWatchList** mutation. If the **removeAllFromWatchList** mutation succeeds, a all items will be removed from the user's watchlist. If the **removeAllFromWatchList** mutation fails, an error detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the items will not be removed from the user's Watchlist. 
"""
union RemoveAllFromWatchListOutput = RemoveAllFromWatchListSuccess

"""
This type indicates that the **removeAllFromWatchList mutation succeeded, and all items were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist. This type returns the number of items successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
"""
type RemoveAllFromWatchListSuccess {
  """
  The number of items that were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
  """
  numberOfItemsUnwatched: Int!
}

"""
This type indicates that the **removeFromWatchList** mutation failed, and that all requested items failed to be removed for the user's Watchlist. The unique identifier of each item that failed to be removed from the Watchlist is returned, alongside the reason each failed.  This type also returns the total number of items being watched by the user after the failed mutation and the maximum number of items they can add to their Watchlist.
"""
type RemoveFromWatchListFailure implements BusinessError {
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
     **Maximum length**: 500 characters
     **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
     **Maximum length**: 500 characters
     **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array returns the unique identifier(s) of the item(s) that failed to be added to the user's Watchlist, along with the reason each failed.
  """
  failedItems: [WatchListRemoveFailure!]!
  """The current total number of items in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListCount: Int!
  """The maximum number of items allowed in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListMaximum: Int!
}

"""The base request type for the **removeFromWatchList** mutation."""
input RemoveFromWatchListInput {
  """
  An array of items to be removed from the user's Watchlist.
  **Note:** This array must contain at least one item.
  """
  itemsToRemove: [WatchListEntryToRemove!]!
}

"""
The union type for the **removeFromWatchList** mutation. This type covers three possible scenarios: success, partial failure, or failure. If the **removeFromWatchList** mutation succeeds, the specified items will be removed from the user's Watchlist. If the **removeFromWatchList** mutation fails or partially fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why each item failed will be returned, and the item(s) will not be removed from the user's Watchlist. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error. 
"""
union RemoveFromWatchListOutput = RemoveFromWatchListFailure | RemoveFromWatchListPartialFailure | RemoveFromWatchListSuccess

"""
This type indicates that the **removedFromWatchList** mutation partially failed. Some of the specified items were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist, but one or more failed to be removed. The unique identifier of each item that successfully removed from the Watchlist is returned. In addition, the unique identifier of each item that failed to be removed from the Watchlist is returned, alongside the reason each failed. This type also returns the total number of items removed from the user's Watchlist after the partially failed mutation, the current total number of items being watched by the user, and the maximum number of items they can add to their Watchlist.
"""
type RemoveFromWatchListPartialFailure implements BusinessError {
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
     **Maximum length**: 500 characters
     **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
     **Maximum length**: 500 characters
     **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array returns the unique identifier(s) of the item(s) that failed to be added to the user's Watchlist, along with the reason they failed.
  """
  failedItems: [WatchListRemoveFailure!]!
  """
  The number of items that were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
  """
  numberOfItemsUnwatched: Int!
  """
  This array returns the unique identifier(s) of the item(s) that were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
  """
  removedItems: [Item!]!
  """The current total number of items in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListCount: Int!
  """The maximum number of items allowed in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListMaximum: Int!
}

"""
This type indicates that the **removeFromWatchList** mutation succeeded, and all requested items were successfully removed from a user's Watchlist. The unique identifier of each item that was successfully removed from the Watchlist is returned. This type also returns the total number of items removed from the user's Watchlist after the successful mutation, the current total number of items being watched by the user, and the maximum number of items they can add to their Watchlist.
"""
type RemoveFromWatchListSuccess {
  """
  The number of items that were successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
  """
  numberOfItemsUnwatched: Int!
  """
  This array returns the unique identifier(s) of the item(s) successfully removed from the user's Watchlist.
  """
  removedItems: [Item!]!
  """The current total number of items in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListCount: Int!
  """The maximum number of items allowed in the user's Watchlist."""
  watchListMaximum: Int!
}

"""
This type indicates that the seller has sent a replacement item to the buyer.
"""
type ReplacementSent implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """The machine-readable reason code: 'REPLACEMENT_SENT'."""
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable text of the case referral reason.
  **Max length**: 100 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type is used when a business error occurs with a **requestPurchaseQuote** mutation. 
"""
type RequestPurchaseQuoteBusinessError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier of the specific error. This code can be used by clients to programmatically identify and handle different types of errors without relying on error messages, which may change over time. 
  **Maximum length**: 40 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric characters and underscores, in UPPER_CASE format
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
  **Maximum length**: 500 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric characters, spaces, and common punctuation
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This boolean indicates whether or not the user should try to request the purchase quote again. If this field is returned as 'true', the user can make another attempt to request the purchase quote.
  """
  retryable: Boolean!
}

"""
This input is used by buyer to request a purchase quote when using the **requestPurchaseQuote** mutation.
"""
input RequestPurchaseQuoteInput {
  """
  This array is used to provide two or more item commitment identifiers that will become a part of the requested purchase quote. A comma is used as a delimiter for each item commitment identifier.
  """
  lineItems: [PurchaseQuoteItemInput!]!
  """
  This field allows the buyer to provide a custom message to the seller regarding the purchase quote being requested.
  **Minimum length**: 1 character
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  messageToSeller: String
  """
  This container is used to provide an alternative shipping address to use if the buyer wishes that the items be sent to this address instead of the buyer's shipping address on file with eBay. 
  """
  shippingAddress: AddressInput
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **requestPurchaseQuote** mutation.
"""
union RequestPurchaseQuoteOutput = RequestPurchaseQuoteBusinessError | RequestPurchaseQuoteSuccess

"""
This base output type is used for a successful **requestPurchaseQuote** mutation, and shows the details of the successfully requested purchase quote.
"""
type RequestPurchaseQuoteSuccess {
  """This container shows the successfully requested purchase quote."""
  purchaseQuote: PurchaseQuote
}

"""
This type is used to provide the name and contact information for one or more responsible persons based in the EU.
"""
type ResponsiblePerson {
  """This container shows the street address for a responsible person."""
  address: BusinessEntityAddress
  """
  This field shows the company name associated with the responsible person.
  """
  companyName: String
  """
  This container shows the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the responsible person. A seller must provide at least one of the three is required if a responsible person is supplied.
  """
  contact: BusinessEntityContact
  """
  This array shows the responsible person type, and the only supported value is`EU_RESPONSIBLE_PERSON`.
  """
  personTypes: [String!]
}

"""
This container includes information associated with retracted bid records.
"""
type RetractedBidMetadata implements BidMetadata {
  """
  The date and time, expressed in UTC, when the corresponding bid was placed.
  
  **Format:** YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.SSSZ
  """
  placedAt: DateTime!
  """
  User-specified text indicating the reason for retracting the corresponding bid.
  
  **Note:** The seller of an item will be able to view all retraction reasons for retracted bids associated with their own item. A bidder will only be able to view the retraction reason associated with their own bid.
  
  **Format:** UTF-8
  **Maximum Length:** None
  **Minimum Length:** When this field is masked it is returned as an empty, non-null string.
  """
  reason: String!
  """
  The date and time, expressed in UTC, when the corresponding bid was retracted.
  
  **Format:** YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.SSSZ
  """
  retractedAt: DateTime!
}

"""
This type, available for the seller, is used to retry refund cancellation action on the contract.
"""
type RetryRefundContractCancellationAction implements ContractCancellationAction {
  """
  The machine-readable cancellation action code for this use case. For this type, the value is `RETRY_REFUND`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message explaining the cancellation action code. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This interface represents various return actions that can be taken by an actor (for example, the buyer or the seller).
**Seller:** Actions include sending a message, submitting an offer, approving a return, declining a return, providing shipment information, recording the returned item received, issuing a refund, and similar actions.
**Buyer:** Actions include sending a message, accept an offer, providing shipment information, recording the item as shipped, and similar actions.
"""
interface ReturnAction {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return action. For example: `SEND_MESSAGE`, `APPROVE_RETURN`, `DECLINE_RETURN`, `PROCESS_RETURN_REFUND`, and similar action codes.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """
  Human-readable text for return action. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
The error type indicates when an action is not allowed. This is used when a user attempts to perform an action they don't have permission for, or when the action is not valid in the current state.
"""
type ReturnActionNotPermittedError implements BusinessError {
  """
  A list of one or more actions that are available to the user in the current state. This can be used to guide the user on what actions they can take.
  """
  availableActions: [ReturnAction!]
  """A machine-readable error code: `RTRN_ACTION_NOT_PERMITTED`"""
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable error message. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
}

"""
This interface represents a return address associated with a user or a business. Address formats vary by country and carrier, and some fields may not apply or can be omitted based on regional conventions and data availability. Optional string fields may be returned as null when:
- it was not provided by the user
- it is not applicable in the region
- it is unknown
When a field is present, values are returned in their localized form and may be normalized (for example, uppercased postal codes) depending on upstream systems.

**Note:** Avoid relying on empty strings. Absence of a value is represented as null.
"""
interface ReturnAddress {
  """
  The contact details associated with this address (e.g., name, phone). This field is only returned in the case of a buyer receiving the seller’s contact details for a return address to generate a return label.
  """
  addressContact: AddressContact
  """
  The unique public identifier for the address. This field is used primarily for Return Address records and for sharing a reference that is stable across requests.
  
  **Example:** 'RA-9c4b2f58-1f4e-4e72-9a4c-702d5e2b74e1'
  """
  addressId: ID
  """
  The first line of the street address (e.g., house number and street name).
  	
  **Examples:**
  - '2025 Hamilton Avenue'
  - '221B Baker Street'
  - 'Building 12' (in regions where street numbering is uncommon)
  	
  **Notes:** 
  - This field is required in most street-addressing countries (e.g., United States, United Kingdom).
  - This field may be null in regions that rely primarily on district/building names rather than street numbers (e.g., Hong Kong).
  - This field may be null for pure P.O. Box formats or institutional addresses where the line is not used separately (e.g., UAE, certain Qatar addresses).
  """
  addressLine1: String
  """
  The second line of the street address, such as apartment, suite, building, floor, or additional delivery detail.
  
  **Examples:**
  - 'Apt 5B'
  - 'Suite 1200'
  - 'Room 303, East Wing'
  
  **Notes:**
  - This field is common and often present in the U.S., Canada, and the U.K. for unit-level delivery.
  - This field is null if no secondary address details are provided or applicable.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  The city, town, or locality name.
  
  **Examples:**
  - 'San Jose'
  - 'London'
  - 'Toronto'
  
  **Notes:**
  - This field may be null in regions that instead use district/municipality without a conventional **city** field (e.g., Hong Kong, Macau).
  - This field may be null for rural/local addresses that rely on townland or parish concepts (e.g., some legacy Irish addresses).
  """
  city: String
  """
  The two-letter [ISO 3166](https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html) country code of the return address.
  
  **Examples:**
  - 'US', 'GB', 'CA', 'IE', 'HK'
  
  **Note:** This field is required for all addresses.
  """
  countryCode: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The postal code, ZIP code, or PIN code used for mail routing for the return address.
  
  **Examples:**
  - '95110' (U.S. ZIP)
  - 'SW1A 1AA' (UK post code)
  - 'H3Z 2Y7' (Canada postal code)
  
  **Note:** This field may be null in countries or territories that do not use postal codes (e.g., many Hong Kong and UAE addresses relying on P.O. Boxes).
  """
  postalCode: String
  """
  The state, province, region, or administrative area code or name.
  
  **Examples:**
  - 'CA' or 'California'
  - 'ON' or "Ontario' 							 
  
  **Notes:**
  - This field may be null in countries without a state/province concept (e.g., Singapore, Hong Kong).
  - This field may be null when the locality and postal code provide sufficient routing and the region does not require this field.
  - This field may be present as either code or full name depending on upstream normalization.
  """
  stateOrProvince: String
}

"""
Return Adjustment type
A return adjustment refers to the modification of a transaction or order after a customer returns
a product. This adjustment typically involves updating the payment, inventory, or order state to
reflect the return of goods. It ensures that the financial and inventory records are accurate after
the product is returned, whether due to a defect, dissatisfaction, or change of mind.
"""
type ReturnAdjustment implements OrderAdjustment {
  """User-friendly ID of the adjustment."""
  adjustmentId: ID!
  """Creation date of the adjustment."""
  createdAt: DateTime!
  """Return event associated to this adjustment."""
  return: OrderReturn!
  """State of the adjustment."""
  state: OrderAdjustmentState!
  """Last updated date-time of the adjustment."""
  updatedAt: DateTime!
}

"""This type details a seller's automation preferences."""
type ReturnAutomationPreference {
  """
  The return addresses eligible for use in the seller's automation return preferences. Addresses are available per eBay business policies.
  """
  eligibleReturnAddress: [ReturnAddress!]
  """
  A list of seller-defined listing groups used in return automation rules. These groups can be referenced in rule conditions to target specific listings. Each group may contain a limited number of listings.
  """
  listingGroups: [ReturnRuleListingGroup!]
  """
  This list of one or more rules defines the seller-configured respond rules that determine **how** to respond a buyer's return request. Each rule defines the conditions and parameters for an automation decision:
  - `APPROVE_KEEP_THE_ITEM`: Buyer keeps the item and return is approved with Refund.
  - `APPROVE_RETURN_THE_ITEM`: Buyer is instructed to return the item
  The rules are evaluated in order of priority (lowest numbered first), with the first matching rule produces the approval automation outcome. This is then used to drive subsequent routing through the **returnToAddressRules**.
  """
  returnResponseRules: [ReturnResponseRule!]
  """
  This list of one or more rules defines the seller-configured routing rules that determine **where** an approved return should be sent once a buyer is instructed to return the item. Each rule within this list corresponds to the `RETURN_TO_ADDRESS` automation type and specifies the conditions under which a particular return address (from the eligible address pool) should be used. These routing rules are evaluated before an approval rule (for example, `APPROVE_RETURN_THE_ITEM`) has matched, and are prioritized by `priority`
  (lowest first). The first matching rule resolves the `returnAddressId` to which the buyer will be directed.
  """
  returnToAddressRules: [ReturnToAddressRule!]
}

"""
This interface provides for an automation return rule definition with ID, categories, status, priority, and conditions.
"""
interface ReturnAutomationRule {
  """The associated condition set for this rule."""
  conditionSet: ReturnRuleConditionSet!
  """
  The unique name of the rule.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  name: String!
  """
  This integer defines the rule's evaluation order. Rules are processed from lowest to highest number, where a lower number means higher priority. Evaluation stops as soon as a rule matches. For example, a rule with priority 1 is evaluated before a rule with priority 5.
    
  **Note:** Each rule must have a unique priority number.
  """
  priority: Int!
  """The unique identifier for the rule generated by the system."""
  ruleId: ID!
  """Status of the rule. Only rules with the status `ENABLED` are executed."""
  status: SellerReturnRuleStatus!
}

"""
This type indicates that the return was closed without completion and is considered cancelled. Instances when this status applies:
- the buyer closes the return request without shipping the item back
- eBay closes the return due to timeout occurring due to the following:
  - an approved return was not shipped back by the buyer within the allowed time
  - a requested return was not approved by the seller, and the buyer did not ask eBay to step in and assist
- eBay closes the return because the buyer filed an external payment dispute
"""
type ReturnCancelled implements ReturnStatus {
  """A machine-readable return status code: `CANCELLED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable return status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicate the return is closed (is at an end state). This typically indicates that the return lifecycle completed successfully.
- the buyer keeps the item and receives a full refund
- the buyer ships the item back and receives a full refund
- the buyer keeps the item and receives a partial refund after negotiating with seller
The refund object provides the refund amount and breakdown, and the return shipment section provides package or shipment details.
"""
type ReturnClosed implements ReturnStatus {
  """A machine-readable return status code: `CLOSED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable return status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""This interface describes why the line item is ineligible for return."""
interface ReturnCreationIneligibilityReason {
  """A machine-readable ineligibility code."""
  code: String!
  """A human-readable ineligibility message."""
  displayMessage: String!
  """The specific line item that is ineligible for return."""
  orderLineItem: OrderLineItem!
}

"""
This error type provides for a return creation eligibility error that denotes return creation is blocked due to eligibility issues. It provides additional details explaining why the return line item is not eligible for return.
"""
type ReturnCreationNotAllowedError implements BusinessError {
  """A machine-readable return error code: `RTRN_CREATION_NOT_ALLOWED`"""
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable error message. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """Reason describing why the line item is not eligible for return"""
  returnIneligibilityReasons: [ReturnCreationIneligibilityReason!]!
}

"""
This type indicates the return is declined by the seller or eBay admin and it's in an end state, in both code and a human-readable description.
"""
type ReturnDeclined implements ReturnStatus {
  """A machine-readable code providing the return status: `DECLINED`"""
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the return status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""This type indicates that the buyer returned the wrong item."""
type ReturnedWrongItem implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """Machine-readable reason code: 'BUYER_RETURNED_WRONG_ITEM'."""
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable text of the case referral reason.
  **Max length**: 100 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type represents the fulfillment details of a return. This object bridges between the user-facing return process and the underlying logistics execution. It provides the shipment-related context for a return, such as label details, addresses, and tracking data. Buyers and sellers interact primarily with high-level fulfillment states, the internal logistics components (for example, carrier tracking and events) are managed under `logisticExecutionDetail`.
"""
type ReturnFulfillment {
  """
  The destination address where the return package is expected to be delivered.
  """
  finalDestinationAddress: ReturnAddress! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.return.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.return&eBayUser"])
  """
  This object represents user-friendly fulfilment states for a return. These states convey to buyers and sellers where their return stands in the fulfillment lifecycle, while also aligning with underlying logistics milestones.
    
  **Note:** Returns presently have one package per return line item.
  """
  fulfillmentStatus: ReturnFulfillmentStatus!
  """
  The summary of the return fulfillment including the latest events for the return shipment. This provides the minimal details required for launching the return. This optional object is present only when a return shipment is initiated.
  """
  returnFulfillmentSummary: ReturnFulfillmentSummary
  """
  This object provides RMA (Return Merchandise Authorization) details for the return shipment, optionally present based on seller preference.
  """
  rmaDetails: [RmaDetail!]
  """
  This object provides details for initiating the return shipment and is optionally present when return fulfillment is to be initiated. It is not present if there are no action items for the seller to initiate the return fulfillment or the fulfillment has already been initiated. Included in this object are available ways to start the return, for example, a seller-provided label or other label that could be used by the buyer or eBay to initiate the return shipment, and address information.
  """
  sellerFulfillmentInitiation: ReturnFulfillmentInitiation @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.return.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.return&eBayUser"])
}

"""
This type indicates that the return shipment is currently in transit to the destination or being processed by the carrier.
"""
type ReturnFulfillmentComplete implements ReturnFulfillmentStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return fulfillment status.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """The date and time when the return shipment was completed (delivered)."""
  completedAt: DateTime!
  """
  A human-readable label identifying the return fulfillment status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates that the return shipment is currently in transit to the destination or being processed by the carrier.
"""
type ReturnFulfillmentException implements ReturnFulfillmentStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return fulfillment status.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable label identifying the return fulfillment status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type provides details for initiating the return shipment and is optionally present when return fulfillment is to be initiated. Included are available ways to start the return, for example, a seller-provided label or other label that could be used by the buyer or eBay to initiate the return shipment, and address information.
"""
type ReturnFulfillmentInitiation {
  """
  The address that has been provided as the return destination address for the return shipment. This address could be a seller address or a facility address if the package has to be routed to an intermediate facility before reaching final destination. Sellers and Buyers are encouraged to use this address for initiating providing the return label.
  """
  destinationAddress: ReturnAddress!
  """
  A list of one or more available options for initiating the return shipment. Available actions may vary based on the return and the actor, and include the following:
  - Use Platform Label
  - Attach Label to Return
  - Record Label was sent offline
  This list is provided only when the return label provisioning options are available for the return. It is omitted if the return label has been already provided.
  """
  labelProvisionOptions: [ReturnLabelProvisionOption!]
  """
  The origin address from which the return shipment will be initiated. This may be the buyer's address or, if the package was routed through an intermediate facility, the facility's address. Buyers and sellers are encouraged to use this address when initiating the return.
  """
  originAddress: ReturnAddress!
  """
  A list of one or more return labels provisioned to be used to send the return packages. This optionally present return label is not returned if the label is already provisioned for the return shipment.
  """
  provisionedLabels: [ProvisionedReturnLabel!]
}

"""
This type indicates that the return shipment is currently in transit to the destination or being processed by the carrier.
"""
type ReturnFulfillmentInProgress implements ReturnFulfillmentStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return fulfillment status.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable label identifying the return fulfillment status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This interface represents the user-friendly fulfillment states for a return. These states convey to buyers and sellers where their return stands in the fulfillment lifecycle, while also aligning with underlying logistics milestones.
"""
interface ReturnFulfillmentStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return fulfillment status.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable label identifying the return fulfillment status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type provides a summary of the return fulfillment including the latest events for the return shipment. It includes the latest events for every return shipment package.
"""
type ReturnFulfillmentSummary {
