  **Note:** The userId of the user requesting listings is retrieved from the context. Users may only retrieve their own listings.
  """
  endedListings(searchInput: SellerEndedListingSearchInput): SellerListingSearchResult!
  """
  This type contains the seller's scheduled listings that satisfy the search criteria specified by `SellerScheduledListingSearchInput`.
  
  **Note:** The userId of the user requesting listings is retrieved from the context. Users may only retrieve their own listings.
  """
  scheduledListings(searchInput: SellerScheduledListingSearchInput): SellerListingSearchResult!
}

"""
This union is used to request the list of active, ended, and/or scheduled listings based on the provided search criteria. If no listings are identified that satisfy the search criteria an empty result is returned. If there is an input error, 'SellerListingSearchInvalidInput' is returned.

**Note:** The user issuing this call **must** be the seller associated with the listings.
"""
union SellerListingSearchResult = SellerListingSearchInvalidInput | SellerListings

"""
This type is used to pass in listing ID values for the **sellerListings** query.
"""
input SellerListingsInput {
  """List of SellerListingInput for bulk retrieval"""
  listings: [SellerListingInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to specify sort criteria and sort order for the requested listings.
"""
input SellerListingSortField {
  """
  This enumeration value specifies the criteria on which listings are to be sorted.
  """
  field: SellerListingSortFieldEnum!
  """
  This enumeration value specifies if listings will be returned in ascending or descending order based on the specified `field` criteria.
  
  **Default Value:** ASC
  """
  sortOrder: SortOrder = ASC
}

"""
This enumeration type contains the list of available fields by which listings may be sorted.
"""
enum SellerListingSortFieldEnum {
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their available quantity.
  """
  AVAILABLE_QUANTITY
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their respective number of bids.
  """
  BID_COUNT
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the current price of the listing. Sorting is currency-agnostic.
  
  **IMPORTANT:** Currency conversion is not applied to prices in different currencies. Prices are compared based on their numeric value only. It is recommended that this enumeration value be used in combination with the `marketplaces` filter when listings are from multiple marketplaces to avoid inconsistent ordering due to currency differences.
  """
  CURRENT_PRICE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the custom label or Stock Keeping Unit (SKU) assigned by the seller to the listing.
  """
  CUSTOM_LABEL_SKU
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the duration specified at the time the listing became active.
  
  Available duration values are:
  - Fixed duration listing values, in days: 1, 3, 5, 7, 10, 30
  - Good 'Til Cancelled (GTC) listings are treated as having an infinite duration for sorting purposes.
      **Note:** 'Buy It Now' listings have a duration of GTC.
  
  When sorted in Ascending order, GTC listings appear last: 1-day, 3-day, ..., 30-day, GTC
  
  When sorted in Descending order, GTC listings appear first: GTC, 30-day, ..., 3-day, 1-day
  """
  DURATION
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the end time of the listing. For active and scheduled listings, scheduled end time is used.
  """
  END_TIME
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their `formatType`. When sorting listings in ascending order, `AUCTION` listings are first, followed by `FIXED_PRICE` listings, and then `CLASSIFIED_AD` listings.
  
  **Note:** Auction listings with a 'Buy It Now' price enabled are considered `AUCTION` listings when being sorted.
  """
  FORMAT
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the listed quantity.
  """
  LISTED_QUANTITY
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the listing IDs.
  """
  LISTING_ID
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their reserve price. Reserve price is used in auction listings to set a minimum price that must be met for the item to be sold. Sorting is currency-agnostic.
  
  **IMPORTANT:** Currency conversion is not applied to prices in different currencies. Prices are compared based on their numeric value only. It is recommended that this enumeration value be used in combination with the `marketplaces` filter when listings are from multiple marketplaces to avoid inconsistent ordering due to currency differences.
  """
  RESERVE_PRICE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their respective shipping costs.
  """
  SHIPPING_COST
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their sold quantity.
  """
  SOLD_QUANTITY
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the initial starting price of the listing. Sorting is currency-agnostic.
  
  **IMPORTANT:** Currency conversion is not applied to prices in different currencies. Prices are compared based on their numeric value only. It is recommended that this enumeration value be used in combination with the `marketplaces` filter when listings are from multiple marketplaces to avoid inconsistent ordering due to currency differences.
  """
  START_PRICE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the date and time the listings became active.
  """
  START_TIME
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their remaining time before ending.
  """
  TIME_LEFT
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by the listing title.
  """
  TITLE
  """
  This enumeration value indicates listings will be sorted by their respective number of watchers.
  """
  WATCH_COUNT
}

"""
This type is used to show the current state of active eBay listings in the **sellerListings** query response. If a listing is found, but is on hold, only the **listingId** and **onHoldReason** fields are returned.
"""
type SellerListingsOutput {
  """
  This array will show the list of eBay listings retrieved with the **sellerListings** query.
  **Note**: With the initial release, only one eBay listing may be retrieved with this query.
  """
  listings: [SellerListingOutput!]!
}

"""
The base request type for the **sellerNegotiationHistory** query. This type is used to define the filters for the response payload.
"""
input SellerNegotiationHistoryInput {
  """
  This container can be used to specify the filters used for retrieving a seller's negotiation history. If this container is omitted, the following default filters will be used:
  - Time window: last **90 days** by most-recent activity
  - Recent negotiation status: **ACTIONABLE**
  - Initiator: **BUYER**
  """
  filters: NegotiationHistoryFilters
}

"""The union type for the **sellerNegotiationHistory** query."""
union SellerNegotiationHistoryOutput = SellerNegotiationHistorySuccess

"""
This type is used for a successful **sellerNegotiationHistory** query. This type returns item negotiation information, as well as pagination for each negotiated item and its latest offer per thread.
**Note**: Pagination is applied at the *item* level; each element in `itemNegotiations` is an item bucket with that item’s negotiation information.
"""
type SellerNegotiationHistorySuccess {
  """
  This container returns item-level buckets, with each element representing one negotiated item and its matching negotiations (latest offer per thread). This includes list of negotiation threads associated with the item and the offers exchanged within each negotiation.
  """
  itemNegotiations: [ItemNegotiation!]!
  """
  This container returns cursor-based pagination for the item buckets (items are paged; negotiations inside an item are not paged).
  """
  pagination: Pagination!
}

"""
This type represents the result of a search for order inquiries, and contains the list of order inquiries for the current page and associated pagination metadata.
"""
type SellerOrderInquiries {
  """
  This array returns the list of order inquiries returned in the current page of the search result.
  """
  orderInquiries: [OrderInquiry!]
  """
  This container can be used to specify optional pagination settings that can be used to control page size and navigate through multiple pages of results. 
  """
  pagination: Pagination!
}

"""
This input used to search for order inquiries based on specific criteria.
- Do not provide both **initialPage** and **pageInfo**; they are mutually exclusive.
- If **maxPageSize** is < '1' or > '100', the server defaults to 20 (no error).
- If **pageCursor** is malformed or expired, an empty result is returned.
- When using **pageInfo**, filters and sorting must match the initial request, or the server will return an empty result.
"""
input SellerOrderInquiriesInput {
  """
  The parameters for the **first page** of a query request.
  **Note:** This container cannot be used together with **cursor**.
  """
  initialPage: OrderInquiryInitialPageInput
  """
  The parameters for fetching a **subsequent page** of results. This container requires the opaque **cursor** (returned in **Pagination.nextCursor** or `Pagination.previousCursor**). This container must use the same filters and sorting as the initial request.
  **Note:** This container cannot be used together with **initialPage**.
  """
  pageInfo: PageInfoInput
}

"""
The union type for the **sellerOrderInquries** query. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **sellerOrderInquries** query succeeds, the  seller order inquiries will be returned. If the **sellerOrderInquries** query fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the query failed will be returned, and the item commitment will not be created. If a query fails, there will always be at least one blocking error.
"""
union SellerOrderInquiriesOutput = OrderInquiryInvalidDateRangeError | OrderInquiryInvalidPageSizeError | OrderInquiryInvalidSearchInputError | SellerOrderInquiries

"""
This type includes the list of returned order line items and pagination information.
"""
type SellerOrderReturns {
  """This array lists one or more line items for the returned order."""
  orderReturns: [OrderReturn!]!
  """
  This object provides pagination information for navigating through the returned page set.
  """
  pagination: Pagination!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **sellerOrderReturns** query. This type supports an initial, filtered query and cursor-based pagination for subsequent pages. Use either **initialPage** or **pagination** in a single request, but not both.
"""
input SellerOrderReturnsInput {
