  The filter and sorting parameters use the same filters and sorting as the initial request (**OrderReturnInitialPageInput** parameters in a previous **initialPage** request). This object requires the opaque `cursor` returned in **Pagination.nextCursor** or **Pagination.previousCursor**.
    
  **Note:** Do not use both this field and the `initialPage` field in a single request. Call using **initialPage** before calling using **cursor**.
  """
  pagination: PageInfoInput
}

"""
This base response union type for the **sellerOrderReturns** query includes the result of the query and any errors encountered.
"""
union SellerOrderReturnsOutput = ReturnActionNotPermittedError | ReturnInvalidDateRangeError | ReturnInvalidPageSizeError | ReturnInvalidSearchInputError | SellerOrderReturns

"""
This type is used to identify a seller's financial account used to receive payout funds.
"""
type SellerPaymentAccount implements FundAccount {
  """The unique identifier of the domain or type of the account."""
  domain: ID!
  """The unique identifier of the account that will receive payout funds."""
  identifier: ID!
}

"""
This type is used to provide common product details for the listing, including product aspects, title, description, condition, images, and more.
"""
type SellerProduct {
  """
  An array of name-value pairs that define the product aspects. For a multiple-variation listing, only the common aspects will be specified in this array, and the pivoting aspects
  (aka traits) will be specified at the item variation level.
  """
  aspects: [NameValuesPair!]
  """
  This object shows is used to provide the eBay and eBay store categories where the item is listed.
  """
  categories: ListingCategory
  """
  The full description of the product. This is a mandatory field for a listing.
  **Note**: This field may contain HTML markup and inline CSS, and may be up to 500,000 characters including the HTML and CSS tags and attributes.
  """
  description: String
  """
  For US or CA eBay Motors vehicle listing. Including Make Model and sub-model.
  """
  ebayGeneratedTitle: String
  """
  An array of images used for the listing and appearing in the listing's photo gallery. eBay listings require at least one image, so this array should never be null.
  """
  images: [ListingImage!]
  """
  This boolean field Indicates whether or not the listing has an attached list of compatible vehicles for a Parts & Accessories item.
  """
  includesCompatibilities: Boolean
  """
  This array is used to define the motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles. Year, Make, and Model are typical aspects used to identify a motor vehicle.
  """
  itemCompatibilities: [ItemCompatibility!]
  """
  This object is used to express the condition of the item(s) in this listing. A large majority of eBay categories require a condition, and this condition is specified through a numeric identifier in the **conditionId** field. For non-new items, the **conditionDescription** may be used by the seller to provide specific details about the item's condition or 'wear and tear'. The **conditionDescriptor** array is returned for graded and ungraded trading cards and provides condition details in a structured manner.
  """
  itemCondition: ItemCondition
  """
  This object shows the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
  """
  motorVehicleIdentifier: ListingMotorVehicleIdentifier
  """
  The title of the listing. This title will be shown in search results and on the View Item page. If the listing is for a motor vehicle, the title will be shown in the **ebayGeneratedTitle** field instead and will consist of the Make, Model, Year, etc. of the vehicle.
  """
  title: String
  """
  This array shows the unique identifier of a product video. This video ID will only be shown to the seller of the listing. The getVideo method can be used to retrieve metadata and status of the video. Currently, only one video may be added to each listing.
  """
  videos: [Video!]
}

"""
This type stores seller-related profile information about the user.

**Note:** If the user requesting this data is not authorized to view some of the requested information, those fields containing sensitive/confidential information will return null values.
"""
type SellerProfile {
  """
  This object returns information related to the seller's direct charity affiliation, if applicable.
  **Note**: This object will return 'null' if the seller does not have a direct charity affiliation.
  """
  charityAffiliation: CharityAffiliation
  """This type stores seller-related profile information about the user."""
  user: User!
  """
  Store-related information for this seller, including the store’s name, URL, and logo.
  Represents the seller’s storefront as managed in the Store Edit Entity Service.
  Seller will have only one store associated with their account in their selected marketplace.
  This can be null if the seller does not own a store.
  """
  sellerStore: SellerStore @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.stores.readonly&eBayUser"])
  """
  List of subscription records for the seller.
  
  Each subscription provides the seller with specific benefits, features, or allowances
  based on their enrolled Store subscription tier.
  
  Returns:
  - An array of subscription objects (empty array [] if seller has no subscriptions)
  - Null only under exceptional circumstances
  """
  subscriptions: [SellerSubscriptionPlan!] @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.account.readonly&eBayUser"])
}

"""
This type represents a promotional shipping rule configured by the seller (e.g., "Free shipping over $25").
"""
type SellerPromotionalShippingRule {
  """
  When provided, this field defines the minimum number of items required to enable this rule.
  """
  minItemCount: Int
  """
  When provided, this field defines the minimum order amount required to enable this rule.
  """
  minOrderAmount: Decimal
  """
  The specific type of the promotional shipping rule defined by the seller.
  """
  promotionalShippingType: String!
  """The shipping cost defined for this rule."""
  shippingCost: Decimal!
}

"""
This type represents a seller's refund breakdown and provides details about the amounts the seller refunds on the contract. 
**Note**: This type provides only the seller pricelines and refund amount that seller received as part contract fulfillment, and doesn't include pricelines such as 'TAX' or 'SERVICE_FEE' that the seller didn't receive in the first place. These fields can only be accessed by a seller.
"""
type SellerRefundBreakdown implements RefundBreakdown {
  """
  This array returns all types of credits applied to the refund, including: 
     - **Total fee credits**. In some instances, marketplaces fees charged are credited to the seller.
     - **Total donation credits**. In some instances, the donation of sale proceeds are credited back with the refund.
  **Note**: Donations are not always credited back if the proceeds were already donated. 
  If this array is returned 'null', there are no additional credits applied to refund.
  """
  credits: [SellerRefundCredit!]
  """
  The net amount being refunded by the seller. This value equals the **totalRefundAmount** subtracted by any withholdings on the order (specified through the **totalWithholdingAmount** container) and any applicable credits (fee credits, donation credits, etc.).
  """
  netRefundAmount: AmountSet!
  """
  This array returns a list of pricelines that are being refunded by seller.
  """
  refundPriceLines: [PriceLineRollup!]!
  """
  The total amount credited for the seller. If this container is returned 'null', there are no additional credits applied to refund.
  """
  totalCreditAmount: AmountSet
  """The total monetary amount being refunded by the seller."""
  totalRefundAmount: AmountSet!
  """
  The total withholding amount applied on the refund by the seller. If this container is returned 'null', there are no additional withholdings applied to refund.
  """
  totalWithholdingAmount: AmountSet
  """This array returns a list of withholding made on the order by seller."""
  withholdings: [RefundWithholding!]
}

"""
This interface defines the type of seller refund credit, along with the amount credited.
"""
interface SellerRefundCredit {
  """The monetary amount credited to the seller."""
  creditAmount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable name for all the seller refund credits intended for consumption by an end user. Valid values include: 
  - 'FEE_CREDIT'
  - 'DONATION_CREDIT'
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type represents a seller's refund estimation breakdown and provides details about refund estimate for sellers including details like what seller gets charged on the contract.
**Note**: This type provides only the seller pricelines and refund amount that seller received as part contract fulfillment, and doesn't include pricelines such as 'TAX' or 'SERVICE_FEE' which seller didn't receive in the first place.
"""
type SellerRefundEstimateBreakdown implements RefundEstimateBreakdown {
  """
  This array returns a list of all types of credits applied for the seller, including:
     - **Total Fee credits**: In some instances, marketplaces fees charged are credited to the seller.
     - **Total Donation credits**: In some instances, the donation of sale proceeds are credited back with the refund.
     **Note**: Donations are not always credited back if the proceeds was already donated. 
  If this array is returned 'null', no additional credits are applied to the refund.
  """
  estimatedCredits: [SellerRefundCredit!]
  """
  This array returns a list of withholdings that can be applied on the contract by the seller. If this array is empty, no additional withholdings have been applied on refund.
  """
  estimatedWithholdings: [RefundWithholding!]!
  """
  The estimated net refund amount. This value is derived using following formula: **netEstimatedRefundAmount** = **totalEstimatedRefundAmount** - **totalEstimatedWithholdingAmount** - **estimatedCredits**
  """
  netEstimatedRefundAmount: AmountSet!
  """
  This array returns a list of pricelines that are being refunded by seller.
  """
  refundPriceLines: [PriceLineRollup!]!
  """
  The total amount estimated as credits to the seller. 
  **Note:** If this container is returned 'null', no additional credits been applied for refund estimation.
  """
  totalEstimatedCreditAmount: AmountSet
  """The estimated total monetary refund amount for the seller."""
  totalEstimatedRefundAmount: AmountSet!
  """
  The total estimated withholding amount, if there are any withholdings applied on the refund by the seller.
  **Note:** If this container is returned 'null', no withholding amount has been applied for refund estimation.
  """
  totalEstimatedWithholdingAmount: AmountSet
}

"""This type provides details on how the seller is funding a refund."""
type SellerRefundFunding implements PayerRefundFunding {
  """
  This array returns a list of funding execution details associated with the refund.
  """
  fundingExecutions: [RefundFundingExecution!]
  """This container returns the funding state of the refund."""
  fundingState: RefundFundingState!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **sellerReturnPreference** query, which indicates the marketplaces for a seller's return preferences operations (retrieve or publish).
"""
input SellerReturnPreferenceInput {
  """
  This enumerated value indicates the Marketplace. If omitted, the default value is used. 
    
  **Default**: `EBAY_US`
  """
  listingMarketplace: ListingMarketplace! = EBAY_US
}

"""
This base response union type for the **sellerReturnPreference** query includes the result of the query and any errors encountered. 
Additional error types may be added to this union.
"""
union SellerReturnPreferenceOutput = ReturnPreferenceNotFoundError | SellerReturnPreferences

"""
This type defines return preferences that a seller configures to automate their return workflow. These preferences apply to **listings published** on a specific marketplace. Each marketplace maintains its own independent set of preferences. The options available to sellers vary depending on marketplace capabilities and policies.
"""
type SellerReturnPreferences {
  """
  This enumerated value indicates the marketplace where the item is **listed/published** (for example, EBAY_US, EBAY_DE, EBAY_UK). All listings published on this marketplace inherit these preferences.
  """
  listingMarketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """This object indicates the seller's automation preferences."""
  returnAutomationPreference: ReturnAutomationPreference @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.return&eBayUser"])
  """
  This optional field indicates whether a Return Merchandise Authorization (RMA) number must be included on the return label. It is returned only when the seller's RMA preference applies to the specified marketplace:
  - `true`: The RMA number is required on the return label
  - `false`: The RMA number is not required on the return label
  """
  rmaPreference: RmaPreference
}

"""
This interface provides the state of an automation return rule. `ENABLED` rules are active and evaluated; `DISABLED` rules are ignored.
"""
interface SellerReturnRuleStatus {
  """
  Status of the rule. Only rules with the status `ENABLED` are executed.
  Available values: `ENABLED`, `DISABLED`
  """
  code: String!
  """
     A human readable rule status. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
     
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
Filter criteria to apply when searching for a seller's scheduled listings. When multiple filters are included, they are combined using a logical `AND` operation.

**Example:** Specify the following filters to return scheduled auction listings in the US or UK marketplace with the specified listing IDs:
```
{
listingIds: ["123", "456"]            # Results must match one of these IDs
marketplaces: [EBAY_US, EBAY_GB]      # AND be in one of these marketplaces
formatType: AUCTION                   # AND be auction format type
```
}
This filter combination returns listings with (listingId IN [123,456]) **AND** (marketplace IN [EBAY_US, EBAY_GB]) **AND** (formatType=AUCTION).
"""
input SellerScheduledListingSearchFilterInput {
  """
  Filter seller listings by their listing format type. Refer to `ListingFormatType` for supported values.
  """
  formatType: ListingFormatType
  """
  Filter seller listings by their listing IDs. When multiple listing ID values are provided, they are combined using a logical `OR` operation.
  
  **Note:** The maximum number of returned listings is 200. If more than 200 listings are identified `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  """
  listingIds: [ID!]
  """
  Filter seller listings by the eBay marketplace(s) in which the listings are created (e.g., EBAY_US, EBAY_GB, EBAY_DE). Refer to `ListingMarketplace` for a complete list of supported enumeration values.
  
  When multiple marketplaces are provided, they are combined using a logical `OR` operation. For example. `marketplaces [EBAY_US, EBAY_GB]` returns listings from the US **OR** UK marketplace.
  """
  marketplaces: [ListingMarketplace!]
  """
  Filter seller listings to return those listings that were modified within a specified date/time range. This filter requires both `startAt` and `endAt` values be specified, and returns those seller listings that have been modified between the specified `startAt` date/time (inclusive) and `endAt` date/time (inclusive).
  - If a `startAt` value or `endAt` value is omitted `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  - If both `startAt` and `endAt` values are omitted, no date range filtering is applied.
  """
  modifiedAtRange: SellerListingDateTimeRangeInput
  """
  Filter seller listings by their primary category ID. When multiple category ids are provided, they are combined using a logical `OR` operation.
  
  **Note:** The maximum number of returned listings is 50. If more than 50 listings are identified `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  """
  primaryCategoryIds: [ID!]
  """
  Filter seller listings by Stock Keeping Unit (SKU) values. An SKU is a seller-defined identifier that can be assigned when listing an item using **AddItem** and related calls. eBay preserves SKUs for items allowing users to access them before and after order line items are created.
  
  When multiple SKU values are provided, they are combined using a logical `OR` operation. For example, filtering seller listings using `skus ["SKU-1", "SKU-2"]` returns listings that exactly match SKU-1 **OR** SKU-2.
  
  **Notes:**
  - SKU filter values are case-senstive and must match an item's SKU exactly.
  - A single SKU may match multiple listings; SKUs are not required to be unique.
  - This filter returns all listings where the SKU exactly matches any value in the array.
  - The maximum number of returned listings is 200. If more than 200 listings are identified `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  
  **Maximum filter length:** 50 characters. If more than 50 characters are specified `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  """
  skus: [String!]
  """
  Filter seller listings to return those listing that are scheduled to become active within a specified date/time range. This filter requires both `startAt` and `endAt` values be specified, and returns those seller listings that are scheduled to become active between the specified `startAt` date/time (inclusive) and `endAt` date/time (inclusive).
  - If a `startAt` value or `endAt` value is omitted `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` is returned.
  - If both `startAt` and `endAt` values are omitted, no date-range filtering is applied.
  """
  startAtRange: SellerListingDateTimeRangeInput
}

"""
Criteria to apply when searching for a seller's scheduled listings. It is strongly recommended that criteria be specified in order to limit the number of listings returned. If no criteria are specified, the search will require more time and the request may timeout.
"""
input SellerScheduledListingSearchInput {
  """The filters to apply when searching for a seller's scheduled listings."""
  filters: SellerScheduledListingSearchFilterInput
  """
  Pagination information to control the number of listings returned, the number of pages of data to return, and the starting point.
  - The maximum number of pages of data to be returned is 200.
  - The maximum number of listings that can be retrieved is 50,000.
  
  To retrieve more than 50,000 records, apply additional filters to narrow the search or use date range filters to segment the queries.
  
  **Default Values:**
  - maxPageSize: 5
  - pageIndex: 0 (zero-indexed)
  
  **Constraints:**
  - maxPageSize <= 200
  - (maxPageSize * (pageIndex + 1)) <= 50,000
  
  Exceeding the above limit returns a `BAD_INPUT_VALUE` error in the response.
  """
  pagination: PaginationInput
  """
  Sort field and sort order to be applied to the search results. If not specified, by default the results will be sorted in ascending order by their respective `START_TIME`.
  """
  sort: SellerListingSortField
}

"""
This type represents a seller-defined shipping rate table. A rate table is a reusable configuration (managed in the seller's Shipping Preferences UI) that defines custom shipping costs by destination region, weight, or surcharge rules. Rate tables reference Region Graph region codes (canonical / ISO-3 style) to determine applicable locations — e.g. 'USA', 'CAN', 'GBR', 'EUROPEAN_UNION', 'WORLDWIDE'. For example:
- $5 to contiguous US (regionCode: 'USA'), $10 to AK/HI, $15 to PR.
- $20 to Canada (regionCode: 'CAN'), $30 to EU (regionCode: 'EUROPEAN_UNION').
"""
type SellerShippingRateTable {
  """
  The display name of the rate table
  **Format**: alphanumeric, spaces allowed
  **Maximum length**: 100 characters
  """
  name: String!
  """The unique numeric identifier of the shipping rate table."""
  shippingRateTableId: ID!
}

"""
This enumeration type contains a list of enum values that cover large geographical regions as well as specific regions within a country. Some of these values can be used as both ship-to or excluded shipping locations in an eBay listing, and some can only be used for one or the other. 
"""
enum SellerShippingRegionCode {
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Adelaide Metro area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  ADELAIDE_METRO
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a US-based seller will not ship to the states of Alaska or Hawaii.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay US listing.
  """
  ALASKA_HAWAII
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to North America and South America.
  **Note**: This enumeration value does not include Central America, which is grouped together with the Caribbean.
  """
  AMERICAS
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a US-based seller will not ship to Army Post Office (APO) or a Fleet Post Office (FPO).
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay US listing.
  """
  APO_FPO
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Brisbane Metro area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  BRISBANE_METRO
  """
  This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to countries in Central America and in the Caribbean.
  """
  CENTRAL_AMERICA_AND_CARIBBEAN
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to the Channel Islands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  CHANNEL_ISLANDS
  """
  This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to European countries that belong to the European Union.
  """
  EUROPEAN_UNION
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Hong Kong-based seller will or will not ship to the Greater China area, which includes mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macau.
  **Note**: This value can only be used in an eBay Hong Kong listing.
  """
  GREATER_CHINA
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Germany-based seller will not ship to the German island of Hiddensee.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Germany listing.
  """
  HIDDENSEE
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to the Isle of Wight.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  ISLE_OF_WIGHT
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Melbourne Metro area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  MELBOURNE_METRO
  """
  This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to the Middle East, which includes Turkey, Yemen, Oman, United Arab Emirates, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Iraq, Israel, Kuwait, Lebanon, Jordan, and Bahrain.
  """
  MIDDLE_EAST
  """
  This enumeration value is used if the seller does not ship the item. This value is applicable for listings that only support local pickup or for an item where the buyer is responsible for arranging shipping.
  """
  NONE
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Germany-based seller will not ship to the North Frisian Islands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Germany listing.
  """
  NORDFRIESISCHE_INSELN
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to Northern Ireland.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  NORTHERN_IRELAND
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Northern Territory region.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  NORTHERN_TERRITORY
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the New South Wales (NSW) region.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  NSW_REGIONAL
  """
  This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to countries/islands located in Oceania, which includes New Zealand, Micronesia, Fiji, Papua New Guinea, Solomon Islands, Marshall Islands, Nauru, Wallis and Futuna, Western Samoa, Tonga, Tuvalu, Vanuatu, Kiribati, New Caledonia, Palau, American Samoa, Niue, French Polynesia, Cook Islands, Guam, and Australia.
  """
  OCEANIA
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Germany-based seller will not ship to the East Frisian Islands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Germany listing.
  """
  OSTFRIESISCHE_INSELN
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Germany-based seller will not ship to a Packstation, which is an automated DHL parcel locker system.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Germany listing.
  """
  PACK_STATION
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Perth Metro area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  PERTH_METRO
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will not ship to a Post Office (PO) Box.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in a listing across all eBay marketplaces.
  """
  PO_BOX
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to Far North Queensland (QLD).
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  QLD_FAR_NORTH
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to regions of Queensland (QLD) beside Far North Queensland and South East Queensland.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  QLD_REGIONAL
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to South East Queensland (QLD).
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  QLD_SOUTH_EAST
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Hong Kong-based seller will or will not ship to Asian countries outside of the Greater China area, which includes mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macau.
  **Note**: This value can only be used in an eBay Hong Kong listing.
  """
  REST_OF_ASIA
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to Regional South Australia (SA).
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  SA_REGIONAL
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to the Scilly Isles (also known as Isles of Scilly).
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  SCILLY_ISLES
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to the Scottish Highlands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  SCOTTISH_HIGHLANDS
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a UK-based seller will not ship to the Scottish Islands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay UK listing.
  """
  SCOTTISH_ISLANDS
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a seller will or will not ship to Southeast Asia, which includes Cambodia, Indonesia, Vietnam, Hong Kong, Philippines, Malaysia, Taiwan, Laos, Thailand, Singapore, Macau, and Brunei Darussalam.
  **Note**: This value should not be used by a Hong Kong-based seller. Instead, they should use GREATER_CHINA (which includes mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Macau) and REST_OF_ASIA to include or exclude other Asian countries.
  """
  SOUTHEAST_ASIA
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the Sydney Metro area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  SYDNEY_METRO
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to the island state of Tasmania .
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  TASMANIA
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a US-based seller will not ship to any of the following US protectorates: Puerto Rico, Guam, American Samoa, Northern Mariana Islands, and U.S. Virgin Islands.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay US listing.
  """
  US_PROTECTORATES
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to Regional Victoria, which are areas of the Australian state of Victoria outside the greater Melbourne metropolitan area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  VIC_REGIONAL
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to Regional Western Australia (WA), which are areas outside the greater Perth metropolitan area.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  WA_REGIONAL
  """
     This enumeration value is used to indicate that a Australia-based seller will not ship to Remote Western Australia (WA), which are isolated areas far from major cities, especially in the north and northeast.
  **Note**: This value can only be used as an excluded shipping location in an eBay Australia listing.
  """
  WA_REMOTE
  """
     This enumeration value is used as a shipping location, and covers all continents, large geographical regions, countries, and special domestic locations.
  **Note**: It is generally accompanied by numerous excluded shipping locations unless a seller truly ships everywhere.
  """
  WORLDWIDE
}

"""
This type provides detailed information about a seller's store, including its name and url.
"""
type SellerStore {
  """
  This field is the public-facing name of the seller's store. If the seller does not own a store, this field will be null.
    
  **Format:** String of alphanumeric characters.
    
  **Maximum length:** 35 characters
  """
  name: String @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.stores.readonly&eBayUser"])
  """
    The fully-qualified URL of the seller's storefront. This URL uniquely identifies the seller's store and is required for storefront access. If a seller does not have a store this field will be empty.
    
    **URL Format:** https://{domain}/str/{storeUrlIdentifier} where:
    - `{domain}` is determined by the seller's registration site ID
    - `{storeUrlIdentifier}` is a unique, alphanumeric identifier for the store with a maximum length of 35 characters.
        **Notes:**
  - Although this string may be the same as the store's `name` it is not required to be the same.
  - Spaces must be encoded as `%20`.
    
    **Maximum length:** 2048 characters
  """
  url: String @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.stores.readonly&eBayUser"])
}

"""
Represents an eBay Store subscription plan purchased or enrolled by a seller.
Each subscription grants the seller access to the associated plan's benefits,
such as listing allowances, premium tools, and enhanced selling features.
"""
type SellerSubscriptionPlan {
  """
  The subscription plan type enrolled by the seller.
  Identifies the specific tier or product that determines the features, benefits, and allowances available to the seller.
  """
  planType: SellerSubscriptionPlanType!
}

"""
eBay Store subscription plan types available to sellers.
Represents different Store subscription tiers that provide ongoing access to enhanced selling features,
listing allowances, and premium tools.
"""
enum SellerSubscriptionPlanType {
  """
  Anchor store subscription tier.
  Comprehensive marketing tools and priority support.
  """
  EBAY_STORE_ANCHOR
  """
  Basic store subscription tier.
  Enhanced listing allowances and store customization features.
  """
  EBAY_STORE_BASIC
  """
  Enterprise store subscription tier.
  Maximum listing allowances and advanced features for high-volume sellers.
  """
  EBAY_STORE_ENTERPRISE
  """
  Featured store subscription tier.
  Premium placement options and advanced selling tools.
  """
  EBAY_STORE_FEATURED
  """
  Starter store subscription tier.
  Entry-level subscription providing basic store features and listing allowances.
  """
  EBAY_STORE_STARTER
}

"""
This enumeration type contains the values that indicate the block of days when a classified ad seller can be contacted by potential buyers to answer questions about an item.
"""
enum SellerSupportListingDaysCode {
  EVERYDAY
  WEEKDAYS
  WEEKENDS
}

"""
This type is used to provide more information when the 'Seller to Vault' fulfillment type is used to deliver the item to the buyer. With 'Seller to Vault' fulfillment, the seller ships the item to the PSA Vault, where the trading card will be authenticated before it is sent to the buyer.  
"""
type SellerToVault implements Labeled {
  """A human-readable label for the entity."""
  label: String!
}

"""
This type represents an amount being withheld by the seller due to issues when the item was exchanged back.
"""
type SellerWithholding implements RefundWithholding {
  """The monetary amount being withheld from the refund."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The name of the withholding.
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SELLER_DEDUCTION'.	
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This interface represents input violations detected during send return message request evaluation. Each violation indicates that the provided input value did not comply with the business rules or constraints defined for sending return message, such as exceeding the maximum allowed characters for the message. Such constraints are governed by eBay's return policies, and may vary based on context, marketplace, or configuration.
"""
interface SendMessageInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific send return message input violation.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the send return message input violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This action type is used for sending a message in a return conversation between the buyer and the seller.
"""
type SendMessageReturnAction implements ReturnAction {
  """A machine-readable return action code: `SEND_MESSAGE`"""
  code: String!
  """
  Human readable text for send message return action. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This input type is used for sending a message in a inquiry conversation. This type can be used to add communication between buyer and seller regarding a inquiry.
"""
input SendOrderInquiryMessageInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the inquiry for which to send the message. 
  **Note:** This must be a valid inquiry that the user has access to.
  """
  inquiryId: ID!
  """
  The text content of the message to send.
  **Minimum length**: 1 character
  **Maximum length**: 500 characters
  """
  message: String!
}

"""
This type represents a business error that is returned when one or more validation errors occurs while sending a message in an order inquiry.
"""
type SendOrderInquiryMessageInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier for this specific error type - 'INQRY_SEND_MESSAGE_VALIDATION_ERROR'
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  The human-readable error message describing the issue. 
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """This array returns details about the specific request violations."""
  violations: [SendOrderInquiryMessageInputViolation!]!
}

"""
This interface represents that input violation(s) were detected while evaluating order inquiry message sending. Each violation indicates that the provided message input value did not comply with the business rules or constraints defined for sending messages in order inquiries. These rules may include:
- Message text exceeding allowed length.
- Unsupported attachment type.
- Missing mandatory message content.
"""
interface SendOrderInquiryMessageInputViolation {
  """
  The machine-readable code identifying the specific message input violation.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable message describing the message input violation. 
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
The union type for the **sendOrderInquiryMessage** mutation. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **sendOrderInquiryMessage** mutation succeeds, the order inquiry message will be sent. If the **sendOrderInquiryMessage** mutation fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the item commitment will not be created. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error.
"""
union SendOrderInquiryMessageOutput = OrderInquiryActionNotPermittedError | OrderInquiryNotFoundError | SendOrderInquiryMessageInputValidationError | SendOrderInquiryMessageSuccess

"""The output type for the **sendOrderInquiryMessage** mutation."""
type SendOrderInquiryMessageSuccess {
  """The result of the **sendOrderInquiryMessage** operation."""
  orderInquiry: OrderInquiry!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **sendReturnMessage** mutation provides fields for responding to an existing message in a conversation, which provides communication between buyer and seller regarding a return.
"""
input SendReturnMessageInput {
  """
  The reply text to include. The message is stored as provided and not localized.
    
  **Minimum length:** 1 character
  **Maximum length:** 500 characters
  """
  message: String!
  """
  The unique identifier of the Return which to send a message. This must be a valid return ID that the user has permission to access.
  """
  returnId: ID!
}

"""
This error type indicates that one or more validation errors occurred while sending the return message.
"""
type SendReturnMessageInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """A machine-readable error code: `RTRN_SEND_MESSAGE_VALIDATION_ERROR.`"""
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable error message describing the issue.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains details about one or more specific request violations.
  """
  violations: [SendMessageInputViolation!]!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **sendReturnMessage** mutation includes the result of the mutation and any errors encountered.
"""
union SendReturnMessageOutput = OrderReturn | ReturnActionNotPermittedError | ReturnNotFoundError | SendReturnMessageInputValidationError

"""
The service was cancelled before completion. Cancellation may be the result
of user action, lack of resources, or other blocking conditions.
"""
type ServiceCancelled implements Labeled {
  """A human-readable label for the state (example: "Cancelled")."""
  label: String!
  """
  This field provides a text-based explanation of why the service was canceled. This optional field is returned if available.
  """
  reason: String
}

"""
The service has finished successfully. All required tasks for this service
are complete and no further action is required unless explicit follow-up is planned.
"""
type ServiceCompleted implements Labeled {
  """
  When `true`, there was unusual complexity involved in order to get the service completed.
  """
  complicated: Boolean!
  """A human-readable label for the state (example: "Completed")."""
  label: String!
  """
  When `true`, the final completed state required a modification to the original plan (for example: re-scheduling, additional steps, or scope changes).
  """
  modificationInvolved: Boolean!
}

"""This type provides details of a service execution attempt."""
type ServiceExecution {
  """
  This timestamp indicates when the service attempt was completed.
    
  **Note**: This field is only returned if the service attempt is in the completed state.
  """
  completedAt: DateTime
  """
  This container provides details on the current state of this specific service execution attempt.
  """
  serviceState: ServiceState!
  """This timestamp indicates when the service attempt began."""
  startedAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type is used to show the execution history and current status of service attempts.
"""
type ServiceExecutionList {
  """
  This array lists individual execution attempts for the service. Each entry represents a distinct attempt, including rescheduled appointments.
  """
  executions: [ServiceExecution!]!
  """
  This container shows details on the current state of the service (for example, completed, failed, or rescheduled).
  """
  serviceState: ServiceState!
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Service Fee."""
type ServiceFee implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SERVICE_FEE'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""This type defines the priceline roll up for service fee subtotal."""
type ServiceFeeSubtotal implements PriceLineRollup {
  """
  The monetary amount of the priceline rollup. This is the monetary value associated with the priceline item group
  """
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable name of the priceline roll up. 
  **Note**: In this context, the name will always be returned as 'SERVICE_FEE_SUBTOTAL'.
  """
  name: String!
  """This array returns the pricelines that are part of the rollup."""
  priceLines: [PriceLine!]!
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Service Fee Tax."""
type ServiceFeeTax implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SERVICE_FEE_TAX'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type is used to provide details of a service that is actively being executed.
"""
type ServiceInProgress implements Labeled {
  """
  When `true`, there is unusual complexity involved in order to get the service to the next state. 
  """
  complicated: Boolean!
  """
  This value indicates the current state of the service (for example, `InProgress`).
  """
  label: String!
}

"""
This type is used to provide details of a service that has been partially completed.
"""
type ServicePartiallyCompleted implements Labeled {
  """
  When `true`, the completed portion involved complex work or special handling.
  """
  complicated: Boolean!
  """
  A human-readable label for the state (for example, `PartiallyCompleted).
  """
  label: String!
}

"""
This type is used to provide details of a service that has been partially started.
"""
type ServicePartiallyStarted implements Labeled {
  """
  When `true`, the started portion of the service is complex and may affect completion or downstream steps.
  """
  complicated: Boolean!
  """
  A human-readable label for the state (for example, `PartiallyStarted`).
  """
  label: String!
}

"""
This type is used to show the scheduled date and time of a planned service appointment at the service-related logistics point.
"""
type ServicePlan {
  """
  The scheduled timestamp for the planned service appointment, such as tire installation.
  """
  scheduledAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type is used to convey information about a service-related logistics point involved in a fulfillment plan. An example of this would be tires being sent to a tire installer company for tires to get installed on the buyer's vehicle.
"""
type ServicePoint implements LogisticsPoint {
  """
  The physical address associated with this service-related logistics point.
  """
  address: PurchaseAddress
  """
  The user-friendly name of the service-related logistics point (for example, 'Service Center').
  """
  name: String!
  """
  This container shows service-specific details associated with this service-related logistics point. The type and amount of data shown here will vary based on the details that are known and available.
  """
  serviceDetails: ServicePointInfo!
  """
  The functional role of the service-related logistics point in the logistics flow (for example, 'SERVICE_SITE', 'CUSTOMER_HOME').
  """
  type: DisplayableId!
}

"""
This union type is used by the **ServicePlan** and **ServiceExecutionList** types to provide details about a service-related logistics plan. 
"""
union ServicePointInfo = ServiceExecutionList | ServicePlan

"""
This union type is used to provide the current state of a service-related line item. This type is used by services in all states. 
"""
union ServiceState = ServiceCancelled | ServiceCompleted | ServiceInProgress | ServicePartiallyCompleted | ServicePartiallyStarted

"""
This type represents a step in a service workflow connecting a participant (such as a buyer or carrier) to a `ServicePoint` for the service action (for example, dropping off, picking up, or transferring an item). This type describes the interaction leading to the service, not the service itself.
"""
type ServiceStep implements LogisticsStep {
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the party responsible for handling this logistics step.
  """
  handler: DisplayableId
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the logistics step. For example, `Buyer Drop Off` or `Carrier Pick Up`.
  """
  methodName: DisplayableId!
  """
  This container shows the service point where this step leads to or occurs representing the physical or operational location of the service interaction.
  """
  servicePoint: ServicePoint!
}

"""
This type represents the request for shipment tracking information, such as tracking number and carrier details.
"""
type ShipmentTrackingInformationRequested implements OrderInquiryInformationRequested {
  """
  The timestamp when the shipping tracking information request was created.
  """
  requestedAt: DateTime!
  """The actor who initiated the shipping tracking information request."""
  requester: PostPurchaseActorRole!
}

"""
This type represents the reason used by seller when there are issues with the buyer's shipping address.
"""
type ShippingAddressIssuesCancellation implements ContractCancellationReason {
  """
  The unique cancellation reason code for this use case. For this type, the value is `SHIPPING_ADDRESS_ISSUES`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the cancellation reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This container captures shipping policy details, as well as any overrides for the shipping policy
"""
type ShippingBusinessPolicy {
  """Provides generic business policy details for this policy"""
  businessPolicy: BusinessPolicy
  """
  This field is used to override the shipping costs for marketplace and non-marketplace shipping service options defined in the fulfillment terms being used for the listing.
    
  This should not be null unless an error has occurred. Please see the error section of the response for more details
  """
  overrideShippingOptions: [OverrideShippingOptions!]
}

"""
This type represents the shipping carrier details associated with a shipment or return. This type provides both the eBay-standard carrier code and, if applicable, the user-provided carrier name when the carrier is not officially supported by eBay Marketplace.
"""
type ShippingCarrier {
  """
  The eBay-standard code representing the shipping carrier. This value corresponds to one of the supported eBay `CarrierCodes`.
  **Note:** The special value `UNSUPPORTED` indicates that eBay does not officially support or recognize the provided carrier.
  """
  carrierCode: String!
  """
  The carrier name provided by the user when eBay does not recognize the carrier.
  **Note: **This field is populated only when **carrierCode** is `UNSUPPORTED`.
  """
  unsupportedCarrierName: String
}

"""This type provides carrier tracking information for a shipment."""
type ShippingCarrierTracking {
  """
  The standardized carrier name associated with the forward and return shipment, examples can include UPS, USPS, and FEDEX.
  """
  shippingCarrier: ShippingCarrier!
  """
  The tracking number for the return shipment, if the label is provided by seller. This is  a common use case for some carriers in certain geographies.
  """
  trackingNumber: String
}

"""This type indicates that the shipment was delivered."""
type ShippingDelivered implements ShippingTrackingStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code representing the current state of the shipment as `DELIVERED`.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """A human-readable description of the shipment tracking status."""
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type is used to provide details on a single shipping execution event, either completed or in progress.
"""
type ShippingExecution {
  """
  This timestamp indicates when the shipment was delivered to the destination. This field is returned if the item has been delivered.
  """
  deliveredAt: DateTime
  """This array lists the line items packaged in the shipment."""
  lineItemReferences: [LineItemReference!]
  """
  This timestamp indicates when the shipment was sent from the origin. This field is returned if the item has been shipped.
  """
  shippedAt: DateTime
  """The name of the shipping carrier handling this shipment."""
  shippingCarrier: String
  """
  This container shows the current state of fulfillment that this shipping execution event is contributing towards.
  """
  shippingState: LogisticsFulfillmentState!
  """
  The shipment tracking number assigned by the shipping carrier. This field is returned if available.
  """
  trackingNumber: String
  """
  This timestamp indicates when tracking information was first made available.
  """
  trackingProvidedAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type provides details about a shipping step in progress, and includes the shipping step state and the list of executions associated with this shipping step.
"""
type ShippingExecutionList {
  """
  This array shows the list of executions associated with this shipping step. Each entry describes a separate fulfillment event.
  """
  executions: [ShippingExecution!]!
  """
  This container shows the current state of fulfillment that this shipping step is contributing towards.
  """
  shippingState: LogisticsFulfillmentState!
}

"""
This type is used to indicate the date and time that the seller should wait for before proceeding with fulfillment. 
"""
type ShippingFulfillmentHoldDetails {
  """
  The date and time until which the seller should hold the fulfillment before proceeding.
  """
  holdUntil: DateTime!
}

"""
This type defines the seller's shipping configuration for a shipping policy, including shipping calculation type, available services, rate tables, discounts, and free shipping eligibility.
"""
type ShippingFulfillmentOptions {
  """
  The shipping services configured in the seller's Business Policies for this shipping policy and includes service-level details and handling costs.
  """
  BusinessPolicyShippingServices: [BusinessPolicyShippingServiceDetails]
  """
  This field is the unique identifier of a seller's domestic or international shipping discount profile. If a buyer satisfies the requirements of the discount rule, this buyer will receive a shipping discount for the order. The seller can create and manage shipping discount profiles using (Get/Set) **ShippingDiscountProfiles** calls in the Trading API or through Shipping Preferences in **My eBay**. Can be null when no discount profile is configured. 
  
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  combinedShippingRuleId: ID
  """
  This field indicates whether the seller offers free domestic shipping as the primary domestic shipping service option. This applies to only the first domestic shipping service in **shippingServices** array in the **ShippingFulfillmentOptions** type (it is ignored if set for subsequent shipping services or for any international shipping service option). 
  The first specified shipping service option has a **sortOrder** value of `1` or if the **sortOrderId** field is not used, it is the shipping service option that's specified first in the **shippingServices** array.
  - `true`: Free shipping is offered
  - `false` Free shipping is not offered
  
  **Note:** Free shipping only applies to domestic shipping. 
  
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  freeShippingAvailable: Boolean
  """
  This boolean indicates whether or not the seller has set up a promotional shipping discount that will be available to buyers who satisfy the requirements of the shipping discount rule. The seller can create and manage shipping promotional discounts using (Get/Set) **ShippingDiscountProfiles** calls in the **Trading API** or through Shipping Preferences in **My eBay**.
  - `true`: Promotional shipping discount is offered
  - `false`: No promotional shipping discount is available
  
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  promotionalShipping: Boolean
  """
  This ID is the domestic or international shipping rate table associate with the fulfillment policy. The <a href="https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables" target="_blank">getRateTables</a> method can be used to retrieve shipping rate table IDs. With domestic and international shipping rate tables, the seller can set different shipping costs based on shipping regions and shipping speed/level of service (one-day, expedited, standard, economy). There are also options to add additional per-weight and handling charges. May be null when no rate table is used.
  
  **Note:** Also see <a href="https://www.ebay.com/ship/rt" target="_blank">Shipping rate tables</a> in **My eBay**.
  
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  shippingRateTableId: ID
  """
  This enumerated value specifies how shipping costs are calculated for this shipping policy (for example, flat-rate shipping or calculated shipping).
  """
  shippingType: LogisticsOptionType
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Shipping Handling Price."""
type ShippingHandlingPrice implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'DOMESTIC_HANDLING_PRICE'.
  """
  name: String!
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Shipping Handling Tax."""
type ShippingHandlingTax implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SHIPPING_HANDLING_TAX'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""This type indicates the shipment tracking status is in transit."""
type ShippingInTransit implements ShippingTrackingStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the current state of the shipment as `IN_TRANSIT`.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """A human-readable description of the shipment tracking status."""
  displayText: String!
}

"""
Represents a snapshot of the item for which the shipping label was created.
"""
type ShippingLabelItem {
  """
  The carrier associated with this shipping label (e.g., USPS, FedEx, UPS, DHL).
  """
  carrier: String!
  """
  the level or type of shipping service provided by a carrier (like USPS, FedEx, UPS, DHL, etc.).
  It determines how fast the package is delivered, what features are included (like tracking or insurance), and how much it costs.
  it could be null if not provided. e.g. MSP_TRK_48_DRP_OFF
  """
  shippingService: String
  """The tracking number assigned to this shipment."""
  trackingNumber: String!
}

"""
This type specifies the geographic locations and identifies a country or continent and regions, for various listing purposes such as shipping exclusions and inclusions.
"""
type ShippingLocation {
  """
  Identify by continent using a predefined set of continent codes. See the **ContinentCode** enum for the full list of supported continent codes.
  """
  continent: ContinentCode
  """
  Identify by country using the ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code standard.
  See the [`ISOAlpha2CountryCode`] enum for the full list of supported country codes.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  Identify by a specify a geographic region not covered by country or continent codes.
  """
  sellerShippingRegion: SellerShippingRegionCode
}

"""
This type shows details of a shipping logistics option, including the shipping service code, shipping carrier code, and shipping cost.
"""
type ShippingLogisticsOption implements PurchaseQuoteLogisticsOption {
  """
  This container shows the cost of the shipping logistics option. If the shipping logistics option is free to the buyer, this container will show a value of '0.0'.  
  **Note**: If the authenticated user uses a different currency than the default currency used by the eBay marketplace, this amount will also be shown in that user's currency.
  """
  cost: AmountSet!
  """The display name of the shipping logistics option."""
  displayName: String!
  """
  The uniqe identifier of the shipping carrier.
  **Examples**: USPS, UPS, DHL
  """
  shippingCarrierCode: ID
  """
  The uniqe identifier of the shipping service option.
  **Example**: UK_RoyalMailSecondClassStandard
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify one shipping logistics option that is provided by the seller.
"""
input ShippingLogisticsOptionInput {
  """
  This container is used to specify the shipping cost to ship the order if the shipping service option specified in the corresponding **shippingServiceCode** field is used. To offer a shipping service option as free to the buyer, the value of this field is set to '0.0'.  
  **Note**: The default currency of the eBay listing marketplace should be used.
  """
  cost: AmountInput!
  """
  The enumeration value associated with the shipping service. In listing and Business Policy APIs, the enumeration values of shipping services are specified to set the shipping services that are available to ship the item. 
  **Example**: UK_RoyalMailSecondClassStandard
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID!
}

"""
This type provides information on domestic and international shipping, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated) and the shipping service options available to ship the item.
"""
type ShippingOptionDetails {
  """
  This field indicates the shipping cost type used for domestic or international shipping. Shipping cost types include flat-rate and calculated.
  """
  shippingCostType: ListingShippingCostType
  """
  Shipping Preference applied by the seller which includes ratetable, discount rule and promotional discount
  """
  shippingPreference: SellerAppliedShippingPreference
}

"""
This type provides information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions.
"""
type ShippingPackageSpec {
  """
  This boolean field indicates whether or not the shipping package is an irregular or non-standard shape. A shipping carrier may charge additional handling fees for an irregular package.
  """
  irregularPackage: Boolean
  """
  The enumeration value returned in this field indicates the type of package used to ship the item.
  """
  listingPackageType: ListingPackageType
  """
  The measurement system used by the eBay marketplace for the package dimensions and weight.
  """
  listingUnitOfMeasure: MeasurementSystem
  """
  This container is used to specify the dimensions of the shipping package and the unit of measurement used.
  """
  packageDimensions: ListingPackageDimensions
  """
  This container is used to specify the weight of the shipping package and the unit of measurement used to measure weight.
  """
  packageWeight: ListingPackageWeight
}

"""
This type provides details about a planned shipping step prior to execution.
"""
type ShippingPlan {
  """
  This container is returned if there is a hold on the shipping step, and indicates when the hold is expected to be released
  """
  shippingHoldDetail: ShippingFulfillmentHoldDetails
}

"""
This union type is used by the **ShippingPlan** type to provide details about a planned shipping step and by the **ShippingExecutionList** type to provide details about a shipping step in progress.
"""
union ShippingPlanOrExecution = ShippingExecutionList | ShippingPlan

"""
This type is used to convey information about a shipping logistics point involved in a fulfillment plan. 
"""
type ShippingPoint implements LogisticsPoint {
  """The physical address associated with this logistics node."""
  address: PurchaseAddress
  """
  The user-friendly name of the shipping logistics point. (for example, 'San Jose Warehouse', 'Customer Home').
  """
  name: String!
  """
  The functional role of the node in the logistics flow (e.g., 'WAREHOUSE', 'CUSTOMS', 'DESTINATION').
  """
  type: DisplayableId!
}

"""
This type provides shipping-specific details for a seller's shipping policy, including if the policy applies to motor vehicles, available domestic and international shipping options, ship-to exclusions and inclusions, handling time, and participation in special programs such as eBay's Global Shipping Program (GSP) or freight.
"""
type ShippingPolicyDetails {
  """
  This field is applicable for motor vehicle listings. When set to `true` for a motor vehicle listing this indicates that it will be the buyer's responsibility to arrange for shipment of the motor vehicle. May be null when not applicable.
  - `true`: The buyer is responsible for shipping costs/arrangements 
  - `false`: The seller is responsible for shipping costs. 
  
  **Note:** In the majority of motor vehicle listings, the seller does make the buyer responsible for pickup or shipment of the vehicle.
  
  **Default value:** `false`
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  buyerResponsibleForShipping: Boolean
  """
  This object contains shipping options for domestic deliveries under this policy. May be null or empty if domestic shipping is not offered or specified.
  """
  domesticShippingOptions: ShippingFulfillmentOptions
  """
  This field indicates whether the item is eligible for **Click and Collect**. This is currently available only to large retail merchants in the eBay AU, UK, DE, FR, and IT marketplaces. If returned as `true`, local pickup is also available for this policy.
  - `true`: The item is eligible for **Click and Collect**
  - `false`: The item is not eligible 
  
  **Occurrence:** Always
  """
  eligibleForPickupDropOff: Boolean
  """
  This array lists shipping locations where the seller does not ship under this policy. The location may be countries, regions, states or provinces, or marketplace defined domestic regions. The supported eBay marketplace location codes are marketplace specific.
  - May be empty if no locations are configured
  - Values are not localized
  
  **Example:** `["AFG","ALB","DZA","ASM","AND","AGO","AIA"]`
  """
  excludedShipToLocations: [ShippingLocation!]
  """
  This field applies only for the eBay United Kingdom marketplace (EBAY_GB). If returned as true, **eBay's Global Shipping Program** will be used by the seller to ship items to international locations. All other sites should return `false` for this field.
  
  **Occurrence:** Always
  """
  globalShippingProgramParticipant: Boolean
  """
  The maximum number of business days the seller commits to for preparing and shipping an order after the order is placed. This time does not include the transit time it takes the shipping carrier to deliver the order. If only local pickup or freight shipping is available for the item, this value may not get returned. May be null when not applicable or not specified.
  
  **Occurrence:** Conditional
  """
  handlingTime: Int
  """
  This array lists shipping locations where the seller ships to under this policy. The location may be countries, regions, states or provinces, or marketplace defined domestic regions. Each eBay marketplace supports its own set of allowable shipping locations. 
  - May be empty if no locations are configured
  - Values are not localized
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ShippingLocation!]
  """
  This object contains shipping options for  international deliveries under this policy. May be null or empty if international shipping is not offered or specified.
  """
  internationalShippingOptions: ShippingFulfillmentOptions
  """
  Indicates whether this policy is for motor vehicle listings.
  - `true`: Motor vehicle shipping policy (applies to motor vehicle listings)
  - `false` Standard shipping policy (applies to non-motor vehicle listings)
  
  **Occurrence:** Always
  """
  motorVehiclePolicy: Boolean
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Shipping Price."""
type ShippingPrice implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SHIPPING_PRICE'.   
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type represents input violations related to shipping price refund withholding. It indicates that the seller attempted to withhold the shipping cost when it is not allowed.
"""
type ShippingPriceRefundWithholdViolation implements ProcessReturnRefundInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific rule that was violated (for example. `SHIPPING_PRICE_REFUND_WITHHOLD_VIOLATION`).
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the rule violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This type represents input violations related to partial refund shipping price. This indicates that the seller attempted to waive the shipping price when it is not allowed.
"""
type ShippingPriceWaiverViolation implements ProposeKeepItemWithPartialRefundInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific rule that was violated (for example, `SHIPPING_PRICE_WAIVER_VIOLATION`).
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the rule violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This type shows the list of domestic or international shipping service options that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is idenfied through the **shippingServiceOptionCode** field.
"""
type ShippingServiceDetails {
  """
  The cost of shipping each additional item if the same buyer purchases multiple quantity of the same line item. This field is required when creating a multiple-quantity, fixed-price listing.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCostAmount: ConvertedAmount
  """
  This array is the list of continents, geographical regions, and/or individual countries that the corresponding shipping service operates in.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ShippingLocation!]
  """
  This field shows any package handling cost applied to a shipping service. It is added on top of the shipping cost for each service option. A null value means no additional cost.
  """
  listingPackageHandlingCost: ConvertedAmount
  """
  An integer value that controls the order (relative to other shipping services) in which the corresponding ShippingService will appear in the View Item and Checkout page
  """
  rank: Int
  """
  The base cost of shipping one unit of the item using the shipping service specified in the corresponding Shipping Service field.
  """
  shippingCostAmount: ConvertedAmount
  """
  A shipping service option being offered by the seller to ship an item to a buyer.
  """
  shippingService: ListingShippingService
}

"""
This type convey details of a shipping logistics step involved in a fulfillment plan. 
"""
type ShippingStep implements LogisticsStep {
  """
  This container shows the estimated delivery window for the item going from the **shipFrom** to the **shipTo** location.
  """
  estimate: LogisticsFulfillmentEstimate
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the party responsible for handling this shipping logistics step.
  """
  handler: DisplayableId
  """
  This container shows the user-friendly description and unique identifier of the shipping logistics step. 
  """
  methodName: DisplayableId!
  """
  The information shown in this container is dependent on the state of the logistics step. If the logistics step has not yet started and there is no hold associated with the logistics step, it may get returned as empty or null. If the logistics step is active or completed, the state and full shipping details for this shipping step will be shown. 
  """
  planOrExecution: ShippingPlanOrExecution!
  """
  This container shows details on the ship-from location, including the user-friendly name, location type, and a full street address. May be null when data is not available.
  """
  shipFrom: LogisticsPoint
  """
  This container shows details on the ship-to location, including the user-friendly name, location type, and a full street address. 
  """
  shipTo: LogisticsPoint!
}

"""This type defines the priceline roll up for shipping subtotal."""
type ShippingSubtotal implements PriceLineRollup {
  """
  The monetary amount of the priceline rollup. This is the monetary value associated with the priceline item group
  """
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable name of the priceline roll up. 
  **Note**: In this context, the name will always be returned as 'SHIPPING_SUBTOTAL'.
  """
  name: String!
  """This array returns the pricelines that are part of the rollup."""
  priceLines: [PriceLine!]!
}

"""This type defines the priceline for Shipping Tax."""
type ShippingTax implements PriceLine {
  """The monetary value associated with the priceline item."""
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable priceline name. 
  **Note**: In this case, the name will always be returned as 'SHIPPING_TAX'.      
  """
  name: String!
}

"""
This type provides information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
"""
type ShippingTerms {
  """
  Indicates whether the buyer is responsible for vehicle shipping/pickup.
  """
  buyerResponsibleForShipping: Boolean
  """
  This array is used to indicate the locations where the seller will not ship the item. The values in this array can be contients, large geographical regions, countries, or special domestic locations. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  """
  excludedShipToLocations: [ShippingLocation!]
  """
  This field indicates how many business days that the seller needs to ship the item after payment is made by the buyer.
  The handling time is required for most categories. Top-rated sellers typically set the handling time to 0 or 1 day,
  but longer handling times are supported.
  """
  handlingTimeDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This array shows the list of locations where the seller will ship the item. The values in this array can be continents, large geographical regions, or countries. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations**vvvvcbefueuvdddftkvvjkhgfkndhjrdhgvbdvvdgbnh
  lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ShippingLocation!]
  """
  This container provides information on shipping options for locations within the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated)
  and the shipping service options available to ship the item.
  
  There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to apply a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not used business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  marketplaceShippingOptions: ShippingOptionDetails
  """
  This container provides information on shipping for locations outside of the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated)
  and the shipping service options available to ship the item.
  
  There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to apply a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not used business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  nonMarketplaceShippingOptions: ShippingOptionDetails
  """
  Business policy container for specifying shipping policy details, as well as any overrides for the shipping policy
  """
  shippingBusinessPolicy: ShippingBusinessPolicy
  """
  This array provides the list of shipping service options that are available to the
  buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one.
  
  Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
  
  **Maximum number of shipping services**: 10, out of which 5 apply for locations within the marketplace and other 5 apply for locations outside of marketplace
  
  This should never by an empty list, there needs to be at least one shipping service available
  
  This is null only if an error has occurred. See the error section of the response for more details
  """
  shippingServices: [ShippingServiceDetails!]
}

"""This interface indicates the shipment tracking status."""
interface ShippingTrackingStatus {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the return fulfillment status. Values can include `IN_TRANSIT`, `OUT_FOR_DELIVERY`, `DELIVERED`, `EXCEPTION`, and similar.
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric with underscores
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  code: String!
  """A human-readable description of the shipment tracking status."""
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This interface type defines a shipping zone, and typically consists of city, state, postal code, and country information for a user address.
"""
interface ShippingZone {
  """
  The two-letter ISO 3166 country code for the shipping zone.
  **Note:** This field may be omitted based on user access permissions
  """
  countryCode: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The postal code of the shipping zone.
  **Note:** This field may be omitted based on user access permissions
  """
  postalCode: String
  """
  The state or province of the shipping zone.
  **Note:** This field may be omitted based on user access permissions
  """
  stateOrProvince: String
}

"""
This type represents the request for proof of delivery information that includes signature confirmation details.
"""
type SignatureConfirmationRequested implements OrderInquiryInformationRequested {
  """
  The timestamp when the proof of delivery information request was created.
  """
  requestedAt: DateTime!
  """The actor who initiated the proof of delivery information request."""
  requester: PostPurchaseActorRole!
}

"""Entity representing a single SKU Listing. """
type SingleSkuListing implements ListingV2 {
  """
  Item that can be bundled as part of a listing.
    
  There will always be at least one item
  """
  items: [Item!]!
  """Id of a Listing."""
  listingId: ID!
  """
  This query will return all item commitments spawned from the corresponding listing, and meeting other search criteria.
  **Note**: The authenticated user (seller or buyer) must have a relationship to item commitments for them to be returned.
  **Note**: Other filters in addition to **listingId** may be used.
  """
  itemCommitments: ItemCommitments! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.commitment.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.commitment", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.commitment.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.commitment"])
  """Seller-scoped Unanswered questions count for the listing"""
  unansweredQuestions: UnansweredQuestions @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.listing.read"])
  """
  Entry point for the authenticated viewer’s order data **in the context of this listing**.
    
  Semantics:
  • Results are implicitly filtered to `listingId == this.listingId`.
  • For sellers: surfaces orders where the viewer is the seller of this listing.
  • For buyers: surfaces orders where the viewer purchased this listing.
    
  Behavior:
  • Clients may add filters/sort; the implicit `listingId` filter is always applied and
  should not be overrideable.
  • Requires authentication; if the viewer has no related orders, the lists are empty.
  """
  orders: Orders! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.order.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.order&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.order.read&eBayUser", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.order&eBayUser"])
  """
  This query will return all purchase quotes that involve this listing, and meeting other search criteria.
  **Note**: The authenticated user (seller or buyer) must have a relationship to purchase quote(s) for them to be returned.
  **Note**: Other filters in addition to **listingId** may be used.
  """
  purchaseQuotes: PurchaseQuotes! @authorize(scopes: ["https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.purchase.quote.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.purchase.quote.read", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/buy.purchase.quote", "https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope/sell.purchase.quote"])
  """
  Commercial terms such as location, shipping, returns, etc. that
  apply to every item in the listing unless overridden at the item level.
  The item level terms currently include sku, price, quantity, and extended producer responsibility (EPR) terms.
    
  This field will only be null if there is an error. Please see error section of response for more details.
    
  This should not be null unless an error has occurred. Please see the error section of the response for more details
  """
  listingTerms: ListingTerms
  """
  The unique identifier of the eBay marketplace where the listing is hosted.
  """
  marketplace: ListingMarketplace
  """
  Container for the seller product like epid, title, description, aspects, etc
  """
  sellerProduct: SellerProduct
}

"""
This error is returned when the number of Stock Keeping Units (SKUs) provided for the `sellerListingSearch` query exceeds the maximum allowed count.
"""
type SkusExceedMaxCountError implements SellerListingSearchInputError {
  """The actual number of Stock Keeping Units (SKUs) provided."""
  actualCount: Int!
  """
  Technical description of the error for developers and debugging purposes.
  """
  errorDescription: String!
  """The maximum number of Stock Keeping Units (SKUs) allowed."""
  maxAllowed: Int!
  """
  User-friendly suggestion on how to fix the error. This can be displayed to end users to help them correct their input.
  """
  remedy: String!
}

"""
This error is returned when one or more Stock Keeping Units (SKUs) provided for the `sellerListingSearch` query exceeds the maximum allowed length.
"""
type SkusExceedMaxLengthError implements SellerListingSearchInputError {
  """
  Technical description of the error for developers and debugging purposes.
  """
  errorDescription: String!
  """The maximum length allowed for each SKU."""
  maxLength: Int!
  """
  User-friendly suggestion on how to fix the error. This can be displayed to end users to help them correct their input.
  """
  remedy: String!
  """List of SKUs that exceed the maximum length."""
  violatingSkus: [String!]!
}

"""This type is used to identify Sofort as the payment method."""
type Sofort implements PaymentMethodType {
  """The unique identifier of Sofort."""
  code: ID!
  """The descriptive name of the Sofort payment method."""
  descriptiveName: String!
  """The display name of the Sofort payment method."""
  displayName: String!
}

"""
This enumerated type provides values for the sort order used in pagination.
"""
enum SortOrder {
  """Ascending order (oldest to newest)."""
  ASC
  """Descending (newest to oldest)."""
  DESC
}

"""
This type is used to display information about operation validation errors when these errors are triggered.
"""
type StandardListingValidationRuleViolation implements ListingValidationRuleViolation {
  """
  This array will show a list of one or more key-value pairs providing additional, structured context for the violation. For example, for a maximum length exceeded violation, this might contain {name: "maxLength", value: "80"}. Null values in a name-value pair indicates that no additional information is available on the violation.
  """
  additionalInformation: [NameValuePair!]
  """
  This array will show one or more string values that show the full path(s) to the input field(s) that caused the violation. 
  """
  inputPath: [String!]!
  """
  A unique identifier of the violation. Clients can use this code to implement custom logic. 
  """
  violationCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the violation, intended to be displayed to an end user.
  """
  violationDescription: String!
}

"""
This type is used to display information about operation warnings when these warnings are triggered. With warnings, the operation will be successful or partially successfully, but there are issues that the user should be aware of and may need to address these issues at a later time.
"""
type StandardListingWarning implements ListingWarning {
  """
  This array will show a list of one or more key-value pairs providing additional, structured context for the warning. Null values in a name-value pair indicates that no additional information is available on the warning.
  """
  additionalInformation: [NameValuePair!]
  """
  A unique identifier of the warning. Clients can use this code to implement custom logic. 
  """
  warningCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the warning, intended to be displayed to an end user.
  """
  warningMessage: String!
}

"""
This error is returned when the start date provided for the `sellerListingSearch` query is after the end date provided for a date range filter.
"""
type StartDateAfterEndDateError implements SellerListingSearchInputError {
  """The provided end date."""
  endDate: DateTime!
  """
  Technical description of the error for developers and debugging purposes.
  """
  errorDescription: String!
  """
  User-friendly suggestion on how to fix the error. This can be displayed to end users to help them correct their input.
  """
  remedy: String!
  """The provided start date."""
  startDate: DateTime!
}

"""
This type is used to show any errors that occurred during the execution of a mutation or query.
"""
type StartListingPreviewsCreationError {
  """
  A description of an error that occurred while executing a mutation or query. This field is intended to be a debugging aid for humans. The description is not localized and is subject to change.  Do not use these error descriptions for client-side error handling logic.
  """
  errorDescription: String!
}

"""
This is the base type for the **startListingPreviewsCreation** mutation. It contains an array of **externalProducts** that need to be converted into eBay listing previews.
"""
input StartListingPreviewsCreationInput {
  """
  This array is used to provide details of external products. Product details include title, images, product identifiers, product aspects, category name, and SKU value. In order to successfully identify an external product, send a title or an image, and include other fields such as product id (UPC, ISBN, or EAN). A SKU is optional, but it is highly recommended as it acts as a key to track/identify different external products. 
  """
  externalProducts: [ExternalProductDetailsInput!]
}

"""
The base type of the **startListingPreviewsCreation** mutation response. A successful mutation will return the **id** value for the task, and the listing preview results cannot be returned until the task is complete.
"""
type StartListingPreviewsCreationOutput {
  """
  An array of one or more errors that may have been triggered with the mutation request. This field will be returned as null if there are no errors.
  """
  errors: [StartListingPreviewsCreationError!]
  """
  This base response container should be returned with a successful mutation, but the listing preview results cannot be returned until the task is complete.
  """
  listingPreviewsCreationTask: ListingPreviewsCreationTask
}

"""Unique identifier of a custom category in which to list the item"""
type StoreCategory {
  """Store category Id"""
  id: ID!
}

"""
The input type for submitting a referral (review request) on an order inquiry. Select a reason from **OrderInquiryReferralAction.referralReasons** and provide its machine-readable **code** as **referralReasonCode** (see **PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason.code**). The provided **referralReasonCode** must match a valid **OrderInquiryReferralReason.code**.
"""
input SubmitOrderInquiryReferralInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the inquiry for which the referral is being submitted. This must reference a valid inquiry that is eligible for referral.
  """
  inquiryId: ID!
  """
  The machine-readable reason code from a selected **OrderInquiryReferralReason** (see **PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason.code**).
  """
  referralReasonCode: String!
}

"""
This type represents a business error that is returned when one or more validation errors occurs while submitting an order inquiry referral.
"""
type SubmitOrderInquiryReferralInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier for this specific error type - 'INQRY_SUBMIT_REFERRAL_VALIDATION_ERROR'
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  The human-readable message describing the shipment info input violation.
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """This array returns details about the specific request violations."""
  violations: [SubmitOrderInquiryReferralInputViolation!]!
}

"""
The interface represents input violation(s) detected while evaluating order inquiry referral submission. Each violation indicates that the provided referral input value did not comply with the business rules or constraints defined for submitting the referral. These rules may include:
- Missing required referral reason.
- Invalid referral reason.
"""
interface SubmitOrderInquiryReferralInputViolation {
  """
  The machine-readable code identifying the specific referral input violation.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable message describing the referral input violation. 
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
The union type for the **submitOrderInquiryReferral** mutation. This type covers two possible scenarios: success or failure. If the **submitOrderInquiryReferral** mutation succeeds, the referral request will be submitted. If the **submitOrderInquiryReferral** mutation fails, an array of blocking errors detailing why the mutation failed will be returned, and the item commitment will not be created. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error.
"""
union SubmitOrderInquiryReferralOutput = OrderInquiryActionNotPermittedError | OrderInquiryNotFoundError | SubmitOrderInquiryReferralInputValidationError | SubmitOrderInquiryReferralSuccess

"""The output type for the **submitOrderInqueryReferral** mutation."""
type SubmitOrderInquiryReferralSuccess {
  """The successfully submitted order inquiry."""
  orderInquiry: OrderInquiry!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **submitReturnReferral** mutation. This type provides the input for submitting a referral (review request) on an order return. Select a reason from `ReturnReferralAction.referralReasons` and provide its machine-readable `code` as `referralReasonCode` (see `PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason.code`).
"""
input SubmitReturnReferralInput {
  """
  The machine-readable reason code from a selected `OrderReturnReferralReason` (see **PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason.code**). For example, `REFER_RETURN_TO_EBAY`.
  """
  referralReasonCode: String!
  """
  The unique identifier of the return for which the referral is being submitted. This required field must reference a valid, return eligible, return ID that the user has permission to access.
  """
  returnId: ID!
}

"""
This error type indicates that one or more validation errors occurred while submitting the return referral.
"""
type SubmitReturnReferralInputValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """A machine-readable error code: `RTRN_SUBMIT_REFERRAL_VALIDATION_ERROR`"""
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable error message describing the issue.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains details about one or more specific request violations.
  """
  violations: [SubmitReturnReferralInputViolation!]!
}

"""
This interface represents input violations detected during submit return referral request evaluation, such as accepted values or codes (for example, referral reason code). Such constraints are governed by eBay's return policies, and may vary based on context, marketplace, or configuration.
"""
interface SubmitReturnReferralInputViolation {
  """
  A machine-readable code identifying the specific rule that was violated.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the rule violation. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **submitReturnReferral** mutation includes the result of a referral submission on an order return and any errors encountered. If successful, the updated return is returned. Otherwise, an error is returned indicating that the return was not found or the referral action was not permitted.
"""
union SubmitReturnReferralOutput = OrderReturn | ReturnActionNotPermittedError | ReturnNotFoundError | SubmitReturnReferralInputValidationError

"""Specifies the type of tag update operation to perform."""
enum TagUpdateAction {
  """
  Add the provided tags to the existing tag list. 
    
  **Note:** Tags that already exist will be ignored.
  """
  ADD
  """
  Remove the provided tags from the existing tag list. 
    
  **Note:** Tags that do not exist will be ignored.
  """
  DELETE
}

"""
This container shows sales tax information for an item in a specific tax jurisdiction
"""
type TaxInfo {
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller wants the sales tax rate for the jurisdiction to apply to the cumulative
  amount of item cost and shipping charges. This field is only applicable if the **salesTaxPercentage** and **salesTaxJurisdictionId**
  fields are also set.
  **Default**: false
  """
  salesTaxApplicableToShipping: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to specify a US territory or a Canadian province that will be charged the sales tax rate specified in the
  **salesTaxPercentage** field. The supported US territories are `AS` (America Samoa), `GU` (Guam),
  `MP` (Northern Mariana Islands), `PW` (Palau), and `VI` (US Virgin Islands).
    
  The two-letter codes for Canadian provinces can be found here on the
  [Government of Canada](https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/businesses/topics/completing-slips-summaries/financial-slips-summaries/return-investment-income-t5/provincial-territorial-codes.html)
  website. This field can only be used on the US and Canadian marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxJurisdictionId: String
  """
  This field is used along with **salesTaxJurisdictionId** field to set the sales tax rate for a specific US territory or a Canadian province.
  The percentage set here will be applied to sale price as the sales tax for the order line item. The value passed in is stored with a precision of 1 digits after the decimal point.
  This field can only be used on the US and Canadian marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller has an account level sales tax table set up and wishes to use the
  sales tax rates set up in that table. If this field is set to 'true', the values contained in the other sales tax fields
  (if set) in this container will be overridden by the values set in the sales tax table.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  salesTaxTableUsed: Boolean
  """
  Tax exception category code.  This field is used to provide a special category of tax such as a recycling fee or disposal tax.
  This is to be used only by sellers who have opted into sales tax being calculated by a sales tax calculation vendor.
  """
  thirdPartyTaxCategoryCode: String
  """
  The VAT (Value-added Tax) percentage rate that will be charged to buyers when an item is purchased from the listing.
  VAT is not applicable to all countries, including the US. Allowed VAT percentage rates can vary by region/country,
  so sellers should be aware of the rates they are legally required/allowed to charge, and they are responsible for charging
  the correct VAT rate. Only one digit is allowed to the right of the decimal point.
  """
  vatPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field is set to 'true' if the seller is registered on the listing site as a Business Seller and intends to use
  listing features that are offered to business users only. This field will always be 'true' if the
  **vatRestrictedToBusinessUser** field is set to 'true'.
    
  **Default**: false
  """
  vatRecognizedBusinessSeller: Boolean
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if a business seller wishes to make the listing exclusively available to potential buyers
  registered on eBay as business users. If false (or not returned), this indicates that the seller elects to offer the item to all
  users.
    
  This feature is only applicable to business sellers residing in Germany, Austria, or
  Switzerland who are listing in a B2B VAT-enabled category on the eBay Germany (DE), Austria (AT), or Switzerland (CH) sites.
    
  If this is set true, the seller must be a business seller and have a valid VAT-ID registered with eBay
  **Default value**: false
  """
  vatRestrictedToBusinessUser: Boolean
}

"""This type defines the priceline roll up for tax subtotal."""
type TaxSubtotal implements PriceLineRollup {
  """
  The monetary amount of the priceline rollup. This is the monetary value associated with the priceline item group
  """
  amount: AmountSet!
  """
  The human-readable name of the priceline roll up. 
  **Note**: In this context, the name will always be returned as 'TAX_SUBTOTAL'.
  """
  name: String!
  """This array returns the pricelines that are part of the rollup."""
  priceLines: [PriceLine!]!
}

"""
An RFC-3339 compliant time scalar for representing time-of-day without a date component.
**Format**: ISO 8601 time format following RFC-3339 (hh:mm:ss.sssZ or with timezone offset).
**Usage**: Used when only the time of day is relevant, independent of the date.
**Example**: '14:30:00.000Z' or '10:30:00-04:00'
**Note**: At runtime, this scalar converts to **java.time.OffsetTime** objects, preserving timezone information.
"""
scalar Time

"""
This type indicates that a participant (buyer or seller) is experiencing communication difficulties with the other party.
"""
type UnableToReachAgreement implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """Machine-readable reason code: 'UNABLE_TO_REACH_AGREEMENT'."""
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable text of the case referral reason.
  **Max length**: 100 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
Unanswered buyer-questions data for this listing (seller-scoped).
Count is 0 when there are no unanswered questions.
Field is null when data is not applicable or cannot be shown if:
- The user is not the listing’s seller.
- Listing is ended or beyond the data retention window used by M2M, which is 10 months.
- Upstream error or timeout from the Service/DB.
"""
type UnansweredQuestions {
  """
  Number of unanswered questions for the listing
  Example: If a seller has received 10 questions from buyers for a listing, and has
  responded to/answered 7 of them, the count returned will be 3.
  Usage: This field is intended to show sellers how many questions they have yet to answer.
  """
  count: Int!
}

"""
This type indicates that cancellation reason is undisclosed to the current viewer. For example, certain cancellations created by eBay do not disclose the actual reason to sellers.
"""
type UndisclosedCancellation implements ContractCancellationReason {
  """
  The unique cancellation reason code for this use case. For this type, the value is `UNDISCLOSED`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the cancellation reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type represents transactions that use unrecognized or unsupported payment methods.
"""
type UnknownPaymentMethod implements PaymentMethodType {
  """
  The unique identifier of the payment method code for unknown payments. Value: `UNKNOWN`.
  """
  code: ID!
  """The descriptive name of the unknown payment method."""
  descriptiveName: String!
  """The display name of the unknown payment method."""
  displayName: String!
}

"""
This type represents the reason used by seller when the buyer has not completed payment after the maximum waiting period defined by eBay's policy for resolving unpaid items. For more details, refer to the policy: https://www.ebay.com/help/selling/getting-paid/resolving-unpaid-items-buyers?id=4137
"""
type UnpaidContractCancellation implements ContractCancellationReason {
  """
  The unique cancellation reason code for this use case. For this type, the value is `UNPAID_CONTRACT`.
  """
  code: String!
  """
  A human-readable description of the cancellation reason. This alphanumeric string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type indicates that a participant (buyer or seller) has not received a response from the other party.
"""
type UnresponsiveTradingPartner implements PostPurchaseCaseReferralReason {
  """Machine-readable reason code: 'SELLER_NO_RESPONSE'."""
  code: String!
  """
  The human-readable text of the case referral reason.
  **Max length**: 100 characters
  **Format**: Alphanumeric
  """
  displayText: String!
}

"""
This type is used to show the identifier(s) of an item that failed to be updated with a **bulkUpdateInventory** mutation. An array of one or more violations will be present and an array of non-blocking warnings will also be present if any occurred.
"""
type UpdateInventoryFailure {
  """
  This container will show either the **listingId** of the item's listing that failed to be updated or the **sku** value of the item. Which of these identifiers is returned depends on which identifier was used in the input to identify the item.
  """
  listingItemIdentifier: ListingItemIdentifier!
  """
  This array will show one or more validation rule violations that prevented the item from being successfully updated.
  """
  violations: [ListingValidationRuleViolation!]!
  """
     This array will show one or more non-blocking validation warnings or issues that occurred during the update operation. 
  **Note**: This array will be returned as empty if no warnings occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to update the price and/or quantity for one to four items in fixed price listings. For each item identified in the array, either the price, the quantity, or both fields must be included. These items can all be separate SKUs in the same multiple-SKU listing, items in four different listings, or a combination of the two. 
"""
input UpdateInventoryInput {
  """
     The new available quantity for the item in the fixed-price listing. If the available quantity for the item is not changing, this field does not need to be included. 
  **Note**: If you are not changing the available quantity, you can include this field with no value, but providing a null value will result in an execution error.
  """
  availableQuantity: Int
  """
     The new 'Buy it Now' price for the item in the fixed-price listing. If the price for the item is not changing, this field does not need to be included. 
  **Note**: Up to two digits can be included to the right of the decimal point to indicate the new price, and the price will be in the currency of the listing marketplace.
  **Note**: If you are not changing the price, you can include this field with no value, but providing a null value will result in an execution error.
  """
  fixedPrice: Decimal
  """
     This container is used to identify a specific item to update. An item within a single-SKU listing can be identified with a **listingId** or a **sku** value (if a sku value is defined in the listing). A **sku** value must be used for an item within a multiple-SKU listing. 
  **Note**: Either the **listingId** or **sku** value is used to identify but don't use both.
  """
  listingItemIdentifier: ListingItemIdentifierInput!
}

"""
This type is used to show the identifier(s) of an item that was successfully updated with a **bulkUpdateInventory** mutation. An array of non-blocking warnings will also be present if any occurred.
"""
type UpdateInventorySuccess {
  """
  This container will show the **listingId** of the item's listing that was successfully updated, and also the **sku** value of the item if the **sku** value was used in the input to identify the item.
  """
  listingItemIdentifier: ListingItemIdentifier!
  """
     This array will show one or more non-blocking validation warnings or issues that occurred during the update operation. 
  **Note**: This array will be returned as empty if no warnings occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
Represents details about an error that occurred while updating an item commitment.
"""
type UpdateItemCommitmentError {
  """A user-friendly, non-localized message describing the error."""
  displayMessage: String!
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. Below are the five errors that may occur:
  - INVALID_INPUT: This error indicates that the item commitment ID is not recognized. 
  - NOT_AUTHORIZED: This error indicates that the item commitment doesn't belong to the authenticated eBay user, so this action cannot be taken. 
  - VERSION_LOCKED: This error indicates that the latest version of item commitment is locked, possibly because the item commitment was being modified by another process. With this error, the user can make another attempt to update the item commitment.
  - TEMPORARILY_NOT_AVAILABLE: This error indicates that a system error occurred. This error may occur with a complete failure, and the user can try again after a short period of time. 
  - DEPENDENCY_TIME_OUT: — This error indicates that a timeout occurred. With this error, the user can try again after a short period of time.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  The ID of the item commitment that failed to be updated with a mutation.
  """
  inputItemCommitmentId: ID!
  """
  This boolean indicates whether or not the user should retry a mutation to update the corresponding item commitment again. If this field is returned as 'true', the user can make another attempt to update the item commitment.
  """
  retryable: Boolean!
}

"""
This type is used to add or delete one or more custom tags for up to 100 item commitments.
"""
input UpdateItemCommitmentTagInput {
  """
  The enumeration value here controls whether the provided custom tags in the **tags** array are tags to add or delete. The supported values are:
  - ADD
  - DELETE
  """
  action: TagUpdateAction!
  """
  The unique identifier of the item commitment for which one or more tags will be added or deleted.
  """
  itemCommitment: ID!
  """
  This array is used to specify from one to five custom tags to add or delete. Each custom tag should be delimited with a comma.
  **Note**: When deleting one or more custom tags, the user must make sure the custom tag(s) to delete are exact matches. An error will occur if that is not the case.
  **Maximum length**: 10 characters (each tag)
  **Maximum items**: 5
  """
  tags: [String!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the starting bid price and/or reserve price for an auction listing.
"""
input UpdateListingAuctionPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the lowest price at which the seller is willing to sell an item in an auction listing. A small fee is charged to use this feature. If the **reservePrice** field value is not met or surpassed during bidding, the auction will end without a winning bidder. This price must be higher than the **startingBidPrice**. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: A Reserve Price can only be lowered in value and not increased, and if there are qualifying bids on the listing or the end time is less than 12 hours away, it can not be changed at all. See the [Setting a reserve price](https://www.ebay.com/help/selling/listings/selling-auctions/reserve-prices?id=4143) help topic for more information on how Reserve Prices work.
  **Note**: If there are no bids in the listing and the end time is more than 12 hours away, you can remove the Reserve Price be including this field and setting its value to '0.0'.
  """
  reservePrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to change the starting bid price for an auction listing. The first bid must meet or exceed this value or it will be rejected. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: The starting bid price cannot be changed once a listing has at least one qualifying bid.
  """
  startingBidPrice: Decimal
}

"""
This type is used to make changes to **Best Offer** settings, including enabling or disabling the Best Offer feature, or to add, modify, or remove the auto-accept and auto-reject thresholds.
"""
input UpdateListingBestOfferTermsInput {
  """
  Include this field to set, modify, or remove the auto-accept threshold price. Best Offers will be automatically accepted by the seller if they meet or exceed the price. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-accept feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to 'true'.
  **Note**: To remove the auto-accept threshold price if one is set up for the listing, included this field and use an empty or null value.
  """
  autoAcceptThreshold: Decimal
  """
  Include this field to set, modify, or remove the auto-decline threshold price. Best Offers will be automatically declined by the seller if the price is at or below this value. For this field to have an effect, the listing category must support the Best Offer auto-decline feature and the corresponding **bestOfferEnabled** field must be included and set to 'true'.
  **Note**: To remove the auto-decline threshold price if one is set up for the listing, included this field and use an empty or null value.
  """
  autoDeclineThreshold: Decimal
  """
  This boolean field is used to enable or disable the Best Offer feature for a fixed-price or auction listing. If set to 'true', the Best Offer feature is enabled, allowing potential buyers to make offers on the item. If set to 'false' the Best Offer feature is disabled.
  **Note** For auction listings, the Buy It Now and Best Offer features cannot be used simultaneously.
  **Note** If Best Offer is enabled for an auction listing, it is automatically disabled as soon as the listing receives a qualifying bid, and any pending offers or counteroffers are invalidated.
  """
  bestOfferEnabled: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the street address for a business entity such as the product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input UpdateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput {
  """
  This field adds or modifies the first line of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine1: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the second line of the entity's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the city of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  city: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the two letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation of the country of the entity's address.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  This field adds or modifies the postal code of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 9 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the state or province of the entity's street address.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  stateOrProvince: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the product manufacturer or responsible person. At least one of the three fields in this type must be specified for a product manufacturer or responsible person.
"""
input UpdateListingBusinessEntityContactInput {
  """
  This field is used to specify the entity's URL for their online Contact Us/Support page.
  **Max length**: 250 characters.
  """
  contactUrl: HttpOrHttpsUrl
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the entity's email address.
  **Max length**: 180 characters.
  """
  email: String
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the entity's phone number.
  **Max length**: 64 characters.
  """
  phone: String
}

"""
This type is used to disable or enable a seller's account-level buyer restrictions and/or set or modify a quantity limit per buyer threshold for a multiple-quantity, fixed price listing.
"""
input UpdateListingBuyerRestrictionsInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to disable all buyer restrictions (that are set in the seller's account) for the listing, or set to 'false' if the seller wishes to have all account-level buyer restrictions to apply to the listing.
  """
  disableBuyerRestrictions: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the maximum quantity of items that a single buyer may purchase during the duration of a fixed price listing (single or multiple-variation). The buyer is blocked from the purchase if that buyer is attempting to purchase a quantity of items that will exceed this value. Previous purchases made by the buyer are taken into account. For example, if **quantityLimitPerBuyer** is set to '5' for a listing, and *Buyer1* purchases a quantity of three in a previous sale, *Buyer1* is only allowed to purchase an additional quantity of two in subsequent orders on the same listing.
  """
  quantityLimitPerBuyer: Int
}

"""
This type is used if the seller wishes to make the listing a charitable listing, or if a charity is already set up, it is used to change the charitable organization and/or the donation percentage per sale.
"""
input UpdateListingCharityInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of the non-profit organization that will benefit from the sale of the item. The [Charity API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/charity/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve the numeric identifiers for the charities and to find out more about the organization.
  """
  charityOrganizationId: ID
  """
  This field sets the percentage of the purchase price that the seller chooses to donate to the selected non-profit organization for each sale generated by the listing. An integer value is used here with supported values ranging from 10 to 100. Within this range, only increments of 5 can be used, so 15, 20, 25, etc.
  **Min value**: 10
  **Max value**: 100
  """
  donationPercentage: Int
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify one or more country-specific product compliance or takeback policies. Up to 6 product compliance policies may be set per country, but only 1 takeback policy may be set per country.
"""
input UpdateListingCountryPolicyInput {
  """
  The two-letter ISO 3166-1 standard abbreviation for a country that hosts an eBay marketplace, a marketplace to which the corresponding policy or policies apply. The supported values are `GB`, `DE`, `FR`, `IT`, and `ES`.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code!
  """
  This array is used to set or modify one or more country-specific product compliance policy ID values or one takeback policy ID value that will apply to the corresponding country. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all policies defined for a seller's account.
  **Note**: All country-specific product policies that the seller would like to apply to the corresponding country in the listing must be included in this array, and not just the new policies being added. There can only be one takeback policy per country, so there will only be just one takeback policy ID in this array.
  """
  policyIds: [ID!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify global or country-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies for a listing.
"""
input UpdateListingCustomPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the global product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. The product compliance policies set with this array will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies should be set with the **regionalProductCompliancePolicies** container instead.
  **Note**: All global product compliance policies that the seller would like to apply to the listing must be included in this array, and not just the new policies being added.
  **Max number of product compliance policies allowed per listing**: 6.
  **Max length of each product compliance policy ID**: 15 characters.
  """
  productCompliancePolicyIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used add or modify the country-specific product compliance policies that will be used for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all product compliance policies defined for a seller's account. Product compliance policies provide buyers with important information and disclosures about products. Country-specific policies may be needed where countries might have special legal/regulatory requirements. For example, if you sell batteries in a country requiring disclosures that apply only to that country, a country-specific product compliance policy could contain this information. If country-specific policies are not needed, use the **productCompliancePolicyIds** array instead.
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per marketplace**: 6 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of product compliance policies allowed per listing**: 30 (6 per country).
  """
  regionalProductCompliancePolicies: UpdateListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify one or more country-specific takeback policies that will be used for a listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The law in some countries may require sellers to take back a used product when the buyer buys a new product but wishes to dispose of it. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy. If a country-specific takeback policy is not needed, one global takeback policy is set with the **takebackPolicyId** field.
  **Maximum number of take back policies allowed per marketplace**: 1 (with supported countries being GB, DE, FR, IT, and ES).
  **Maximum number of take back policies allowed per listing**: 5 (1 per country).
  """
  regionalTakebackPolicies: UpdateListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput
  """
  This field is used to add, change, or remove the global takeback policy to use for the listing. The [getCustomPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/custom_policy/methods/getCustomPolicies) method can be used with the **policyTypes** query parameter to retrieve all takeback policies defined for a seller's account. The takeback policy set with this field will apply to all countries where the seller operates. Country-specific policies should be set with **regionalTakebackPolicies** container instead.
  **Note**: To remove a global takeback policy, include this field and set its value as empty or null.
  **Max length of takeback policy ID**: 15 characters.
  """
  takebackPolicyId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify Energy Efficiency Label related information for such categories as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Note that these three category types will also need Rating and Range product aspects. See the [Energy efficiency information](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/static/inventory/energy-efficiency.html) topic for more information.
"""
input UpdateListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify a brief text-based summary of the information included on the Energy Efficiency Label for a product. The description should be concise and informative, providing key details about the energy efficiency of the product. If this field is provided, the **imageUrl** must also be provided.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the text in the current image description if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 280 characters
  """
  imageDescription: String
  """
  This field is used to specify the URL to the Energy Efficiency Label image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  imageUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including energy efficiency labels.")
  """
  The URL to the Product Information Sheet image that is applicable to a product. This field is required if an Energy Efficiency Label is provided, and the URL provided must be an eBay Picture Services (EPS) URL using 'https'. The image resource of the **Media API** can be used to upload images to eBay.
  **Max length**: 200 characters
  """
  productInformationSheetUrl: HttpsUrl @deprecated(reason: "Use listingTerms.regulatory.documentsIds field instead to attach documents to a listing, including product information sheets.")
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify an eco-participation fee for item(s) in a listing. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries.
"""
input UpdateListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput {
  """
  This is the fee paid for new items to the eco-organization (for example, *eco-organisme* in France). It is a contribution to the financing of the disposal of the item responsibly. In a multiple-SKU listing, this fee should be specified at the variation level and not in this field. The [getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getExtendedProducerResponsibilityPolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports, requires, or recommends eco-participation fees at the listing or variation level.
  """
  ecoParticipationFee: Decimal!
}

"""
This type is used to modify details on how the item will be delivered to the buyer. The data in this container includes available shipping services, ship-to and excluded shipping locations, shipping costs, package details, and more.
"""
input UpdateListingFulfillmentTermsInput {
  """
  This field should be included if the seller wishes to enable or disable digital delivery of an item. A digital delivery item is an item that can be downloaded via a link or delivered to the buyer via email. The  [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see if a leaf category supports digital delivery.
  """
  digitalDeliverySupported: Boolean
  """
  This field can be included if the seller wishes to enable or disable eBay's Global Shipping Program (GSP) to ship items internationally. With GSP, the seller ships the item to eBay's shipping partner, and that shipping partner handles all logistics of the international shipping leg. GSP is only available for listings on the eBay GB (EBAY_GB) marketplace. eBay US (EBAY_US) has a similar program called eBay International Shipping, but there is currently no boolean field associated with this feature.
  """
  globalShippingSupported: Boolean
  """
  This container is used to add or modify information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions. Package weight is required when calculated shipping is used, and shipping services generally have dimension and weight restrictions.
  """
  packageSpecifications: UpdateListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput
  """
  This container is used to modify information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
  """
  shippingTerms: UpdateListingShippingTermsInput
}

"""
This type is used to provide a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for the item. GTIN is a globally unique identifier for trade items used by companies to identify products. GTINs include UPCs, EANs, and ISBNs. Optionally, eBay will search for a catalog product against a provided GTIN if the **includeEbayProductDetails** field is included and set to 'true'. If a matching eBay catalog product is found, the listing will automatically be updated with product details of that catalog product, including product title, product description, product aspects, and stock photo(s).
"""
input UpdateListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  This field is used to supply a European Article Number (EAN) for a product. It is a 13-digit barcode standard used internationally for retail product identification. Also known as International Article Number. Some leaf categories may require an EAN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this EAN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  **Max length**: 13 characters.
  """
  ean: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply an International Standard Book Number (ISBN) for a product. It is a unique identifier for books and book-like products. Can be 10 digits (older format) or 13 digits (current format). Some leaf categories may require an ISBN, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this ISBN, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to true.
  **Max length**: 13 characters.
  """
  isbn: ID
  """
  This field is used to supply a Universal Product Code (UPC) for a product. It is a 12-digit barcode standard used primarily in North America for retail product identification. Some leaf categories may require a UPC, and you can use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see if a leaf category supports or requires this GTIN type. If you wish to search for an eBay catalog product based on this UPC, include the **includeEbayProductDetails** field and set its value to 'true'.
  **Max value**: 12 characters.
  """
  upc: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
"""
input UpdateListingHazardousMaterialInput {
  """
  This field is used by the seller to add or modify component information for the listing. For example, component information can provide the specific material of Hazmat concern.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current additional info text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 120 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to four pictogram codes that represent the possible hazard(s) that a product poses. The pictograms that are stated on the product's Safety Data Sheet should be used. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the codes that can be passed into this array. The pictogram(s) that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Note**: All pictogram codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the hazardous material signal word for the product. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the strings that can be passed into this array.
  **Max length**: 15 characters.
  """
  signalWordCode: ID
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to eight hazardous statement codes that are applicable to the product. These codes map to actual hazardous statement text. Use the [getHazardousMaterialsLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata-test/resources/marketplace/methods/getHazardousMaterialsLabels) method to retrieve the statement codes that can be passed into this array. The hazardous statements that the code(s) represent will be painted on the created listing.
  **Note**: All statement codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]
}

"""
The base request type for the **updateListing** mutation. This type is used to add or modify listing details for an active or scheduled eBay listing. The details that can be modified include listing terms and price and quantity information for each item available for sale in the listing. For multiple-SKU listings, the **listingVariations** container will be used to add or modify variation information for a multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input UpdateListingInput {
  """
  This container is used to identify the listing to be updated. The listing can either be identified with the **listingId** or the SKU value if defined in the listing.
  """
  listingIdentifier: ListingIdentifierInput!
  """
  Use this array in an **updateListing** mutation if you need to update one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing.
  """
  listingItems: UpdateListingItemsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify any listing terms details for the active or scheduled listing, including payment terms, return policy, fulfillment terms, and more.
  """
  listingTerms: UpdateListingTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify variation details for an active or scheduled multiple-SKU listing. This container includes details on the available product variations within the listing, and which traits are different for each of these variations. Products in a multiple-SKU listing tend to vary by one or more traits such as color and size, and interested buyers need to select which variation they want to purchase. For example, the 'Blue, Large' t-shirt.
  """
  listingVariations: UpdateListingVariationsInput
  """
  This field is used to identify the eBay marketplace where the listing exists. Generally, a listing will remain on the same eBay marketplace. See [`ListingMarketplace`] for list of supported enumeration values. It determines the regional settings, currency, and other marketplace-specific configurations.
  """
  marketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
  This container allows a user to run a **updateListing** mutation in validation mode, which means that the listing object will be validated, but a successful mutation will not update a listing. 
  """
  options: ListingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify product data for an active or scheduled listing. Product data under this container includes title, description, product aspects, item condition, images, and more.
  """
  product: UpdateListingProductInput
}

"""
This type is used to update the available quantity for a purchasable item.
"""
input UpdateListingItemAvailabilityInput {
  """
  This field updates the quantity available for an item. For auction listings, this value must always be 1. For a multiple-SKU listing, each item variation can have its own quantity value, allowing sellers to manage inventory for each variation independently.
  **Note**: For a multiple-SKU listing, the quantity for an item variation can be set to 0 if the SKU is temporarily out of stock, but a seller wishes to retain the variation and restock inventory for that SKU at a later time.
  """
  quantityAvailable: Int!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input UpdateListingItemCompatibilitiesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or update the list of compatible vehicles or assemblies through a set of name-value pairs such as *Year*, *Make*, and *Model*. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Max compatibilities allowed on a listing**: 3000
  """
  itemCompatibilities: [UpdateListingItemCompatibilityInput!]
  """
  This field indicates if the entire compatibility list is to be deleted. If `true`, all existing compatibilities will be removed from the listing's compatibility list. If `false` or omitted, the compatibilities specified in the `itemCompatibilities` will be added or updated in the listing's compatibility list.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  replaceAll: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles.
"""
input UpdateListingItemCompatibilityInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the list of compatible vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts and Accessory item. The required/applicable names and values are specific to the primary category for the listing, and can be found using the [getCompatibilityPropertyNames](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyNames) and [getCompatibilityPropertyValues](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/compatibilities/methods/getCompatibilityPropertyValues) methods of the **Metadata API**.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to the compatibility list, the full set of compatibility property name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the compatibility list data that is being added or modified.
  **Max number of allowed fitments on the listing**: 3000.
  **Max compatibility name length**: 65
  **Max compatibility value length**: 65
  """
  compatibilities: [NameValuesPairInput!]!
  """
  The seller can use this field to add or modify compatibility notes pertaining to the parts compatibility being specified. For example, if this compatibility information applies to a vehicle, a seller may use this field to specify the placement of the part on a vehicle or the type of vehicle a part fits.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current compatibility notes text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 500 characters.
  """
  compatibilityNotes: String
  """
  This field indicates if the compatibility is to be deleted. If `true`, the compatibility specified by the `compatibilities` will be removed from the listing's compatibility list. If `false` or omitted, the compatibility specified by the `compatibilities` will be added or updated in the listing's compatibility list.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  removeCompatibilityFromListing: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify condition descriptor data (through name-value pairs) for a single graded and ungraded trading card listing in one of the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
"""
input UpdateListingItemConditionDescriptorInput {
  """
  This field can be used to add or modify additional information about a condition descriptor. One example is using this field to specify the **Certification Number** for a graded card.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current additional information text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 30 characters.
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This field is used to add or change the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor that maps to the condition descriptor name. The IDs for condition descriptor names can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Condition descriptor names for graded cards include **Grader** and **Grade** (both required) and **Certification Number** (optional), and condition descriptor names for ungraded cards include **Card Condition**.
  """
  name: ID
  """
  This array is used to add or change the alphanumeric identifier of the condition descriptor value that maps to an actual value supported by the condition descriptor. For example, graded cards require **Grader** and **Grade** as condition descriptor names, so the value(s) in this array will show the organization that graded the card and the card's actual grade, which ranges from 1 to 10. The numeric IDs for condition descriptor values can be found by using the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method of the **Metadata API**, passing in the category ID as a filter query parameter. Locate the Condition descriptor name first in the response, and then look for the corresponding values in the **conditionDescriptorValues** array of that response.
  """
  values: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to change the condition of the item, to add or modify the condition description for a used item, or to make any changes to the condition descriptor data for a single trading cards listing.
"""
input UpdateListingItemConditionInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or modify additional details about a non-new item's physical state, including any defects, wear, or other characteristics that affect its condition. This field can be used for all categories except those that require the **conditionDescriptors** array.
  **Note**: If this field is used, the text provided in the field will completely overwrite the current condition description if one exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 1000 characters.
  """
  conditionDescription: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify item condition information (through name-value pairs) for a single graded and ungraded trading card listed in the following categories: *Non-Sport Trading Card Singles (183050)*, *CCG Individual Cards (183454)*, and *Sports Trading Card Singles (261328)*. Graded cards require the **Grader** and the **Grade** descriptors, while ungraded cards require a **Card Condition** descriptor unique to trading cards, such as 'Near mint or better'.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to condition descriptor data, the full set of condition descriptor name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the condition descriptor data that is being added or modified.
  """
  conditionDescriptors: [UpdateListingItemConditionDescriptorInput!]
  """
  This field is used to change the item's condition using the numeric identifier for a condition. Supported conditions and the text used to describe the conditions vary by marketplace and leaf category. Use the [getItemConditionPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getItemConditionPolicies) method to get the supported condition IDs and their descriptions for leaf categories.
  """
  conditionId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to modify a specific purchasable item within a listing, allowing you to create, update, or remove them. It includes a unique combination of identifying characteristics such as global identifiers, listing terms, availability, price, and regulatory information requirements. Every listing contains at least one item, providing a unified approach that works transparently across simple single-SKU listings and complex multiple-SKU listing.
"""
input UpdateListingItemInput {
  """
  This container is used to modify the pricing information or available quantity, and can also be used to add or modify the eco-participation fee (if applicable) for a purchasable item.
  """
  itemTerms: UpdateListingItemTermsInput
  """
  For either a single-SKU or a multiple-SKU listing, this container can be used to add or modify a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will overwrite conflicting product details for the active or scheduled listing. For a multiple-SKU listing, the **traits** array will be required if the seller is adding a new variation to the listing. The **traits** array identifies the unique traits of a variation within that multiple-SKU listing. Common unique traits within a multiple-SKU listing are 'Color' and 'Size'. For example, a 'Blue, Large' shirt. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values.
  """
  product: UpdateListingItemProductInput
  """
  The field indicates whether to delete this variation. If set to true, the variation is removed from the listing. Note that this is only applicable for multiple-SKU listings; for single-SKU listings, the field value is ignored if included.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  removeItemFromListing: Boolean
  """
  The seller-defined Stock-Keeping Unit (SKU) that uniquely identifies a purchasable item in the listing. When updating a SKU-managed listing, the behavior of this field is conditional. For single-SKU listings, this field is ignored, as the listing is already identified by its SKU. For multiple-SKU listings, you must provide a variation's existing SKU to identify it for modification (e.g. changing its price). To add a new variation, you must assign it a new SKU, and this value must be unique for each variation in the listing.
  **Important**: For update operations, the presence of a SKU in the item container will cause the listing to be treated as a multiple-SKU (MSKU) listing.
  **Max length**: 50 characters.
  """
  sku: String
}

"""
This type is used to update the item's physical location. Item location is required for every listing. The **country** field is always required, and either the **postalCode** or **location** must also be provided, but not necessarily both.
"""
input UpdateListingItemLocationInput {
  """
  The two-letter country code, as defined in the ISO-3166 standard, must be specified in this field to indicate the country where the item is located. Please keep in mind that the item is often located in the same country as the listing marketplace, but this is not a requirement.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """
  The field indicates the geographic location (city and state/province) where the listing is physically located. If you do not provide a value in this field, you must provide a value in the **postalCode** field and the field value will be derived from the postal code.
  For the CLASSIFIED_AD format for Motor vehicles, the value provided in the field is used as item location only if the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2** fields of the **UpdateListingSellerContactInput** are not provided. If the **addressLine1** and **addressLine2** fields of the **UpdateListingSellerContactInput** are provided, the item location field value is ignored.
  **Max length**: 200 characters.
  """
  location: String
  """
  The postal code (zip code) where the listing is physically located. Either the **location** field or the **postalCode** field must be specified or an error will occur. Postal/zip code format varies by region. e.g. US: 5-digit numeric codes (e.g., 12345), Australia: 4-digit numeric codes (e.g., 2000), GB: Variable-length alphanumeric codes with letters and numbers (e.g., SW1A 1AA). Other regions follow local postal service standards.
  **Max length**: 32 characters.
  """
  postalCode: String
}

"""
This type is used to update price data for an item in a listing, including the price for a fixed price listing or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. Other price fields include auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
"""
input UpdateListingItemPricingTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the starting bid price and/or reserve price for an auction listing.
  """
  auctionPrice: UpdateListingAuctionPriceInput
  """
  This field updates the price of a fixed price item or the 'Buy it Now' price for an auction listing. The 'Buy it Now' option is disabled for an auction listing as soon as that listing has a qualifying bid. The price will be in the default currency for the marketplace for this listing. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  **Note**: For update operations, the mapping behavior depends on the presence of auction price container. If only `fixedPrice` is provided (no `auctionPrice` container), it will be treated as a fixed price listing. If `fixedPrice` is provided along with `auctionPrice` container, it will be treated as an auction listing.
  """
  fixedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This container is used to add or modify pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
  """
  marketingPrice: UpdateListingMarketingPriceInput
}

"""
This type can be used to add or modify a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) for a product or add an eBay product ID (ePID). If the ePID is found or if a provided GTIN value is matched to an eBay catalog product, the product details of that product definition will overwrite conflicting product details of the active or scheduled listing. For a multiple-SKU listing, the **traits** array would be needed if the seller wants to add a new variation to an active or scheduled multiple-SKU listing. The **traits** array identifies the unique traits of the variation within that multiple-SKU listing. Common unique traits within a multiple-SKU listing are 'Color' and 'Size'. For example, a 'Blue, Large' shirt. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values.
"""
input UpdateListingItemProductInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or add an eBay product ID (ePID) for a product. If an eBay catalog product is found that maps to a GTIN or an ePID, product details of that eBay catalog product will be used to update the product details of the active or scheduled listing. The product details in a catalog product include product title, product description, aspects, eBay leaf category, and stock photo.
  **Note**: If an eBay catalog product is found and used to update a listing, any other product-related details defined in the listing may be dropped.
  """
  productIdentifiers: UpdateListingProductIdentifiersInput
  """
  This array is needed if the seller wants to add a new variation to an active or scheduled multiple-SKU listing. This array is used to provide the traits that make each item unique in context of the multiple-SKU listing. Each item in a multiple-SKU listing must have a unique combination of trait values, and the trait names and trait values specified here must be defined as available trait names and trait values in the **variationDetails** container. An error will be thrown if the specified traits do not match the variation traits defined in the **variationDetails** container.
  **Note**: The trait names and values must match the marketplace's language and locale.
  **Max allowed traits**: 5.
  """
  traits: [NameValuePairInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to make updates to an array of one or more purchasable items. A single-SKU listing will only have one item object, while a multiple-SKU listing will have numerous item objects. Each item object will have price, quantity, and global product identifiers if applicable. Item objects within multiple-SKU listings will show unique traits that differentiate them from the rest of the variations within the listing.
"""
input UpdateListingItemsInput {
  """
  This array is used to manage the list of items or variations in the listing, allowing you to create, update, or remove them. For a single-SKU listing, this array must contain exactly one item. For a multiple-SKU listing, it must contain one item for each product variation (e.g. one for "Red / Large", one for "Blue / Small").
  **Maximum number of items for a multiple-SKU listing**: 250.
  """
  items: [UpdateListingItemInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to update quantity and pricing information for a purchasable item, or is also used to provide or update an eco-participation fee if applicable for the item.
"""
input UpdateListingItemTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used to update the available quantity for a purchasable item. Quantity is required for all purchasable items.
  """
  availability: UpdateListingItemAvailabilityInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify an eco-participation fee for an item. An eco-participation fee is a mandatory charge designed to fund the recycling and proper disposal of certain products at the end of their lifecycle. Eco-participation fees are one part of the Extended Producer Responsibility regulation enforced in EU countries. 
  """
  extendedProducerResponsibility: UpdateListingExtendedProducerResponsibilityInput
  """
  This container is used to update price data for a purchasable item, including the price for a fixed price item or the *Buy it Now* price for an auction item. Other price fields include auction reserve price, and other settings related to discount pricing features.
  """
  pricingTerms: UpdateListingItemPricingTermsInput
}

"""
This type is used to change the duration of the listing, and can also be used to modify the future date when a scheduled listing will become active.
"""
input UpdateListingLifecycleTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to change the duration of an active or scheduled listing. All fixed price listings must be set to `GTC`(Good 'til Cancelled), but the listing duration days of auction and ad listings may vary based on marketplace and category. The [getListingTypePolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getListingTypePolicies) method can be used to see supported durations for each leaf category.
  **Note**: A change to the duration of an active auction listing must be made within two hours of the listing going live, and once an auction has one or more qualifying bids, the duration can't be changed.
  """
  listingDurationInDays: ListingDurationInDays
  """
  This field is used if the user wishes to modify the publish date date of a scheduled listing that has not yet gone active. This field cannot be used for an active listing. The timestamp specified in this field must be a future date. For more information on eBay scheduled listings, see the [Listing durations and timings](https://www.ebay.com/help/selling/listings/creating-managing-listings/selecting-listing-duration?id=4652) help topic.
  """
  scheduledToStartAt: DateTime
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the radius for a local listing, making it available to buyers within that specified area. The seller's supplied **postalCode** or **location** field value will be used as the center point for this radius.
"""
input UpdateListingLocalDistanceInput {
  """
  The numeric value for the radius. The unit of measurement for this value is specified in the **distanceUnit** field. This value defines the radius of the area around the seller's location where the listing will be visible to local buyers. The user can call the [getMotorsListingPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** to get supported distances. Look for the [localListingDistances](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies#response.motorsListingPolicies.localListingDistances) array in the response.
  """
  distance: Int!
  """
  The unit of measurement used for the **distance**. Currently, the only supported value is `MILES`.
  """
  distanceUnit: DistanceUnit
}

"""
This type is used to add a product manufacturer contact or to update any of the data currently associated with the product manufacturer that is already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
"""
input UpdateListingManufacturerInput {
  """
  This container adds or modifies the street address for the product manufacturer.
  """
  address: UpdateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field adds or modifies the name of the company that manufactured the product. This field is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the product manufacturer. At least one of the three is required if manufacturer information is supplied.
  """
  contact: UpdateListingBusinessEntityContactInput
}

"""
This type adds or modifies pricing and other settings related to the Minimum Advertised Price, Strikethrough Pricing, or eBay Outlet features. All three of these features are restricted and sellers must qualify to use them.
"""
input UpdateListingMarketingPriceInput {
  """
  This field is used to set/modify and display the **Made for Outlet** comparison price for a listing, and can only be used if the listing will be displayed on an eBay Outlet page. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  madeForOutletComparisonPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to set/modify the Minimum Advertised Price (MAP) for a listing. MAP is an agreement between suppliers (or manufacturers (OEM)) and the retailers (sellers) stipulating the lowest price a listing is allowed to be advertised at. Sellers can offer prices below MAP by means of other discounts. This only applies to fixed price listings and auction listings with the 'Buy It Now' option. This is a restricted feature that sellers must qualify to use. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is only applicable for the Minimum Advertised Price feature, and controls whether the discounted price is shown to buyers prior to checkout by the buyer clicking on a link on the View Item page, or the discounted price is shown just prior to checkout when the buyer has clicked the Buy button. See [`ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  minimumAdvertisedPriceExposure: ListingMinimumAdvertisedPriceExposure
  """
  This field sets the 'originalRetailPrice' for a listing. This price must be provided if a qualified seller is using the Strikethrough Price feature. The 'originalRetailPrice' price is the actual retail price set by the manufacturer (OEM). The price specified in this field should always be more than the price specified in the **fixedPrice** field. The price format must be according to the marketplace's currency format. See the [Get Currencies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCurrencies) call for more information on the currency format.
  """
  originalRetailPrice: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to change the boolean value of the **soldOffEbay** field, whose default value is 'false' when creating a listing. This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOnEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on another e-commerce site at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  """
  soldOffEbay: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to change the boolean value of the **soldOnEbay** field, whose default value is 'false' when creating a listing. This field is only applicable for the Strikethrough Price feature, and is used to indicate whether or not the same item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price. If the Strikethrough Price feature is being used, either this field or the **soldOffEbay** field must be included and set to 'true', and it is acceptable for them both to be included and set to 'true'. Set this field to 'true' if the item was being sold on an eBay marketplace at the manufacturer suggested (OEM) retail price.
  """
  soldOnEbay: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
"""
input UpdateListingMotorVehicleDepositInput {
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the due date (in days) for the buyer to pay off the full balance of the motor vehicle. The clock starts on the full payment due date as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The supported values here are `DAYS_3` `DAYS_7`, `DAYS_10`, and `DAYS_14`.
  """
  daysToMakeFullPayment: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This field sets or modifies the deposit amount to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. This field is required if the seller is requiring a deposit. This deposit must be made immediately by the buyer if **immediatePay** is set to 'true', or within 24, 48, or 72 hours (set with **hoursToDeposit** field) if **immediatePay** is set to 'false'.
  **Max value**: 2000 USD (non-immediate pay), 500 USD (immediate pay)
  """
  depositAmount: Decimal
  """
  This boolean field is included and set to 'true' if the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle.
  **Note**: If a motor vehicle deposit is currently required for the motor vehicle listing, but the seller wants to disable, the field can be included and set to 'false'.
  """
  depositRequired: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to set the deadline (in hours) for the motor vehicle deposit. The deposit amount is specified in the **depositAmount** field. The clock starts on the deposit deadline as soon as the buyer commits to buying the vehicle by clicking the 'Buy It Now' button, by winning the auction, or by the seller accepting that buyer's Best Offer/counteroffer. The three supported integer values here are 24, 48, and 72 (hours). If **immediatePay** is 'true', and the listing qualifies for immediate payment (e.g. the 'Buy It Now' button is used), this field will not be applicable, since the buyer will be required to pay any deposit amount immediately (and not within 24, 48, and 72 hours).
  """
  hoursToDeposit: Int
}

"""
This type is needed for motor vehicle listings to provide the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
"""
input UpdateListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change the Vehicle Identifier Number (VIN) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  **Max length**: 17 characters.
  """
  vin: ID
  """
  This field is used to add or change the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) of the motor vehicle that is to be sold. The VIN or the VRM IDs are needed for motor vehicle listings.
  """
  vrm: ID
}

"""
This union type is used to represent the possible outcomes of the **updateListing** mutation. Three possible results of a **updateListing** mutation are: a listing container (and possibly one or more warnings); a listing container with validation success and possibly one or more warnings; or an array of blocking errors if the mutation fails and the listing is not updated. If a mutation fails, there will always be at least one blocking error, and there may also be one or more warning messages that are triggered.
"""
union UpdateListingOutput = UpdateListingSuccess | UpdateListingValidationError | UpdateListingValidationSuccess

"""
This type is used to override the shipping costs for one or more domestic or international shipping service options defined in the fulfillment business policy being used for the listing. The shipping costs provided will only affect the listing and will not update the fulfillment business policy.
"""
input UpdateListingOverrideShippingOptionInput {
  """
  This field is used to override the additional unit shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost when a buyer is purchasing multiple quantities of the same line item. Note that this value should never be higher than the base shipping cost.
  **Note**: If the additional shipping cost of the corresponding shipping service was already overriding the cost set up in the fulfillment business policy, the dollar value supplied here will replace that value.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to specify if the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field is a shipping service. The value of this field should be set to 'false' if the shipping service is a domestic shipping service, and 'true' if it is an international shipping service.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  internationalShippingOption: Boolean = false
  """
  The integer value specified here identifies the shipping service in the fulfillment business policy whose cost value(s) will be overridden. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 if overriding a shipping service option that ships within the marketplace or from 5 to 9 if overriding an shipping service option that ships outside of the marketplace. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page.
  """
  rank: Int!
  """
  This field is used to override the shipping cost set in the fulfillment business policy for the shipping service option identified through the corresponding **rank** field. The dollar value supplied here will be used when calculating the total shipping cost for the line item.
  **Note**: If the shipping cost of the corresponding shipping service was already overriding the cost set up in the fulfillment business policy, the dollar value supplied here will replace that value.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the dimensions of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. When specifying the dimensions of the shipping package, all three values (length, width, and height) are required. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
"""
input UpdateListingPackageDimensionsInput {
  """
  The height (or depth) of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  height: Float
  """
  The length of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  length: Float
  """
  The width of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is inches. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is centimeters. The precision of the dimension values is up to two decimal places.
  **Minimum value**: 0.1
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  width: Float
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the weight of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is pounds for **majorUnit** and ounces for **minorUnit**. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement is kilograms for **majorUnit** and grams for **minorUnit**.
"""
input UpdateListingPackageWeightInput {
  """
  The major weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The major weight value is the whole number part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is pounds. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **majorUnit** is kilograms.
  **Note**: If the package weighs less than one pound or one kilogram, *0* can be used as the value for this field.
  **Minimum value**: 0
  **Maximum value**: As allowed by the selected shipping service.
  """
  majorUnit: Int
  """
  The minor weight value of the shipping package according to the unit of measurement applicable to the marketplace. The minor weight value is the decimal part of the weight. For English measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is ounces. For Metric measurement system, the supported unit of measurement for **minorUnit** is grams.
  **Minimum value**: 0
  **Maximum value**: 15 for English measurement system (ounces); 999 for Metric measurement system (grams).
  """
  minorUnit: Int
}

"""
This type is used to modify various payment terms and information for the listing, including immediate payment requirement, offline payment methods, and motor vehicle deposit information. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a payment business policy with the listing.
"""
input UpdateListingPaymentTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change a payment business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all payment settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getPaymentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/payment_policy/methods/getPaymentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all payment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
  This field is included to enable or disable the immediate payment requirement for fixed price listings and auction listings where the 'Buy it Now' option is used.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  immediatePay: Boolean
  """
  This container is used when the seller requires a deposit to secure the purchase of a motor vehicle. The settings under this container include the amount of the deposit, when the deposit is due, and when the full payment of the motor vehicle is due.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  motorVehicleDeposit: UpdateListingMotorVehicleDepositInput
  """
  This field is used if the seller wants to add or modify instructions related to payment.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite existing payment instructions if defined in the listing.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  **Max length**: 500 characters.
  """
  paymentInstructions: String
  """
  This array is used to modify the list of offline payment methods for listings that support offline transactions. Use the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method to see the payment methods supported for a leaf category.
  **Note**: The full list of payment methods must be included in the array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  paymentMethods: [ListingPaymentMethod!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the primary eBay category for the listing, and optionally, add or modify a secondary eBay category and/or eBay store categories. If a seller has an eBay store and does not specify a store primary category ID, eBay will automatically put that listing into the default *Other* category in the seller's eBay store.
"""
input UpdateListingProductCategoriesInput {
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to change the eBay primary category of the listing. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  **Note**: If the eBay primary category is being changed, it is recommended that the user check to see if the optional, recommended, and required aspects are different for that new category and to make adjustments as needed.
  """
  primaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to add or change the eBay secondary category of the listing. The [getCategoryTree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategoryTree) or [getCategorySubtree](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getCategorySubtree) methods of the [Taxonomy API](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/methods) can be used to retrieve leaf category IDs. The **leafCategoryTreeNode** boolean field indicates which categories are leaf categories.
  """
  secondaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to change the eBay store primary category of the listing. If this field was not specified during the original creation of the listing, the listing is placed in the default *Other* category of the seller's eBay store. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storePrimaryCategoryId: ID
  """
  This field is used if the seller wishes to add or change the eBay store secondary of the listing. This field is optional, but if specified, it must be a valid eBay store category ID. The [getStoreCategories](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/resources/store/methods/getStoreCategories) method of the [Stores API Overview](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/stores/overview.html) can be used to retrieve the unique store category IDs for the seller.
  **Note**: eBay Stores can have up to three levels of store categories. Listings must only be placed in a store's terminal categories.
  """
  storeSecondaryCategoryId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify a Global Trade Item Number (GTIN) or an eBay product ID (ePID), and eBay will attempt to match to and leverage the product details of a product defined in eBay's product catalog. The user can directly provide the identifier of the eBay catalog product, or they can provide a GTIN value that can possibly be matched to an eBay catalog product. When an eBay catalog product is used, the product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that product will update the active or scheduled listing.
"""
input UpdateListingProductIdentifiersInput {
  """
  The unique identifier of an eBay catalog product. If this field is provided, the title, description, item specifics, and stock photo defined for that eBay product will be used in the resultant listing, overriding the seller provided information. The [search](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/catalog/resources/product_summary/methods/search) method of the **Catalog API** can be used to search for eBay catalog products and get their IDs.
  """
  ebayProductId: ID
  """
  This container is used to add or modify a UPC, EAN, or ISBN value for a product, and optionally, try to match the value to an eBay catalog product so that the product details of that catalog product will be used to update an active or scheduled listing.
  """
  globalIdentifiers: UpdateListingGlobalProductIdentifiersInput
  """
     This field controls whether or not an eBay catalog product is leveraged to update a listing with that catalog product's details, including product title, product description, item specifics, and stock photo. If you want to use an eBay catalog product to update your listing, you can either set this field to true or omit it entirely, as true is the default value. If you provide a GTIN (Global Trade Item Number) or eBay Product ID but do not want to use the corresponding eBay catalog product to update your listing, you must set this field to false.
  **Default value**: true
  """
  includeEbayProductDetails: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify common product details for the listing, including title, description, listing category, condition, product aspects, images, and more.
"""
input UpdateListingProductInput {
  """
  This array is used to update the existing set of name-value pairs that define the product aspects. The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method can be used to see which aspects are required, recommended, or optional for a leaf category. This method also returns typical values for an aspect name and will indicate if an aspect name supports multiple values or just one value. For a multiple-SKU listing, only the common aspects will be specified in this array, and the pivoting aspects (aka traits) will be specified at the item level.
  **Note**: If any changes are being made to product aspects, the full set of aspect name-value pairs that you wish to be on the listing must be included, and not just the aspects that are being added or modified.
  **Max value**: 65 characters for each aspect name and value.
  """
  aspects: [NameValuesPairInput]
  """
  This container is used to change the primary eBay category for the listing, and optionally, add or modify a secondary eBay category and/or eBay store categories.
  """
  categories: UpdateListingProductCategoriesInput
  """
  This field is used to update the listing description. HTML markup and inline CSS can be used. However, a seller can not use any active content in their listing description. Active content includes animation or video via JavaScript, Flash, plug-ins, or form actions. All active content will be blocked/removed from a listing. Sellers are only allowed to provide links to product videos, freight shipping services, or other legally required information, and when providing these links in the listing description, the secure 'https' protocol must be used instead of 'http'. In addition, any valid links to sites outside of eBay should use the target="_blank" attribute in the a href tag so a new browser window will be loaded when the link is clicked instead of buyers being redirected off of eBay.
  **Note**: If this field is used, all text provided in this field will completely overwrite the current listing description.
  **Max length**: 500,000 characters (including all markup tags/CSS)
  """
  description: String
  """
  This array is used to update the list of image URLs that will become photos in the listing's photo gallery. Most eBay categories support up to 24 photos per listing at no extra charge. The URLs used in this array must use 'https'. Either all eBay Picture Services (EPS) or all self-hosted picture URLs may be used in this array, but not a combination of both.
  **Note**: The full set of image URLs that you wish to be images in the listing must be included, and not just the images that are being added.
  **Max images allowed on a listing**: 24
  """
  imageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]
  """
  This container is used to change the condition of the item, to add or modify the condition description for a used item, or to make any changes to the condition descriptor data for a single trading cards listing.
  """
  itemCondition: UpdateListingItemConditionInput
  """
  This container is used to add or update the list of motor vehicles or assemblies that are compatible with a Parts & Accessories item. This structured compatibility information helps buyers filter and find parts that are compatible with their specific vehicles. Year, Make, and Model are typical aspects used to identify a motor vehicle.
  **Max compatibilities allowed on a listing**: 3000
  """
  listingCompatibilities: UpdateListingItemCompatibilitiesInput
  """
  This container is needed for motor vehicle listings and is used to add or change the Vehicle Identification Number (VIN) or the Vehicle Registration Mark (VRM) for the motor vehicle.
  """
  motorVehicleIdentifier: UpdateListingMotorVehicleIdentifierInput
  """
  This field is used to update the product title displayed on the listing. If this field is used, the text in this field will overwrite the current listing title.
  **Max length**: 80 characters.
  """
  title: String
  """
  This array is used to add or replace a seller's video to the listing. A unique identifier for a seller's video is passed into this array to add a product video to the listing. Although a video can be added to a listing before it is in the `LIVE` state, the video won't be available for viewing in the listing until it does reach this state. To know more about the video upload process and various states for a video, see the [Media API documentation](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/media/overview).
  **Note**: Currently, only one video may be added to each listing.
  **Note**: If a video is already associated with a listing, but a new video ID is passed into this field, that video will replace the current one. To remove the current video and not add a new one, include this array as empty and the current video will be removed.
  **Max videos allowed on a listing**: 1
  """
  videoIds: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify product safety information for an item, including product safety statements and pictograms. The [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
"""
input UpdateListingProductSafetyInput {
  """
  This free-form text field is used to add or modify additional product safety information that goes beyond what is expressed through the pictogram(s) and/or safety statements.
  **Note**: This field cannot be used without the **pictogramCodes** and/or **statementCodes** arrays.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current additional info text if it exists for the listing.
  **Max length**: 120 characters
  """
  additionalInformation: String
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to four product safety pictogram codes, and if successful, the pictogram(s) associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes, and this method will also return the URLs to the pictograms so that these pictograms can be previewed before adding them to a listing.
  **Note**: All pictogram codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of pictogram codes allowed**: 4 pictograms.
  **Max length of each pictogram code**: 15 characters.
  """
  pictogramCodes: [ID!]
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one to eight product safety statement codes, and if successful, the safety statements associated with these codes will be displayed on the View Item page. The [getProductSafetyLabels](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getProductSafetyLabels) method can be used to get these codes and the safety statements associated with them.
  **Note**: All statement codes that the seller wishes to associate with the listing should be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of statement codes allowed**: 8 statements.
  **Max length of each statement code**: 15 characters.
  """
  statementCodes: [ID!]
}

"""
This type is used to attach one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
"""
input UpdateListingRegionalProductCompliancePoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to add or modify one or more country-specific product compliance policies.
  **Note**: All country-specific product compliance policies that the seller wants to be attached to the listing should be included in this array, and not just any new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of product compliance policies allowed per marketplace**: 6.
  """
  countryPolicies: [UpdateListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or change country-specific takeback policies. Each country may only have one specific takeback policy.
"""
input UpdateListingRegionalTakebackPoliciesInput {
  """
  This array is used to specify a country-specific takeback policy. Each country may only have one country-specific takeback policy.
  **Note**: All country-specific takeback policies that the seller would like to apply to the listing must be included in this array, and not just the new policies being added.
  **Max number of takeback policies allowed per marketplace**: 1.
  """
  countryPolicies: [UpdateListingCountryPolicyInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
"""
input UpdateListingRegulatoryInput {
  """
  This array is used to attach one or more documents to the listing using their unique identifiers. The **Media API** is used to upload documents to a seller's account. See the [DocumentTypeEnum](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/media/types/api:DocumentTypeEnum) type of the **Media API** for the full list of supported document types.
  **Note**: The document ID values for all documents that the seller would like to attach to the updated listing must be included in this array, and not just the new ones that are being added.
  **Max number of document IDs allowed**: 10.
  **Max length of each document ID**: 50 characters.
  """
  documentIds: [ID!]
  """
  This container is used to add or modify Energy Efficiency Label related information for such category types as appliances, smart phones, and tablets. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend Energy Efficiency Label information.
  """
  energyEfficiencyLabel: UpdateListingEnergyEfficiencyLabelInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify hazardous material related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend hazardous material information.
  """
  hazardousMaterial: UpdateListingHazardousMaterialInput
  """
  This container is used to add a product manufacturer contact or to update any of the data currently associated with the product manufacturer that is already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide product manufacturer information in their eBay listings.
  """
  manufacturer: UpdateListingManufacturerInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify product safety related information about a product, including pictograms and statements. Use the [getRegulatoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getRegulatoryPolicies) method to see which leaf categories require or recommend product safety information.
  """
  productSafety: UpdateListingProductSafetyInput
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the manufacturer's repair index score for a product. This value should be between 0.1 (extremely difficult to fix) to 10 (extremely easy to fix). A maximum of one digit to the right of the decimal point may be used. 0 or 0.0 should never be used as values as this would indicate that the product is not repairable.
  **Min value**: 0.1
  **Max value**: 10.0
  """
  repairIndexScore: Float
  """
  This array is used to add one or more responsible person contacts or to update any of the data currently associated with one or more of the responsible person entities that are already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide either the product manufacturer or responsible person(s) contact information in their eBay listings. This array is only necessary if the product manufacturer contact is not based in an EU country.
  **Note**: If the listing already has one or more responsible persons defined, all current data must be included in the array, even the data that is not changing.
  **Max number of EU responsible persons allowed**: 5.
  """
  responsiblePersons: [UpdateListingResponsiblePersonInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to add one or more responsible person contacts or to update any of the data currently associated with one or more of the responsible person entities that are already defined in the listing. As a part of General Product Safety Regulation (GPSR) requirements, sellers operating in, or shipping to EU-based countries or Northern Ireland are conditionally required to provide either the product manufacturer or responsible person(s) contact information in their eBay listings.
"""
input UpdateListingResponsiblePersonInput {
  """
  This container is used to add or modify a street address for a responsible person.
  """
  address: UpdateListingBusinessEntityAddressInput
  """
  This field is used to add or modify the company name associated with the responsible person.
  **Max length**: 100 characters.
  """
  companyName: String!
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the phone number, email address, and/or the Contact/Support page URL for the responsible person. At least one of the three is required if a responsible person is supplied.
  """
  contact: UpdateListingBusinessEntityContactInput
  """
  This array is required for each responsible person specified, and the only allowed value is `EU_RESPONSIBLE_PERSON`.
  **Max number of person types allowed**: 1.
  """
  personTypes: [String!]!
}

"""
This container is used to add or modify a domestic return policy or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
"""
input UpdateListingReturnTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to add or change a return business policy to use for the listing. If this field is used, none of the other fields in this container should be used since all return policy settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/return_policy/methods/getReturnPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all return business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicyId: ID
  """
  This container is used to modify the seller's domestic return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
  **Note**: If the listing only has a domestic return policy set up, but the item is shipped internationally, the settings in this container will also apply to international returns.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  domesticReturnTerms: UpdateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the seller's international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  """
  internationalReturnTerms: UpdateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput
  """
  This free-form text field is used to add or modify details about a seller's return policy. Currently, this field is only supported on the EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT, EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, and EBAY_ES marketplaces.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite existing return instructions if defined in the listing.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if the seller is using business policies.
  **Max length**: 8000 (for EBAY_DE, EBAY_AT); 5000 (for EBAY_FR, EBAY_IT, EBAY_ES).
  """
  returnInstructions: String
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify the seller's domestic or international return policy for a listing, which includes whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item and the duration of the return period.
"""
input UpdateListingReturnTermsOptionsInput {
  """
  This field specifies the refund method that will be used if the buyer returns the item. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item. Currently, the only supported value for this field is `MONEY_BACK`.
  **Note**: Although `MONEY_BACK_OR_REPLACEMENT` is defined in the schema, replacement items are not currently supported in Returns flow, so `MONEY_BACK` is the only option.
  """
  refundMethod: ListingRefundMethod
  """
  This field is used to indicate whether or not the seller accepts returns for the item. This field set to 'true' if the seller accepts returns for the item or 'false' if the seller does not accept returns for the item.
  """
  returnAccepted: Boolean
  """
  This field specifies the amount of time the buyer has to return an item. The return duration begins when the item is marked 'delivered' at the buyer's specified ship-to location. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and sets the number of days that a buyer has to return the item for a full refund. Supported values are `DAYS_14`, `DAYS_30`, and `DAYS_60`. The supported return periods can vary by category (with `DAYS_14` limited to just a few categories), and the [getReturnPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getReturnPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** can be used to see the supported return periods for a category.
  """
  returnDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This field specifies either the buyer or the seller as the party who pays for return shipping charges. This field must be included if the seller accepts returns for the item, and specifies the person responsible for return shipping costs if the item is returned due to a buyer remorse. See [`Invoicee`] for the list of supported enumeration values. The seller is always responsible for return shipping costs when an item is being returned due to a Significantly not as described (SNAD) issue.
  """
  returnShipmentInvoicee: Invoicee
}

"""
This type is used to specify the days and times when a seller may be contacted regarding a classified ad listing. This container is used by the **primarySellerContactHours** and **secondarySellerContactHours** containers and the days specified here should not overlap between the two.
"""
input UpdateListingSellerContactHoursInput {
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller is available the full 24 hours on the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. If this field is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  anyTime: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to indicate the end time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursEndAt** value should always be later than the **supportHoursStartAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursEndAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to indicate the start time of support hours for the days specified through the **supportOnDays** field. Military time should be used here and times should be on the hour or half hour (e.g. 9:00, 9:30, etc.). The **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields are always used together and the **supportHoursStartAt** value should always be earlier than the **supportHoursEndAt** value.
  **Note**: If the **anyTime** is set to 'true', the **supportHoursStartAt** and **supportHoursEndAt** fields should not be used.
  """
  supportHoursStartAt: Time
  """
  This field is used to specify the block of days that the support hours will apply to. See [`ListingDaysCode`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  supportOnDays: ListingDaysCode
}

"""
This type is used for classified ad listings, and provides contact information for the seller, including days and hours when the seller accepts inquiries from potential buyers.
"""
input UpdateListingSellerContactInput {
  """The first line of the street address of the seller."""
  addressLine1: String
  """
  The second line of the seller's street address. This field is not always used, but can be used for secondary address information such as 'Suite Number' or 'Apt Number'.
  """
  addressLine2: String
  """
  This field adds or modifies the company name (if any) associated with the seller.
  """
  companyName: String @deprecated(reason: "Company name is no longer supported")
  """
  This field is used to indicate whether potential buyers can contact the seller via email. A value of 'true' in this field indicates that potential buyers can contact the seller of the listing via email.
  """
  contactByEmailEnabled: Boolean
  """
  Two-letter [ISO 3166 Country Codes](https://www.iso.org/iso-3166-country-codes.html) to indicate which country the seller is located.
  """
  country: CountryAlpha2Code
  """The county where the seller resides."""
  county: String
  """The seller's phone number."""
  phone: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the seller's primary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekdays. This container should always be provided to let potential buyers know when the seller may be contacted.
  """
  primarySellerContactHours: UpdateListingSellerContactHoursInput
  """
  This container is used to provide the seller's secondary support days and hours. This will generally be used to show support hours on weekends if the support hours vary on weekends.
  """
  secondarySellerContactHours: UpdateListingSellerContactHoursInput
}

"""
This type is used to modify information on domestic and international shipping, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated) and the shipping service options available to ship the item. There is also a field to add or change a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
"""
input UpdateListingShippingOptionsInput {
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  **Note**: To remove the existing combined shipping rule, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  combinedShippingRuleId: ID
  """
  This field is used to change the shipping cost type for locations within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping. Note that all of the specified shipping services should support the shipping cost type specified here.
  **Note**: To specify local pick only option for listings, set this field to `NOT_SPECIFIED`.
  """
  costType: ListingShippingType
  """
  This field is included to add, modify, or remove a flat-rate handling cost for shipping. This cost is in addition to whatever the final shipping cost is based on the buyer's location and selected shipping service option.
  **Note**: To remove the existing package handling cost, include this field and set value to '0.0'.
  """
  packageHandlingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable a seller's promotional shipping discount for the listing. A seller can only have one promotional shipping discount active on a marketplace. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the details of the promotional shipping discount, and the [SetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/SetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to add/modify the promotional shipping discount.
  """
  promotionalShipping: Boolean
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping rate table, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  rateTableId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use shippingRateTableId instead")
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a specific flat or calculated shipping discount for the listing. The numeric identifier for the shipping discount is passed into this field. The [GetShippingDiscountProfiles](https://developer.ebay.com/devzone/xml/docs/Reference/eBay/GetShippingDiscountProfiles.html) call can be used to retrieve the numeric IDs of the shipping discounts defined for the seller's account. The shipping cost type must match the shipping discount type being enabled or the shipping discount will not be active in the listing.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping discount profile, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  shippingDiscountRuleId: ID @deprecated(reason: "Use combinedShippingRuleId instead")
  """
  This field is included to add, change or remove a location within marketplace and outside of marketplace shipping rate table for the listing. Shipping rate tables let sellers customize flat-rate shipping costs based on buyer's location and selected shipping service level. The numeric identifier for the shipping rate table is passed into this field. The numeric IDs for a seller's shipping rate tables can be retrieved with the [getRateTables](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTables) method, and details on a specific shipping rate table can be retrieved with the [getRateTable](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/getRateTable) method. The [updateShippingCost](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/v2/resources/rate_table/methods/updateShippingCost) method can be used to modify the shipping costs for a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: The shipping cost type must be set to flat-rate to use a shipping rate table.
  **Note**: To remove the existing shipping rate table, include this field and leave value as empty.
  """
  shippingRateTableId: ID
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify information about the shipping package that will be used to ship the item, and includes package type, weight, and dimensions.
"""
input UpdateListingShippingPackageSpecificationsInput {
  """
  This field should be included if the seller wants to mark the shipping package as irregular size or if the seller wishes to undo this setting. A shipping carrier may charge additional handling fees for an irregular package.
  """
  irregularPackage: Boolean
  """
  The measurement system used by the marketplace for the package dimensions and weight. If the value is not supplied, the default measurement system for the marketplace will be used. See [`MeasurementSystem`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  measurementSystem: MeasurementSystem
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the dimensions of the shipping package.
  """
  packageDimensions: UpdateListingPackageDimensionsInput
  """
  This field is used to change the type of package used to ship the item. See [`ListingPackageType`] for the list of supported enumeration values.
  """
  packageType: ListingPackageType
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the weight of the shipping package. The weight of the shipping package is required when the listing is using the calculated shipping cost type.
  """
  packageWeight: UpdateListingPackageWeightInput
}

"""
This type is used to modify the list of domestic or international shipping service options that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
"""
input UpdateListingShippingServiceInput {
  """
  This field adds or modifies the flat-rate shipping cost to ship each additional unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for multiple-quantity, fixed price listings using flat-rate shipping. The cost specified in this field must be the same or lower than the cost specified in the **shippingCost** field, with the idea being that multiple quantities of the line item might be shipped in the same shipping package, decreasing the per-unit cost for shipping.
  """
  additionalUnitShippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This array is used to add or modify the list of geographical regions or individual countries that the corresponding international shipping service operates in.
  **Note**: The full list of shipping locations must be included with each update operation, and not just the ones that are being added.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  The integer value specified here controls the order in which the corresponding shipping service will be displayed in the View Item page. This should be a positive integer from 1 to 4 for a shipping service that ships within the marketplace or from 5 to 9 for a shipping service that ships outside of marketplace. A rank value of '1' means it is the first shipping option displayed in the View Item page. If this field is not used, the rank and hence order of the shipping services will depend on the order they are specified under the **shippingServices** array.
  """
  rank: Int
  """
  This field adds or modifies the flat-rate shipping cost to ship one unit of the item using the corresponding shipping service. This field is required for each shipping service if flat-rate shipping is being used. This field must still be included and set to '0.0' if the corresponding shipping service is offered free of charge to the buyer.
  """
  shippingCost: Decimal
  """
  This field identifies the domestic or international shipping service and is required for each specified shipping service. Use the [getShippingServices](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices) method to retrieve the full list of domestic and international shipping services supported on a marketplace. The enumeration values representing each shipping service option are returned in the [shippingService](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/shipping:marketplace/methods/getShippingServices#response.shippingServices.shippingService) fields of the **getShippingServices** response.
  """
  shippingServiceCode: ID
}

"""
This type is used to modify information about where the item can be shipped, the shipping cost type, the shipping services offered, the handling time, applicable shipping discounts, and more.
"""
input UpdateListingShippingTermsInput {
  """
  This field is used to provide information about the shipping business policy to be used for the listing.
  If this field is used, none of the other fields in UpdateListingShippingTermsInput container should be used since all shipping settings are configured in the business policy instead. The [getFulfillmentPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/account/resources/fulfillment_policy/methods/getFulfillmentPolicies) method can be used to retrieve all fulfillment business policies defined for a seller on an eBay marketplace.
  """
  businessPolicy: UpdateShippingBusinessPolicyInput
  """
  This field is only applicable to motor vehicle listings and indicates if the buyer is responsible for shipping or picking up the purchased vehicle.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  buyerResponsibleForShipping: Boolean
  """
  This array is used to add or modify locations where the seller will not ship the item. The values specified in this array can be continents, geographical regions, countries, or special locations within the marketplace. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: The entire array of excluded shipping locations must be included for an update, and not just locations that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  excludedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This field indicates how many business days that the seller needs to ship the item after payment is made by the buyer. The handling time is required by most categories. Top-rated sellers typically set the handling time to 0 or 1 day, but longer handling times are supported.
  **Note**: This field is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  handlingTimeDuration: ListingTimeDuration
  """
  This array is used to add or modify locations where the seller will ship the item. The values specified in this array can be continents, geographical regions or countries. The **excludedShipToLocations** and **includedShipToLocations** lists should not contradict one another. If there is a contradiction between the shipping exclusions and inclusions, the exclusion usually takes precedence. This means if a location is both included and excluded, it will be treated as excluded.
  **Note**: The entire array of shipping locations must be included for an update, and not just locations that are being added.
  **Note**: This array is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  includedShipToLocations: [ListingShippingLocationInput!]
  """
  This container is used to modify information on shipping local to the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to add or change a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  marketplaceShippingOptions: UpdateListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This container is used to modify information on shipping not local to the marketplace, including the shipping cost type used (flat vs. calculated). There is also a field to specify a shipping rate table to use against the listings and fields to add or change a shipping discount.
  **Note**: This container is not applicable if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  nonMarketplaceShippingOptions: UpdateListingShippingOptionsInput
  """
  This field is used to provide information of shipping services that are available to the buyer for shipment of the item, and the costs associated with using each one. Each available shipping service option is identified through the **shippingServiceCode** field.
  **Maximum number of shipping services**: 10, out of which 5 apply for locations within the marketplace and other 5 apply for locations outside of marketplace
  **Note**: This array is not needed if business policies are being used by the seller.
  """
  shippingServices: [UpdateListingShippingServiceInput!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **updateListing** mutation that is run in `EXECUTE` mode. It will show the complete details of the updated listing, and will also include a list of non-blocking warning messages if any occurred.
"""
type UpdateListingSuccess {
  """This container shows the complete details of the updated listing."""
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows the type of discount(s) applied to listing fees, if any.
  """
  listingDiscount: [ListingFeeDiscount!]
  """
  This array shows the list of estimated listing fees that the updated listing will incur.
  **Note**: Always consider the fee amounts to be estimated only.
  """
  listingFees: [SellerListingFee!]
  """
  This array shows the list of non-blocking warnings triggered by the mutation request, if any occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify various tax information, including VAT rates, sales tax rates tor US territories and Canadian provinces, and special tax category codes.
"""
input UpdateListingTaxTermsInput {
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller wants the sales tax rate for the jurisdiction to apply to the cumulative amount of item cost and shipping charges, or set to 'false' if the seller does not want sales tax to apply to shipping charges. This field is only applicable if the **salesTaxPercentage** and **salesTaxJurisdictionId** fields are also set.
  """
  salesTaxApplicableToShipping: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to specify a US territory or a Canadian province that will be charged the sales tax rate specified in the **salesTaxPercentage** field. The supported US territories are `AS` (America Samoa), `GU` (Guam), `MP` (Northern Mariana Islands), `PW` (Palau), and `VI` (US Virgin Islands). The two-letter codes for Canadian provinces can be found here on the [Government of Canada](https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/tax/businesses/topics/completing-slips-summaries/financial-slips-summaries/return-investment-income-t5/provincial-territorial-codes.html) website.
  **Note**: Sales tax rates are only applicable on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA and EBAY_CAFR marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxJurisdictionId: String
  """
  This field is used along with **salesTaxJurisdictionId** field to set or modify the sales tax rate for a specific US territory or a Canadian province. The percentage set here will be applied to sale price as the sales tax for the order line item. The value passed in is stored with a precision of 1 digits after the decimal point.
  **Note**: Sales tax rates are only applicable on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA and EBAY_CAFR marketplaces.
  """
  salesTaxPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if the seller has an account level sales tax table set up and wishes to use the sales tax rates set up in that table. If this field is set to 'true', the values contained in the other sales tax fields (if set) in this container will be overridden by the values set in the sales tax table.
  """
  salesTaxTableUsed: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to provide a special category of tax such as a recycling fee or disposal tax.
  """
  thirdPartyTaxCategoryCode: String
  """
  This field is used to set or modify the VAT (Value-added Tax) percentage rate that will be charged to buyers when an item is purchased from the listing. VAT is not applicable to all countries, including the US. Allowed VAT percentage rates can vary by region/country, so sellers should be aware of the rates they are legally required/allowed to charge, and they are responsible for charging the correct VAT rate. Only one digit is allowed to the right of the decimal point.
  """
  vatPercentage: Decimal
  """
  This field should be included and set to 'true' if the seller is registered on the listing site as a Business Seller and intends to use listing features that are offered to business users only. This field must be included and set to 'true' if the **vatRestrictedToBusinessUser** field is also included and set to 'true'.
  """
  vatRecognizedBusinessSeller: Boolean
  """
  This field is included and set to 'true' if a business seller wishes to make the listing exclusively available to potential buyers registered on eBay as business users. This feature is only applicable to business sellers residing in Germany, Austria, or Switzerland who are listing in a B2B VAT-enabled category on the eBay Germany (EBAY_DE), Austria (EBAY_AT), or Switzerland (EBAY_CH) marketplaces. To set this field as 'true', the **vatRecognizedBusinessSeller** field must also be included and set to 'true'.
  """
  vatRestrictedToBusinessUser: Boolean
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify listing terms details for the listing, including listing duration, item location, return policy, fulfillment terms, and more.
"""
input UpdateListingTermsInput {
  """
  This container is used for classified ad listings, and adds or modifies contact information for the seller, including days and hours when the seller accepts inquiries from potential buyers.
  """
  adsSellerContact: UpdateListingSellerContactInput
  """
  This container is used if the seller wishes to make changes to **Best Offer** settings, including enabling or disabling the Best Offer feature, or to add, modify, or remove the auto-accept and auto-reject thresholds.
  """
  bestOfferTerms: UpdateListingBestOfferTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to disable or enable a seller's account-level buyer restrictions and/or set or modify a quantity limit per buyer threshold for a multiple-quantity, fixed price listing.
  """
  buyerRestrictions: UpdateListingBuyerRestrictionsInput
  """
  This container is used if the seller wishes to make the listing a charitable listing, or if a charity is already set up, this container is used to change the charitable organization and/or the donation percentage per sale.
  **Note**: eBay for Charity is only supported on the eBay US, eBay UK, eBay Germany, and eBay Canada marketplaces.
  """
  charity: UpdateListingCharityInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify global or country-specific product compliance and/or takeback policies for a listing.
  """
  customPolicies: UpdateListingCustomPoliciesInput
  """
  This container is used to modify details on how the item will be delivered to the buyer. The data under this container includes available shipping services, ship-to and excluded shipping locations, shipping costs, package details, and more. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a fulfillment business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies.
  """
  fulfillmentTerms: UpdateListingFulfillmentTermsInput
  """
  This field can be included and set to 'true' if the seller wishes to make the listing private. With private listings, the eBay user and feedback scores for bidders and buyers are obfuscated to everyone except for the seller. If the scheduled or active listing is currently marked as a private listing and the seller does not wish to keep this setting, this field should be included and set to 'false'.
  """
  hideParticipation: Boolean
  """
  This array can be used if the seller wishes to add or modify site visibility settings. With site visibility, sellers can choose to actively display their listing on one or more other eBay marketplaces for a small fee. Currently, this feature can only be used on the EBAY_US, EBAY_CA, EBAY_GB, and EBAY_IE marketplaces. EBAY_US and EBAY_CA listings can specify `EBAY_GB` and `EBAY_IE` in this array to have their listing displayed on the EBAY_GB and EBAY_IE marketplaces, and EBAY_GB and EBAY_IE listings can specify `EBAY_US` and `EBAY_CA` in this array to have their listing display on the EBAY_US and EBAY_CA marketplaces.
  """
  internationalSiteVisibility: [CrossBorderTradingRegion!]
  """
  This container is used to change the actual physical location of the item(s) in this listing. The **country** field is always required, and then either the **location** or **postalCode** must be provided, but not necessarily both.
  """
  itemLocation: UpdateListingItemLocationInput
  """
  This container is used to change the duration of the listing, and can also be used to modify the future date when a scheduled listing will become active.
  """
  lifecycleTerms: UpdateListingLifecycleTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify the radius for a Motors Local Listing. The value supplied in the **distance** field sets the radius of the area in which the vehicle will be available and exposed to interested local buyers. The seller's supplied **postalCode** or **location** field value will be used as the center point for this radius. You can use the [getMotorsListingPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getMotorsListingPolicies) method of the **Metadata API** to get the supported listing distance values for a leaf category. Seller provide the unit of measurement for the **distance** value through the **distanceUnit** field.
  """
  localListingDistance: UpdateListingLocalDistanceInput
  """
  This field is needed to modify the lot size for the lot-enabled listing. With lot-enabled listing, the seller is selling a set of two or more similar/related items as a part of one listing. An example of a lot listing might be a collection of children's clothes. The value specified in this field will be the number of distinct items in the lot. Not all leaf categories support lot listings, and the [getCategoryPolicies](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/sell/metadata/resources/marketplace/methods/getCategoryPolicies) method can be used to see which leaf categories do support lot listings.
  **Min value**: 2
  **Max value**: 450,000
  """
  lotSize: Int
  """
  A reference identifier used to attribute the source of data across API families. This ID is returned in the response of the **listingPreviewsCreationTaskById** query of the **Inventory Mapping API**. To ensure continuity and traceability of the data flow, it is strongly recommend that you include this reference ID in any create, update, or relist mutation. Using this ID associates any mutations with the listing preview referenced to create or update the listing.
  **Max length**: 25
  """
  mappingReferenceId: String
  """
  This container is used to modify payment terms and information for the listing, including immediate payment requirement, offline payment methods, and motor vehicle deposit information. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a payment business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies. This container is optional for sellers not opted into business policies.
  """
  paymentTerms: UpdateListingPaymentTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to add or modify various types of regulatory information for a listing, including energy efficiency labels, hazardous material information, product safety information, and more. Based on the listing category, sellers doing business in an EU country or Northern Ireland may be legally required to provide some of this regulatory information for listings.
  """
  regulatory: UpdateListingRegulatoryInput
  """
  This container is used to modify a domestic return policy and/or an international return policy (if the seller ships internationally) that is to be used for the listing. This container also has a **businessPolicyId** field that is used to associate a return business policy with the listing, and that must be used instead of the other fields in this container if the seller's account is opted into business policies. With the exception of a few categories, this container is generally required even if the seller's *return policy* is to not accept returns.
  """
  returnTerms: UpdateListingReturnTermsInput
  """
  This field is used by the seller to add or modify custom, application-specific data associated with the listing. The string specified here is stored by eBay with the listing but it is not used by eBay in any way other than that.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text provided will overwrite the custom data text that is currently associated with the listing.
  **Max length**: 32
  """
  sellerCustomData: String
  """
  This container is used to add or modify various tax information, including VAT rates, sales tax rates to US territories and Canadian provinces, and special tax category codes.
  """
  taxTerms: UpdateListingTaxTermsInput
  """
  This container is used to enable or disable Bold Title or Gallery Plus listing upgrades, or to add, modify, or remove a Subtitle. Each of these listing upgrades will incur a small fee.
  **Note**: If any of these listing upgrades are currently active on the listing but the seller chooses to disable one or more of them, the seller will generally not receive a refund against the fee that was charged for these listing upgrades when they were first added to the listing.
  """
  visualEnhancements: UpdateListingVisualEnhancementsInput
}

"""
This type is used when the **updateListing** mutation fails due to one or more blocking validation errors. A list of validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying will be shown, and one or more non-blocking warning messages will also be shown if any were triggered during the processing of the mutation.
"""
type UpdateListingValidationError implements BusinessError {
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. This code can be used by clients to programmatically identify and handle different types of errors without relying on error messages, which may change over time.     
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """
  A human-readable message describing the error. This message is intended for developers and should not be displayed directly to end users. It provides additional context about what went wrong and may include suggestions for how to resolve the issue.
  """
  errorMessage: String!
  """
  This array contains a list of blocking validation rule violations that must be fixed before retrying.
  """
  violations: [ListingValidationRuleViolation!]!
  """
  This array contains a list of non-blocking validation warnings that do not block processing but provide useful feedback for improving listings.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used for a successful **updateListing** mutation that is run in `VALIDATE` mode, and the listing object is successfully validated without any errors. The results of the validation will be shown, including warnings if any occurred.
"""
type UpdateListingValidationSuccess {
  """
  This container shows the complete details of the validated listing object.
  """
  listing: SellerListing!
  """
  This array shows the type of discount(s) applied to the expected fees, if any.
  """
  listingDiscount: [ListingFeeDiscount!]
  """
  This array shows the list of estimated listing fees that the listing object would occur if updated.
  """
  listingFees: [SellerListingFee!]
  """
  This array shows the list of non-blocking warnings generated during the validation, if any occurred.
  """
  warnings: [ListingWarning!]
}

"""
This type is used to identify or modify the main trait by which SKUs within a multiple-variation listing differ, and to provide image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each item variation.
"""
input UpdateListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput {
  """
  The trait name by which pictures of the item variations vary. The specified trait will be used to determine which images to display when a buyer selects a variation in the View Item page. For example, if the trait is 'Color', then a corresponding product image in the **traitValueImages** array will be displayed when that color is selected in the View Item page. The trait name specified here must be one of the variation traits specified in the **variationTraits** array.
  **Max length**: 65 characters.
  """
  traitName: String!
  """
  This array is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the *traitImageUrls** array.
  **Note**: The full list of trait value images must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  """
  traitValueImages: [UpdateListingVariationTraitValueImageInput!]!
}

"""
This type is used to add or modify name-value pairs for the traits where each SKU within a multiple-SKU listing differs, such as 'Color' and 'Size'. Each available color and each available size will be listed through the **variationTraits** array. If the listing featured t-shirts, each variation within that listing would have a unique color and size combination such as 'Blue, Large'.
"""
input UpdateListingVariationsInput {
  """
  This container identifies the main trait by which variations differ, and provides image URLs demonstrating the variations of this trait for each variation. For example, the varying trait may be 'Color', and image URLs would be provided showcasing the different color of each variation.
  """
  imagesVaryByTrait: UpdateListingVariationImagesVaryByTraitInput
  """
  This array provides the names of the varying traits and the available values for each of these traits. For example, one trait might be 'Color', and all of the available colors would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. Another trait might be 'Size', and all of the available sizes would be specified in the corresponding **values** array. If the multiple-SKU listing has two varying traits such as 'Color' and 'Size', each variation would have a different combination of each of these traits, such as a 'Large, Red' shirt.
  The [getItemAspectsForCategory](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/getItemAspectsForCategory) method of the **Taxonomy API** can be used to retrieve aspects that are optional, recommended or required for a specific category. The  [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method in the **Taxonomy API** works similarly but is processed asynchronously and provides optional, recommended or required aspects every leaf category on an eBay marketplace. The [fetchItemAspects](https://developer.ebay.com/api-docs/commerce/taxonomy/resources/category_tree/methods/fetchItemAspects) method can be paired up with the **Taxonomy SDK** to help maintain an up-to-date list of aspects for each leaf category.
  **Note**: The full list of all variation traits and values must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  **Max number of traits**: 5.
  **max values per trait**: 50.
  **Max length of each trait name and value**: 65 characters.
  """
  variationTraits: [NameValuesPairInput!]
}

"""
This type is used to provide an array of one or more image URLs for each available value of the trait. So, if the trait is 'Color', each of the available colors would be specified through the **traitValue** field, and then each color would have at least one image URL specified through the **traitImageUrls** array.
"""
input UpdateListingVariationTraitValueImageInput {
  """
  An array of one or more images that demonstrate the corresponding **traitValue**. For example, if the **traitName** is 'Color' and the **traitValue** is 'Red', the image(s) would show a red variation of the product. Depending on the product, one image per variation may be enough, but multiple images may be specified for each **traitValue**. For example, it is possible that a seller would want to show the front and back of each shirt in each color.
  **Note**: The full list of image URLs must be included in this array, and not just the ones that are being added.
  **Note** All images, whether they are hosted by eBay Picture Server (EPS) or self-hosted, must comply with eBay picture requirements. eBay Picture Server (EPS) and self-hosted picture URLs should not be mixed, and all URLs must use 'https' and not 'http'.
  **Max number of images per trait value**: 12.
  """
  traitImageUrls: [HttpsUrl!]!
  """
  The trait value of the corresponding image(s) in the **traitImageUrls** array. If the **traitName** is 'Color', values in this field may include *Red*, *Blue*, *Green*, etc. At least one of the variations within the multiple-SKU listing must have this value.
  **Max length**: 65 characters.
  """
  traitValue: String!
}

"""
This type is used to enable or disable Bold Title or Gallery Plus listing upgrades, or to add, modify, or remove a Subtitle. Each of these listing upgrades will incur a small fee.
"""
input UpdateListingVisualEnhancementsInput {
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable the Bold Title listing upgrade. With this upgrade, the listing title will be in boldface type in search results for greater visibility.
  **Note**: If this listing upgrade is disabled for an active listing, the seller is generally not entitled to a refund against that fee.
  **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing as motor vehicle listing titles are automatically generated by eBay based on Year, Make, Model, and other aspects of the vehicle such as engine type and trim.
  """
  boldTitle: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to enable or disable the Gallery Plus feature. With Gallery Plus, a larger gallery image of the item is displayed in search results.
  **Note**: If the this listing upgrade is disabled for an active listing, the seller is generally not entitled to a refund against that fee.
  **Note**: This feature cannot be enabled for a motor vehicle listing.
  """
  galleryPlus: Boolean
  """
  This field is used to add or modify a customized subtitle for the listing. By using a subtitle, more keywords can be provided and search results may be improved.
  **Note**: If this field is included, the text in this field will overwrite the current subtitle if one is defined for the listing.
  **Note**: If the this listing upgrade is disabled for an active listing, the seller is generally not entitled to a refund against that fee.
  **Max length**: 55 characters.
  """
  subtitle: String
}

"""
This error type represents details about an error that occurred while updating an order.
"""
type UpdateOrderError {
  """
  A human-readable description of the error message. This string is not localized and may change without notice.
    
  **Maximum length:** 512 characters
  """
  displayMessage: String!
  """
  The machine-readable error code for identifying the type of error. For this type, the available values are:
  - `INVALID_INPUT`: The input data is invalid. (Not retryable)
  - `NOT_AUTHORIZED`: The user is not authorized to perform this action. (Not retryable)
  - `VERSION_LOCKED`: The order was modified by another process. (Retryable)
  - `TEMPORARILY_NOT_AVAILABLE`: The service is temporarily unavailable. (Retryable)
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """The ID of the order that failed to update."""
  inputOrderId: ID!
  """
  When `true`, the operation can be retried and may succeed. When `false`, a retry will not succeed.
  """
  retryable: Boolean!
}

"""
This input type specifies tag updates for an order and has the following constraints:
- Accepts a maximum of 5 tags.
- Each tag must be up to 10 characters long.
"""
input UpdateOrderTagInput {
  """
  This enumerated value specifies the operation to perform on the specified tags.
  """
  action: TagUpdateAction!
  """The unique ID of the order."""
  orderId: ID!
  """
  Use this array to provide up to 5 custom tags to apply to the order. 
    
  **Note:** A maximum of 5 tags can be specified, with each up to 10 characters long.
  """
  tags: [String!]!
}

"""
This type displays the unique identifiers of all purchase quotes that were not successully updated, and the error(s) that caused them not to be updated.
"""
type UpdatePurchaseQuoteError {
  """A user-friendly, non-localized message describing the error."""
  displayMessage: String!
  """
  The unique identifier of the error. Below are the four errors that may occur:
  - INVALID_INPUT: This error indicates that there were one or more issues with the input data in the mutation request. 
  - TEMPORARILY_NOT_AVAILABLE: This error indicates that a system error occurred. This error may occur with a complete failure, and the user can try again after a short period of time. 
  - NOT_AUTHORIZED: The user is not authorized to perform this action and/or there is an issue with the token.
  - VERSION_LOCKED: This error indicates that the purchase quote was being modified by another process at the time of the request, and the user can try again after a short period of time.
  """
  errorCode: String!
  """The unique identifier of the purchase quote that failed to be updated."""
  inputPurchaseQuoteId: ID!
  """
  This boolean indicates whether or not the user should try to update the corresponding purchase quote again. If this field is returned as 'true', the user can make another attempt to update the corresponding purchase quote.
  """
  retryable: Boolean!
}

"""
This input is used to update an existing purchase quote when using the **bulkUpdatePurchaseQuotes** mutation.
"""
input UpdatePurchaseQuoteInput {
  """
  This boolean field is used to control whether or not the seller should receive an email copy of the updated purchase quote sent to the buyer. If this field is included and set to 'true', the seller will receive a copy of the updated purchase quote in their eBay Inbox.
  **Default value**: false
  """
  emailCopyToSeller: Boolean = false
  """
  This array is used to update the list of item commitments that are a part of the purchase quote. A comma is used as a delimiter for each item commitment identifier.
  **Note**: All item commitment IDs that are a part of the purchase quote must be included here. Omitted item commitments will be removed from the purchase quote.
  """
  lineItems: [PurchaseQuoteItemInput!]
  """
  This container is used to add or modify available shipping and/or pickup logistics options provided by the seller.
  """
  logisticsOptions: PurchaseQuoteLogisticsOptionInput
  """
  This field allows the seller to provide a custom message to the buyer regarding the update(s) that were made to purchase quote.
  **Minimum length**: 1 character
  **Maximum length**: 512 characters
  """
  messageToBuyer: String
  """
  This required field is used to provide the identifier of the purchase quote to update.
  """
  purchaseQuoteId: ID!
  """
  This container is used to add or modify handling charges and/or a shipping discount for a purchase quote.
  """
  total: PurchaseQuoteTotalsInput
}

"""
This is the base request type for the **updateSellerReturnResponseRuleCondition** mutation, used to create a single automation return rule.

**Note:** The rule **name** is optional, but can be used to change the name of existing rule. If not provided, existing name will remain (unchanged).
"""
input UpdateSellerReturnResponseRuleConditionInput {
  """
  Conditions that, when met, trigger the rule.
  All conditions provided here will replace existing conditions.
  """
  conditionSet: ReturnRuleConditionSetInput!
  """
  The unique name of the rule. This optional field can be used to change name of existing rule.
    
  **Note:** If a rule name is not provided, the existing name will remain (unchanged).
    
  **Requirements:**
  - the name must be unique. No two rules can have the same name
  - the name must use characters fromteh following set: [A-Z, a-z, 0-9, hyphen(-), underscore(_), period(.), colon(:), comma(,), apostrophe(')]
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  name: String
  """The unique identifier of the rule to be updated."""
  ruleId: ID!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **updateSellerReturnResponseRuleCondition** mutation reflects whether the seller's rule conditions were successfully updated or if an error occurred that prevented the update. All existing conditions will be replaced by the new conditions provided in the input. It returns an error if:
- the provided **ruleId** does not exist.
- the provided **returnRuleConditionSet** contains invalid condition data (categories are not leaf IDs, invalid country codes, or an invalid **refundRange** where the minimum is less than maximum).
- the provided rule name is already used by another rule for the seller on the given marketplace.
- the rule name violates allowed format, length, or characters (for example, exceeds maximum length, has disallowed characters).
- the return rules feature is not enabled for the seller.
"""
union UpdateSellerReturnResponseRuleConditionOutput = ReturnResponseRule | ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleInvalidConditionsError | ReturnRuleMissingConditionError | ReturnRuleNameError | ReturnRuleNotFoundError

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **updateSellerReturnResponseRulesPriorities** mutation. This mutation updates the order that the seller's return-respond automation rules should be executed. To reorder the rules, provide all `ruleIds` in the list, regardless of their status (enabled or disabled). Only the priority is updated (rule status remains unchanged, disabled rules will continue to stay disabled). Once updated, the active rules are evaluated in the order specified.
"""
input UpdateSellerReturnResponseRulesPrioritiesInput {
  """
  Marketplace where the item is **listed/published** (e.g., EBAY_US, EBAY_DE, EBAY_UK).
  All listings published on this marketplace inherit these preferences .
  """
  listingMarketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
  A list of one or more `ruleIds` arranged in the desired priority order. The first rule in the list represents the highest priority. All existing rules, regardless of their status (enabled or disabled), must be included in the input list or an error will be returned.
  """
  prioritizedRuleIds: [ID!]!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **updateSellerReturnResponseRulesPriorities** mutation indicates whether the return-respond automation rules were successfully reordered according to the priority specified in the input or if an error occurred that prevented its creation. It returns an error if:
- one or more `ruleIds` in the input list do not exist
- the input list contains duplicate `ruleIds`
- the input list includes one or more `ruleIds` that are invalid or do not belong to the same marketplace
- the return rules feature is not enabled for the seller
"""
union UpdateSellerReturnResponseRulesPrioritiesOutput = ReturnRuleDuplicateRuleIdsError | ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleInvalidRuleIdsError | ReturnRuleMissingRuleIdsError | UpdateSellerReturnResponseRulesPrioritiesSuccess

"""
This type defines the new priority order for the seller's return-response automation rules.
"""
type UpdateSellerReturnResponseRulesPrioritiesSuccess {
  """The r eturn response rules arranged in the updated priority order."""
  returnResponseRules: [ReturnResponseRule!]!
}

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **updateSellerReturnRuleStatus** mutation, which allows the seller to enable or disable a seller's rule.
"""
input UpdateSellerReturnRuleStatusInput {
  """The unique identifier of the rule."""
  ruleId: ID!
  """
  The status can be `ENABLED` or `DISABLED`:
  - `ENABLED`: The rule is evaluated according to its assigned priority (lower priority number execute first). The first rule that meets the specified conditions will be applied to the return request
  - `DISABLED`: The rules is not evaluated and will be skipped
  """
  status: ReturnPreferenceStatus!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **updateSellerReturnRuleStatus** mutation is used to enable or disable an automation return rule and indicates if the rule was successfully updated or if an error occurred that prevented the update. Disabled rules are not evaluated during return processing. It returns an error if:
