  Conditions that, when met, trigger the rule.
  All conditions provided here will replace existing conditions.
  """
  conditionSet: ReturnRuleConditionSetInput!
  """
  The unique name of the rule. This optional field can be used to change name of existing rule.
    
  **Note:** If a rule name is not provided, the existing name will remain (unchanged).
    
  **Requirements:**
  - the name must be unique. No two rules can have the same name
  - the name must use characters fromteh following set: [A-Z, a-z, 0-9, hyphen(-), underscore(_), period(.), colon(:), comma(,), apostrophe(')]
    
  **Format:** Alphanumeric
  **Maximum length:** 100 characters
  """
  name: String
  """The unique identifier of the rule to be updated."""
  ruleId: ID!
}

"""
This base response union type for the **updateSellerReturnToAddressRuleCondition** mutation reflects whether the seller's rule conditions were successfully updated or if an error occurred that prevented the update. All existing conditions will be replaced by the new conditions provided in the input. It returns an error if:
- the provided **ruleId** does not exist.
- the provided **returnRuleConditionSet** contains invalid condition data (for example, categories are not leaf IDs, invalid country codes, or an invalid **refundRange** where the minimum is less than maximum).
- the provided rule name is already used by another rule for the seller on the given marketplace.
- the rule name violates allowed format, length, or characters (for example, exceeds maximum length, has disallowed characters).
- the return rules feature is not enabled for the seller.
"""
union UpdateSellerReturnToAddressRuleConditionOutput = ReturnRuleFeatureNotEnabledError | ReturnRuleInvalidConditionsError | ReturnRuleMissingConditionError | ReturnRuleNameError | ReturnRuleNotFoundError | ReturnToAddressRequiredError | ReturnToAddressRule

"""
This input type defines the payload for the **updateSellerReturnToAddressRulesPriorities** mutation, which updates the order in which the seller's return address rules should be executed. To reorder the rules, provide all `ruleIds` in the list, regardless of their status. Only the priority is updated (rule status remains unchanged, disabled rules will continue to stay disabled). Once updated, enabled rules are evaluated in the order specified.
"""
input UpdateSellerReturnToAddressRulesPrioritiesInput {
  """
  This enumerated value is the marketplace where the item is **listed/published** (for example, EBAY_US, EBAY_DE, EBAY_UK). All listings published on this marketplace inherit these preferences.
  """
  listingMarketplace: ListingMarketplace!
  """
